{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dfi9x4KYz3p6uj2C6yT5tF","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/scripts/pack_single_html.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"7a1debc8-deaa-4836-96c2-ac1662842ae2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:55.991Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Dfi9x4KYz3p6uj2C6yT5tF":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/scripts/pack_single_html.py"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dfi9x4KYz3p6uj2C6yT5tF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Packs the browser build into one self-contained HTML page: no other files, no network loads.\n3\t\n4\tusage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\n5\t           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\n6\t\n7\tBINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\n8\t--single-file makes it and runs this. The page is web/index.html with the options written into\n9\tits <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\n10\tgiven), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\n11\tloader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\n12\tinline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\n13\tnames no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\n14\tURLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\n15\t\"\"\"\n16\timport argparse\n17\timport base64\n18\timport gzip\n19\timport html\n20\timport json\n21\timport pathlib\n22\timport re\n23\timport sys\n24\t\n25\tROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n26\tPAGE = ROOT / \"web\" / \"index.html\"\n27\t\n28\t# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\n29\tLOADER = \"\"\"\n30\t(() => {\n31\t  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n32\t  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\n33\t  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n34\t  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\n35\t    query.set('scene', scene);\n36\t    try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + query + location.hash); }\n37\t    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\n38\t  }\n39\t  const line = document.createElement('div');\n40\t  line.style.cssText = 'font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.7; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums';\n41\t  msg.style.flexDirection = 'column';\n42\t  msg.style.gap = '8px';\n43\t  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\n44\t  const paint = () => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));\n45\t  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\n46\t  const glue = new Promise((resolve) => { window.gameGlue = resolve; });\n47\t  window.loadGame = async () => {\n48\t    line.textContent = 'Unpacking…';\n49\t    await paint();\n50\t    // The gzipped wasm's base64 block leaves the page once read, to free its text.\n51\t    const block = document.getElementById('game-wasm'), size = +block.dataset.size, text = block.textContent;\n52\t    block.remove();\n53\t    let packed;\n54\t    if (Uint8Array.fromBase64) packed = Uint8Array.fromBase64(text);\n55\t    else {\n56\t      const bin = atob(text);\n57\t      packed = new Uint8Array(bin.length);\n58\t      for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) packed[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);\n59\t    }\n60\t    const wasm = new Uint8Array(size);\n61\t    const reader = new Blob([packed]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip')).getReader();\n62\t    let n = 0;\n63\t    for (let r = await reader.read(); !r.done; r = await reader.read()) {\n64\t      wasm.set(r.value, n);\n65\t      n += r.value.length;\n66\t      line.textContent = `Unpacking ${Math.floor((100 * n) / size)}%`;\n67\t    }\n68\t    if (n !== size) throw new Error(`the packed game is damaged (${n} of ${size} bytes)`);\n69\t    line.textContent = 'Starting…';\n70\t    await paint();\n71\t    const init = await glue;\n72\t    await init({ module_or_path: wasm });\n73\t  };\n74\t})();\n75\t\"\"\"\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef fail(text):\n79\t    sys.exit(f\"pack_single_html: {text}\")\n80\t\n81\t\n82\tdef replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\n83\t    \"\"\"Replaces the one match of `pattern` in the page; anything else means index.html changed.\"\"\"\n84\t    page, n = re.subn(pattern, make, page)\n85\t    if n != 1:\n86\t        fail(f\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\")\n87\t    return page\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef main():\n91\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n92\t    ap.add_argument(\"bindgen_dir\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\"wasm-bindgen output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm)\")\n93\t    ap.add_argument(\"--title\", help=\"<title> (default: index.html's)\")\n94\t    ap.add_argument(\"--description\", help=\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\")\n95\t    ap.add_argument(\"--theme-color\", help=\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\")\n96\t    ap.add_argument(\"--scene\", help=\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\")\n97\t    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\")\n98\t    a = ap.parse_args()\n99\t\n100\t    js, wasm_path = a.bindgen_dir / \"shardfall.js\", a.bindgen_dir / \"shardfall_bg.wasm\"\n101\t    for p in (js, wasm_path):\n102\t        if not p.is_file():\n103\t            fail(f\"{p} is missing: run wasm-bindgen --target web --out-name shardfall first\")\n104\t    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\n105\t    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\n106\t    glue = js.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n107\t    if (a.bindgen_dir / \"snippets\").exists() or re.search(r\"^import\\b\", glue, re.M):\n108\t        fail(\"the JS glue imports other files (wasm-bindgen snippets); inline them before packing\")\n109\t    if re.search(r\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\", glue):\n110\t        fail(\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\")\n111\t    init = re.search(r\"^export \\{[^}]*?\\b([\\w$]+) as default\\b\", glue, re.M)\n112\t    if not init:\n113\t        fail(\"can't find the JS glue's default export (its init function)\")\n114\t\n115\t    page = PAGE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n116\t    if a.title is not None:\n117\t        page = replace_one(page, r\"<title>[^<]*</title>\", lambda m: f\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\", \"<title>\")\n118\t    for name, value in ((\"description\", a.description), (\"theme-color\", a.theme_color)):\n119\t        if value is not None:\n120\t            page = replace_one(\n121\t                page,\n122\t                rf'<meta name=\"{name}\" content=\"[^\"]*\">',\n123\t                lambda m, name=name, value=value: f'<meta name=\"{name}\" content=\"{html.escape(value)}\">',\n124\t                f\"<meta name={name}>\",\n125\t            )\n126\t    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\n127\t    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")\n128\t\n129\t    wasm = wasm_path.read_bytes()\n130\t    packed = gzip.compress(wasm, compresslevel=9, mtime=0)\n131\t    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \"<\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\n132\t    loader = LOADER.replace(\"__SCENE__\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\"))\n133\t    tail = (\n134\t        f'<script id=\"game-wasm\" type=\"application/octet-stream\" data-size=\"{len(wasm)}\">'\n135\t        f\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\n\"\n136\t        f\"<script>{loader}</script>\\n\"\n137\t        f'<script type=\"module\">\\n{glue}\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\n</script>\\n'\n138\t    )\n139\t    page = replace_one(page, r\"</body>\", lambda m: tail + \"</body>\", \"</body>\")\n140\t\n141\t    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\", page)[1])\n142\t    out = a.out or ROOT / \"target\" / \"web\" / f\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\"\n143\t    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n144\t    out.write_text(page, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n145\t    mb = lambda n: f\"{n / 1e6:.1f} MB\"  # noqa: E731\n146\t    print(f\"{out}: {mb(out.stat().st_size)} (wasm {mb(len(wasm))}, gzipped {mb(len(packed))}; JS glue {mb(len(glue))})\")\n147\t\n148\t\n149\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n150\t    main()\n151\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"5a1283fd-e57e-42d4-b83c-6bd7607a3fad","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:56.007Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/scripts/pack_single_html.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Packs the browser build into one self-contained HTML page: no other files, no network loads.\n\nusage: python3 -I scripts/pack_single_html.py BINDGEN_DIR [--title T] [--description D]\n           [--theme-color C] [--scene NAME] [--out PATH]\n\nBINDGEN_DIR is wasm-bindgen's output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm); scripts/build-web.sh\n--single-file makes it and runs this. The page is web/index.html with the options written into\nits <title>, <meta name=description> and <meta name=theme-color> (left as they are when not\ngiven), the manifest link dropped, and, before </body>, the gzipped wasm as base64 text, a\nloader that sets window.loadGame (index.html's script calls it when set) and the JS glue as an\ninline module script. The loader shows a progress line, bakes in --scene (used when the address\nnames no room or scene) and unpacks with the browser's DecompressionStream. No blob: or data:\nURLs are needed. Out: target/web/<title>.html.\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport base64\nimport gzip\nimport html\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport re\nimport sys\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nPAGE = ROOT / \"web\" / \"index.html\"\n\n# Runs while the page parses, before index.html's module script.\nLOADER = \"\"\"\n(() => {\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n  // The start scene baked in at build time, unless the address names a room or a scene.\n  const scene = __SCENE__, query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n  if (scene && !query.get('room') && !query.get('scene')) {\n    query.set('scene', scene);\n    try { history.replaceState(history.state, '', '?' + query + location.hash); }\n    catch (error) { console.warn('Could not put the start scene in the address:', error); }\n  }\n  const line = document.createElement('div');\n  line.style.cssText = 'font-size: 14px; opacity: 0.7; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums';\n  msg.style.flexDirection = 'column';\n  msg.style.gap = '8px';\n  msg.replaceChildren(`Loading ${document.title}…`, line);\n  const paint = () => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));\n  // The JS glue is the module script at the end of the page: it hands over its init function.\n  const glue = new Promise((resolve) => { window.gameGlue = resolve; });\n  window.loadGame = async () => {\n    line.textContent = 'Unpacking…';\n    await paint();\n    // The gzipped wasm's base64 block leaves the page once read, to free its text.\n    const block = document.getElementById('game-wasm'), size = +block.dataset.size, text = block.textContent;\n    block.remove();\n    let packed;\n    if (Uint8Array.fromBase64) packed = Uint8Array.fromBase64(text);\n    else {\n      const bin = atob(text);\n      packed = new Uint8Array(bin.length);\n      for (let i = 0; i < bin.length; i++) packed[i] = bin.charCodeAt(i);\n    }\n    const wasm = new Uint8Array(size);\n    const reader = new Blob([packed]).stream().pipeThrough(new DecompressionStream('gzip')).getReader();\n    let n = 0;\n    for (let r = await reader.read(); !r.done; r = await reader.read()) {\n      wasm.set(r.value, n);\n      n += r.value.length;\n      line.textContent = `Unpacking ${Math.floor((100 * n) / size)}%`;\n    }\n    if (n !== size) throw new Error(`the packed game is damaged (${n} of ${size} bytes)`);\n    line.textContent = 'Starting…';\n    await paint();\n    const init = await glue;\n    await init({ module_or_path: wasm });\n  };\n})();\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef fail(text):\n    sys.exit(f\"pack_single_html: {text}\")\n\n\ndef replace_one(page, pattern, make, what):\n    \"\"\"Replaces the one match of `pattern` in the page; anything else means index.html changed.\"\"\"\n    page, n = re.subn(pattern, make, page)\n    if n != 1:\n        fail(f\"expected one {what} in {PAGE.relative_to(ROOT)}, found {n}: update this script\")\n    return page\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.split(\"\\n\")[0])\n    ap.add_argument(\"bindgen_dir\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\"wasm-bindgen output (shardfall.js, shardfall_bg.wasm)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--title\", help=\"<title> (default: index.html's)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--description\", help=\"<meta name=description> (default: index.html's)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--theme-color\", help=\"<meta name=theme-color> (default: index.html's)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--scene\", help=\"start scene when the address names no room or scene (default: the game's)\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out\", type=pathlib.Path, help=\"output file (default: target/web/<title>.html)\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n\n    js, wasm_path = a.bindgen_dir / \"shardfall.js\", a.bindgen_dir / \"shardfall_bg.wasm\"\n    for p in (js, wasm_path):\n        if not p.is_file():\n            fail(f\"{p} is missing: run wasm-bindgen --target web --out-name shardfall first\")\n    # The glue goes in the page as an inline module script, so it can't import other files\n    # (wasm-bindgen snippets) or hold text that would end the script element early.\n    glue = js.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if (a.bindgen_dir / \"snippets\").exists() or re.search(r\"^import\\b\", glue, re.M):\n        fail(\"the JS glue imports other files (wasm-bindgen snippets); inline them before packing\")\n    if re.search(r\"(?i)</script|<script|<!--\", glue):\n        fail(\"the JS glue contains <script, </script or <!--, which can't sit inside an inline script\")\n    init = re.search(r\"^export \\{[^}]*?\\b([\\w$]+) as default\\b\", glue, re.M)\n    if not init:\n        fail(\"can't find the JS glue's default export (its init function)\")\n\n    page = PAGE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    if a.title is not None:\n        page = replace_one(page, r\"<title>[^<]*</title>\", lambda m: f\"<title>{html.escape(a.title)}</title>\", \"<title>\")\n    for name, value in ((\"description\", a.description), (\"theme-color\", a.theme_color)):\n        if value is not None:\n            page = replace_one(\n                page,\n                rf'<meta name=\"{name}\" content=\"[^\"]*\">',\n                lambda m, name=name, value=value: f'<meta name=\"{name}\" content=\"{html.escape(value)}\">',\n                f\"<meta name={name}>\",\n            )\n    # A manifest is another file to load: the single page goes without one.\n    page = replace_one(page, r'[ \\t]*<link rel=\"manifest\"[^>]*>\\n', lambda m: \"\", \"manifest link\")\n\n    wasm = wasm_path.read_bytes()\n    packed = gzip.compress(wasm, compresslevel=9, mtime=0)\n    # JSON is valid JS; escaping \"<\" keeps a scene name from closing the script element.\n    loader = LOADER.replace(\"__SCENE__\", json.dumps(a.scene or None).replace(\"<\", \"\\\\u003c\"))\n    tail = (\n        f'<script id=\"game-wasm\" type=\"application/octet-stream\" data-size=\"{len(wasm)}\">'\n        f\"{base64.b64encode(packed).decode()}</script>\\n\"\n        f\"<script>{loader}</script>\\n\"\n        f'<script type=\"module\">\\n{glue}\\nwindow.gameGlue({init[1]});\\n</script>\\n'\n    )\n    page = replace_one(page, r\"</body>\", lambda m: tail + \"</body>\", \"</body>\")\n\n    title = a.title if a.title is not None else html.unescape(re.search(r\"<title>([^<]*)</title>\", page)[1])\n    out = a.out or ROOT / \"target\" / \"web\" / f\"{re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+', '-', title.lower()).strip('-') or 'game'}.html\"\n    out.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    out.write_text(page, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    mb = lambda n: f\"{n / 1e6:.1f} MB\"  # noqa: E731\n    print(f\"{out}: {mb(out.stat().st_size)} (wasm {mb(len(wasm))}, gzipped {mb(len(packed))}; JS glue {mb(len(glue))})\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Dfi9x4KYz3p6uj2C6yT5tF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013mT6n4zrLyuKdLucD75CVo","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/web/index.html"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"94bb9996-a2f6-4d8d-b04e-ca894ff7fcdc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:56.960Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013mT6n4zrLyuKdLucD75CVo":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/web/index.html"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013mT6n4zrLyuKdLucD75CVo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t<!doctype html>\n2\t<html lang=\"en\">\n3\t<head>\n4\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n5\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\">\n6\t<title>Shardfall</title>\n7\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Play Shardfall, a procedural hack-and-slash adventure with an interactive tech demo pavilion.\">\n8\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\">\n9\t<meta name=\"mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n10\t<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n11\t<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\">\n12\t<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"manifest.webmanifest\">\n13\t<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\">\n14\t<style>\n15\t  /* The page is the game: no scrolling, zooming, text selection, callouts or tap flashes. */\n16\t  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #15171c; overscroll-behavior: none;\n17\t               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\n18\t               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\n19\t  /* winit appends the game canvas to <body>; it fills the page and the game follows its size.\n20\t     dvh: the height that is visible while a phone's browser bars come and go. */\n21\t  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n22\t           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\n23\t  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n24\t         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #c9ccd4; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\n25\t  /* Phones held upright: a hint to turn sideways that fades by itself. */\n26\t  #turn { display: none; position: fixed; left: 50%; top: 12px; transform: translateX(-50%); padding: 8px 14px;\n27\t          border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6); color: #ffd690; font: 14px system-ui, sans-serif;\n28\t          pointer-events: none; animation: fade 1s 5s forwards; }\n29\t  @media (orientation: portrait) and (pointer: coarse) { #turn { display: block; } }\n30\t  @keyframes fade { to { opacity: 0; } }\n31\t</style>\n32\t</head>\n33\t<body>\n34\t<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Shardfall…</div>\n35\t<div id=\"turn\">Turn your phone sideways for the best view</div>\n36\t<script type=\"module\">\n37\t  // Start in a demo room with ?room=NAME, or the pavilion with ?scene=world.\n38\t  // Messages name the game by the page title (a single-file build may retitle it).\n39\t  const name = document.title;\n40\t  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n41\t  if (!navigator.gpu) {\n42\t    msg.replaceChildren(`${name} needs WebGPU.`, document.createElement('br'),\n43\t      'Use a recent Chrome, Edge or Safari (iOS 26 or later) with hardware acceleration enabled.');\n44\t  } else {\n45\t    // The game hides this message once its canvas exists, and takes keyboard focus.\n46\t    new MutationObserver((_, obs) => {\n47\t      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n48\t      if (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name} game`); msg.remove(); c.focus(); obs.disconnect(); }\n49\t    }).observe(document.body, { childList: true });\n50\t    // Phones and tablets: the first tap goes full screen and turns sideways, where the browser\n51\t    // allows it (Android; an iPhone keeps its bars, or plays full screen from the home screen).\n52\t    if (matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches) {\n53\t      addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\n54\t        const el = document.documentElement;\n55\t        if (!document.fullscreenElement && el.requestFullscreen) {\n56\t          el.requestFullscreen({ navigationUI: 'hide' })\n57\t            .then(() => screen.orientation && screen.orientation.lock && screen.orientation.lock('landscape'))\n58\t            .catch(() => {});\n59\t        }\n60\t      }, { once: true, capture: true });\n61\t    }\n62\t    try {\n63\t      // The game is shardfall.js and its .wasm beside this page. A single-file build\n64\t      // (scripts/pack_single_html.py) carries both inside the page and sets window.loadGame.\n65\t      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n66\t      else await (await import('./shardfall.js')).default();\n67\t    } catch (error) {\n68\t      console.error(`${name} failed to load:`, error);\n69\t      msg.textContent = `${name} could not load. Please reload the page. If it still fails, check that WebGPU and hardware acceleration are enabled.`;\n70\t      document.body.append(msg);\n71\t    }\n72\t  }\n73\t</script>\n74\t</body>\n75\t</html>\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"b900b888-6752-4cf5-9b9c-e7c026855dcb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:56.973Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/web/index.html","content":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\">\n<title>Shardfall</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Play Shardfall, a procedural hack-and-slash adventure with an interactive tech demo pavilion.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\">\n<meta name=\"mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-capable\" content=\"yes\">\n<meta name=\"apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style\" content=\"black-translucent\">\n<link rel=\"manifest\" href=\"manifest.webmanifest\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\">\n<style>\n  /* The page is the game: no scrolling, zooming, text selection, callouts or tap flashes. */\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #15171c; overscroll-behavior: none;\n               touch-action: none; -webkit-user-select: none; user-select: none; -webkit-touch-callout: none;\n               -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent; }\n  /* winit appends the game canvas to <body>; it fills the page and the game follows its size.\n     dvh: the height that is visible while a phone's browser bars come and go. */\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100vw !important; height: 100vh !important; height: 100dvh !important;\n           outline: none; touch-action: none; }\n  #msg { position: fixed; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;\n         font: 18px system-ui, sans-serif; color: #c9ccd4; text-align: center; padding: 24px; pointer-events: none; }\n  /* Phones held upright: a hint to turn sideways that fades by itself. */\n  #turn { display: none; position: fixed; left: 50%; top: 12px; transform: translateX(-50%); padding: 8px 14px;\n          border-radius: 18px; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6); color: #ffd690; font: 14px system-ui, sans-serif;\n          pointer-events: none; animation: fade 1s 5s forwards; }\n  @media (orientation: portrait) and (pointer: coarse) { #turn { display: block; } }\n  @keyframes fade { to { opacity: 0; } }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading Shardfall…</div>\n<div id=\"turn\">Turn your phone sideways for the best view</div>\n<script type=\"module\">\n  // Start in a demo room with ?room=NAME, or the pavilion with ?scene=world.\n  // Messages name the game by the page title (a single-file build may retitle it).\n  const name = document.title;\n  const msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n  if (!navigator.gpu) {\n    msg.replaceChildren(`${name} needs WebGPU.`, document.createElement('br'),\n      'Use a recent Chrome, Edge or Safari (iOS 26 or later) with hardware acceleration enabled.');\n  } else {\n    // The game hides this message once its canvas exists, and takes keyboard focus.\n    new MutationObserver((_, obs) => {\n      const c = document.querySelector('canvas');\n      if (c) { c.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name} game`); msg.remove(); c.focus(); obs.disconnect(); }\n    }).observe(document.body, { childList: true });\n    // Phones and tablets: the first tap goes full screen and turns sideways, where the browser\n    // allows it (Android; an iPhone keeps its bars, or plays full screen from the home screen).\n    if (matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches) {\n      addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\n        const el = document.documentElement;\n        if (!document.fullscreenElement && el.requestFullscreen) {\n          el.requestFullscreen({ navigationUI: 'hide' })\n            .then(() => screen.orientation && screen.orientation.lock && screen.orientation.lock('landscape'))\n            .catch(() => {});\n        }\n      }, { once: true, capture: true });\n    }\n    try {\n      // The game is shardfall.js and its .wasm beside this page. A single-file build\n      // (scripts/pack_single_html.py) carries both inside the page and sets window.loadGame.\n      if (window.loadGame) await window.loadGame();\n      else await (await import('./shardfall.js')).default();\n    } catch (error) {\n      console.error(`${name} failed to load:`, error);\n      msg.textContent = `${name} could not load. Please reload the page. If it still fails, check that WebGPU and hardware acceleration are enabled.`;\n      document.body.append(msg);\n    }\n  }\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","numLines":76,"startLine":1,"totalLines":76}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013mT6n4zrLyuKdLucD75CVo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019eJJv1xHhoNHzZ7Si7gt98","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/REFERENCE.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"eddbc2e4-1baf-49b2-9f9b-1552df56f704","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:57.790Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019eJJv1xHhoNHzZ7Si7gt98":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/REFERENCE.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019eJJv1xHhoNHzZ7Si7gt98","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Reference\n2\t\n3\tThe detail behind `AGENTS.md`, read on demand: open the section you need, not the whole page.\n4\t`pav help` lists every tool with its arguments.\n5\t- [Code map](#code-map): what each crate and data folder holds.\n6\t- [Studios](#studios): animation, objects and creatures, edited live.\n7\t- [Tools](#tools): each tool family with examples.\n8\t- [Browser and phones](#browser-and-phones): running the web build headless, emulating a phone.\n9\t- [Controls](#controls): keyboard, gamepad, touch and the fixed system keys.\n10\t- [Tests](#tests): what each suite covers.\n11\t\n12\t## Code map\n13\t```\n14\tcrates/\n15\t  pav_core    simulation, no window/GPU/audio deps: Sim, entities, physics (rapier3d),\n16\t              static regions (statics.rs: terrain chunks, rooms, hub; active or dormant;\n17\t              blocks, decor and baked library props: drawn by the view's region cache, one\n18\t              collider box each, no entity),\n19\t              world.rs (pavilion layout, streaming, room tracking), room.rs (room files),\n20\t              terrain.rs (procedural wilderness), tile levels (level.rs), characters\n21\t              (character.rs: movement models instant/momentum/grid/committed, jump,\n22\t              crouch/crawl, ladders, ledge grab/mantle, swimming, axis lock, moving platforms,\n23\t              knockback, pushing shares momentum, bombs, ice slide), puppet (puppet.rs: body\n24\t              plans biped/spider/lizard/beetle/blob/quadruped, procedural animation, hit recoil,\n25\t              creature lunges, foot IK, legs that stride the way the body travels, idle breathing\n26\t              and blinks, cutout look and camera cheats; the biped is a `Skel` of joints that the\n27\t              procedural animation, moves and clips each produce and `dress` turns into parts),\n28\t              moves.rs (attacks and gestures as data, anim/moves.toml: arcs around the shoulders,\n29\t              wind-up from wherever the hands were, strikes with lunge/lean/twist/hop/spin,\n30\t              follow-through; skills name a move, a look may name its own per skill and combo\n31\t              swing: `attack_moves`), clips.rs (motion clips: readable key poses\n32\t              translated from open animation libraries, retargeted onto the biped with IK,\n33\t              crossfaded over the procedural animation, upper body only or mirrored; performers,\n34\t              idle clips, walk clips played as fast as the character moves), anim.rs (the /anim files: embedded, live reload), rig.rs (creature feet that plant and step,\n35\t              follow-the-leader spines, verlet tails/antennae), ai.rs (NPC brains: idle,\n36\t              wander, patrol, circle, follow; they drive characters through InputFrames),\n37\t              nav.rs (walkable grid from blocks and props, A* paths, flow fields),\n38\t              games/ (the hook a new game implements, `Game`, and `GAMES`, the list that\n39\t              makes each one a scene; starter.rs + starter.toml, the template:\n40\t              docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md),\n41\t              fxdef.rs (object lights / particle emitters / distortion, view-only),\n42\t              vehicle.rs (drift car on rapier's raycast vehicle, arcade helicopter: flight only,\n43\t              no weapons, damage or fuel), health.rs (shootable rapier objects: hp, score, boss\n44\t              phases/bar, finish),\n45\t              stealth.rs (guard sight cones with line of sight and an alert meter),\n46\t              zones.rs (trigger zones + labels), course.rs (timers, gates, checkpoints, pits,\n47\t              pads, camera cues, hits/respawn), behaviors.rs (movers, rotators, emitters,\n48\t              spawners), projectile.rs (lightweight bullets), feel.rs (feel metrics),\n49\t              softbody.rs (rapier soft bodies: jelly, balls, cloth, ropes), joints.rs (joints\n50\t              owned by entities, recreated on wake), destruct.rs (crumbling/breakable tiles,\n51\t              conveyors and bounce pads for props), history, params\n52\t  pav_render  wgpu renderer (Vulkan/DX12): Scene description -> particles (compute) -> sun +\n53\t              point-light shadow passes (shadows.rs) -> MSAA scene pass (+ GPU particles) ->\n54\t              bloom chain and distortion (fx.rs) -> composite (outlines, screen-space GI,\n55\t              tonemap, filter stack: pixelate/CRT/scanlines/dither/palettes/grading, split;\n56\t              pixel art on part of the scene: objects flagged `flags::PIXEL`, chosen in the view\n57\t              by `view.filter.pixel_target` = all/characters/hero/others/world/entity/objects/\n58\t              environment; every filter can aim at a part: `flags::OBJECT` marks characters &\n59\t              objects, the normal buffer carries it, `*_on` = all/objects/environment; painterly and\n60\t              print styles: Kuwahara oil paint, CMYK halftone, ASCII, pencil sketch (`filter.stylize`);\n61\t              hazy air: volumetric sun shafts ray-marched through the sun's shadow map and lamp\n62\t              halos in closed form (`view.haze`, `shafts`, `halos`); screen transitions (iris,\n63\t              diamonds, dissolve, mosaic, blinds, fade); wind in the vertex shader for instances\n64\t              flagged `flags::SWAY` (leaves) / `flags::GRASS` (tufts that part around the player)).\n65\t              Procedural meshes + analytic SDF spheres/capsules/rounded cones, SDF-font text in\n66\t              the world (text.rs). Procedural materials: rows of a storage buffer read by one\n67\t              kernel library (shaders/materials.wgsl, matched pixel for pixel by\n68\t              `pav_core::material::eval`); `pav_view::materials` interns them into slots for\n69\t              prop parts, static blocks (world-mapped) and decor. `render_scale` draws below the target's resolution and\n70\t              upscale.rs stretches it over (phones). Offscreen capture -> PNG.\n71\t  pav_view    sim frame -> render Scene: camera rig (tilt/yaw/distance/fov/ortho, all live),\n72\t              look.rs + looks.toml (the Look & Filters layer: filter sections, presets, whole looks),\n73\t              water.rs (water zones ripple: a CPU wave equation on a height grid, stirred by\n74\t              whatever crosses the waterline, splashes, blasts and rain; drawn as a dynamic mesh),\n75\t              assets.rs (`emit_asset`: a library asset drawn from game state each frame),\n76\t              interpolation between ticks, visual settings (ViewSettings)\n77\t  pav_audio   synthesized sound: oscillators/noise/envelopes/filters, event -> sound bank,\n78\t              cpal output (optional), offline .wav rendering\n79\t  pav_tools   agent layer: tool registry + `pav` CLI (one-shot, REPL) + MCP stdio server +\n80\t              live bridge client (bridge.rs), and the motion importer (mocap/: glTF and FBX\n81\t              libraries, CMU's ASF/AMC, BVH; Rigify, Unreal, Mixamo/MotionBuilder, 100STYLE and\n82\t              Bandai Namco skeletons; loops cut at their best cycle; fitted into readable key\n83\t              poses, number for number what my-3D2dge's own importer writes; the whole CMU\n84\t              database surveyed and translated), and the asset importer (import/: what both\n85\t              importers share, one `Scene` read from glTF/OBJ, normalisation, translation into\n86\t              props with fidelity metrics, the licence gate that routes packs to lib/ or\n87\t              local/; `asset_import`, `docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md`)\n88\t  pav_app     the game (`shardfall` binary): window, boot diagnostics, input (keyboard/mouse,\n89\t              gamepad via gilrs), system keys, tuning panel, pause menu, sim thread\n90\t              (simhost.rs; stepped from the frame loop in the browser), live bridge server\n91\t              (bridge.rs), egui input (uiinput.rs), graphics quality (quality.rs: render\n92\t              scale, dynamic resolution). Builds natively and for wasm32 (WebGPU).\n93\t  pav_ui      Shardfall's game UI in egui, drawn by the window and by the tools: the HUD\n94\t              (arpg_ui.rs: orbs, skill bar, banners, minimap), the windows (arpg_items.rs:\n95\t              inventory, shop, stash, character, skills; arpg_tree.rs: the passive tree), touch\n96\t              screens (touch.rs: finger routing, invisible stick, button fan, auto-attack,\n97\t              swipe-to-dismiss), and headless.rs (the same UI on a windowless context: a text\n98\t              reading by window, clicks, and an egui-wgpu overlay painted over captures).\n99\tanim/         animation data, embedded and hot-reloadable (`anim_reload`): moves.toml (the moves table)\n100\t              and clip sets (*.json: QUATERNIUS, MESH2MOTION, CMU, STYLE100: 437 clips with credits).\n101\t              anim/cmu/ holds every take of the CMU database (4,770 clips) and anim/100style/ the\n102\t              100STYLE runs, backward walks and runs, sidesteps and idles (780 loops), on disk\n103\t              only: `clips load=cmu`, `clips load=100style`. anim/local/ (git-ignored) holds what\n104\t              is translated from libraries whose licences forbid sharing it (Bandai Namco, LaFAN1,\n105\t              Mixamo): `clips load=local`. anim/catalogs/ says how each set is made (tags,\n106\t              descriptions, sources, picks): `clip_import catalog=...` rebuilds it from the\n107\t              libraries.\n108\trooms/        room data files (TOML: info card, station guide `[learn]`, wing, primary device, movement model, camera,\n109\t              params, keys, entrance, ASCII tile layers + legend, [[object]]s). Every file\n110\t              here is embedded in the exe at build time AND hot-reloaded at runtime.\n111\t              `_template.toml` documents every field.\n112\t```\n113\t\n114\t## Studios\n115\tAnimation Studio: `scripts/animation-studio.sh` or `shardfall --animation-studio` opens an\n116\tisolated preview and the live bridge. Use `.mcp.animation-studio.json` for visible MCP edits.\n117\t`anim_edit` creates/copies/inspects/edits clips, with revisions and 32-step undo/redo;\n118\t`anim_preview` plays, pauses, scrubs, and inspects their poses. Every accepted edit saves and\n119\tupdates the live library. The preview preserves the game state. Native animation files also\n120\treload automatically. See `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`. REPLs accept structured JSON lines:\n121\t`{\"tool\":\"anim_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"key\",\"name\":\"WORKSHOP/Wave\",\"time\":0.5,\"pose\":{\"armR\":[80,20,50,25,0]}}}`.\n122\tUse the returned `revision` as `if_revision` on later edits. Copy source clips before editing;\n123\tkeep local source copies and their history in `anim/local`.\n124\t\n125\tObject Studio: `scripts/asset-studio.sh` or `shardfall --asset-studio` opens reusable prop\n126\tauthoring on the same live bridge (`.mcp.studio.json`). `assets find=words` searches templates\n127\t(`BUILTIN/`), library packs (`LIB/pack/name`; `LIB/core` is embedded in every build, other packs\n128\tload from disk natively, `assets/props/local/` is git-ignored) and saved definitions, ranked,\n129\twith `category= tags= tier= similar=` filters. `asset_edit` creates/copies/inspects/patches\n130\treadable JSON with stable part names, atomic batches, revisions, and 32-step history.\n131\t`asset_preview` opens the isolated stage; `views=true` returns a framed 4-view contact sheet\n132\t(`figure=true` adds a 1.8 m figure) and leaves the stage and camera as they were. `capture stats=only` returns render cost without\n133\tan image. `asset_spawn` places one-root instances in the preserved scene. Edits refresh visuals\n134\tand compound collision together. Native file changes reload after 250 ms of quiet. Saved\n135\tdefinitions are `assets/props/workshop/*.json` (`PAV_ASSETS` overrides the props root).\n136\t`studio_status ticket=N` confirms frame submission for live edits without a capture. The\n137\tAnimations / Objects / Game tabs retain each workspace's controls and camera. See\n138\t`docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` (tools and format) and `docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md` (the live studio).\n139\tKeep procedural parts as text; use `if_revision` and batch related part changes in one `ops`\n140\tarray. Materials (planks, brick, cobbles … as per-pixel recipes, `docs/MATERIALS.md`): parts say\n141\t`\"mat\":\"MAT/oak_planks\"` or a key in the asset's `materials`; `kind=material` on `assets`,\n142\t`asset_edit` (workshop materials `MAT/workshop/x` in `assets/materials/workshop/`, `PAV_MATERIALS`\n143\toverrides the root; revisions `mat1-`) and `asset_preview` (a swatch with each layer's legibility\n144\tat the game camera). Game code draws units and scenery from its own state with library assets,\n145\tone call per thing per frame: `pav_view::assets::emit_asset(scene, \"BUILTIN/crate\",\n146\tPlacement::at(pos).yaw(deg).id(id), seed, &palette)` (no physics needed; `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`,\n147\t\"Library assets in game code\"). Game data and rooms may name only assets every build carries\n148\t(embedded, or a shipped pack's: `props::store::SHIPPED`).\n149\t\n150\tCreature Studio: `scripts/creature-studio.sh` or `shardfall --creature-studio` opens the\n151\tprocedural creature stage. `tools/creature-compiler` vendors the exact SpawnForge core/modules\n152\tpin and bundles it with `npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm run build` (run in that directory).\n153\tKeep the pin and source hashes intact; do not resolve against a moving upstream checkout.\n154\t`creature_catalog`, `creature_edit`, `creature_preview`, and `creature_status` expose theme,\n155\ttemplate, blueprint, named-part and surface authoring through the same MCP bridge. Edits\n156\tqueue asynchronous builds. Wait for `published`, `failed`, or `superseded`; only publication\n157\tgets a frame ticket. Use the new source `revision` for the next edit, and `studio_status`\n158\tfor actual frame submission. Failed/obsolete builds keep the last valid native mesh.\n159\tSources, history and disposable caches are under `assets/creatures` (`PAV_CREATURES`\n160\toverrides it). Node runs outside the simulation. The Windows package includes the bundle\n161\tand portable Node. See `docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md` for native material limits and the tool\n162\tcontract. This is an authoring/preview stage; gameplay spawning of these rigs is separate.\n163\t\n164\t## Tools\n165\t- Import: `asset_import` alone lists the open model libraries; `get=kenney/mini_dungeon` downloads\n166\t  a pack its catalog pins (`assets/catalogs/<lib>.json`) into .cache/assets, checked by SHA-256;\n167\t  `from=<model> list=true` summarises a .glb/.gltf/.obj (parts, triangles, size in cm, materials,\n168\t  main colours, warnings); `from=<model|folder|lib/pack>` translates into format-2 props\n169\t  (primitives, plus one read-only vertex-coloured mesh part for what they cannot fit; `fit=prims|mesh`)\n170\t  with the catalog's category and tags, routed by the licence gate: CC0/CC-BY packs to\n171\t  `assets/props/lib/<pack>/` (committed, with `PACK.json`; then the index and `CREDITS.md`),\n172\t  other licences, packs whose catalog says `\"local\"` and loose files to the git-ignored\n173\t  `assets/props/local/<pack>/` (or `out=`), with their fidelity (six-view IoU, ΔE, Chamfer mm,\n174\t  tier; `docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md`); `survey=<lib/pack|folder>` fits without writing\n175\t  and fills the ledger (`assets/catalogs/<lib>/<pack>.tsv`, keeping each row's `note`; `fit=false`:\n176\t  census only); `check=<asset.json> compare=true` measures a translation again and returns\n177\t  source-over-translation views. `up= yaw= scale= place=` bring a model into the engine's frame\n178\t  (a translation records them in `source.norm` for `check`).\n179\t- Games on the hook (`pav_core::games`, `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`; scene `starter`): `play` gives\n180\t  the running game's HUD lines, outcome and `status`; `play bot=true` lets its bot play on\n181\t  (`ticks=`, default 60 s); `play bot=true seeds=10` plays fresh runs on seeds 1..10 and leaves\n182\t  the session alone: `wins`, one `[seed, outcome, seconds]` row each, and the state of every\n183\t  run not won.\n184\t- Shardfall (scenes `town`, `arena`): `game` is the status, `autoplay seconds=30` lets a bot\n185\t  fight, `loot_roll level=40 count=5000` summarises loot tables without playing, `give\n186\t  unique=skyfall equip=true` hands over gear, `inventory` describes everything worn/carried,\n187\t  `game_cmd do=sell id=12` does any menu action exactly as the player would (it rides in the\n188\t  input frame, so replays include it). The game UI: `ui` reads what the player sees as text\n189\t  (the HUD, each open window by title, touch controls with their rects); `ui open=inventory,tree`\n190\t  / `close=all`, `device=touch width=844 height=390` (a phone), `hover=[x,y]` (a tooltip),\n191\t  `click=[x,y]` (presses what is there; its commands run) and `image=true` (the game with the UI\n192\t  over it). `capture` draws the UI too when a game runs (`ui=false` leaves it out); the windows\n193\t  `ui` opened stay open for later captures. `tree find=fire`, `tree take=Unbowed` (allocates the\n194\t  path), `tree_map` (PNG of the generated passive tree), `genome seed=7 parts=wings,horns`\n195\t  (grow a creature), `turntable seed=7` / `family=` / `boss=` (render it from all sides),\n196\t  `animsheet` (its attack frame by frame), `bestiary count=500` (generator variety), `boss`\n197\t  (spawn a designed or generated boss). Playable characters (`game/heroes.toml`: the Wanderer,\n198\t  Kestrel, Ysolde; the Hall of Heroes in town): `hero character=kestrel` plays as one (each keeps\n199\t  their own hero; the stash is shared), `game_cmd do=character name=ysolde` as the player would\n200\t  (in town), `turntable character=` / `animsheet character= skill=slash swing=3` show one. Levels: `level depth=17` (what a depth is: name,\n201\t  palette, mechanics, boss; `to=` for a range), `level` (the live one: every feature with its\n202\t  position and state), `levelmap depth=7 seed=3` (top-down PNG of a freshly built level, no\n203\t  GPU), `go place=level depth=9` (travel there, waypoint unlocked), `goto_feature kind=keg`\n204\t  (stand next to one), `game_cmd do=use spot=N` (the way down, a cursed chest);\n205\t  `autoplay` walks levels to their exits by itself.\n206\t- Building and judging content: `see` is a screenshot with numbered marks on monsters, the\n207\t  hero, townsfolk, loot, spots and level pieces plus a legend (talk about \"mark 7\" and know\n208\t  it's a rare Frost Ghoul at 40%); `campaign from=1 to=12 wall=300` lets the bot play down\n209\t  through the levels and reports each (time, deaths, kills, levels gained): run it after data\n210\t  changes; `turntable family=ghoul def={\"parts\":[{\"kind\":\"wings\"}],\"shirt\":\"#3050a0\"}` authors\n211\t  a creature as JSON over any family/boss/genome (or `{\"body\":\"quadruped\",...}` for a new one)\n212\t  and reports its anatomy; `theme_swatch depths=13-20` shows palettes; `levelmap nav=true`\n213\t  shows what the AI thinks is walkable and its planned way out. Game data lives in `game/*.toml`\n214\t  (`game_reload` re-reads it live; the tree is generated from `game/tree.toml`; levels from\n215\t  `themes.toml` and `levels.toml`, dressed with LIB/core props from the sets in `props.toml`).\n216\t- Looks: `look` lists the Look & Filters sections, presets and whole looks; `look name=HD-2D`,\n217\t  `look section=pixel preset=Chunky on=objects` set the session's look layer (applied in every\n218\t  capture); `look bench=all` renders this moment under every look in one numbered PNG. Filters\n219\t  aim at `all`, `objects` (characters & objects) or `environment` through `view.*_on` /\n220\t  `view.filter.*_on` / `pixel_target`, and `view.style_objects` / `view.style_environment`.\n221\t- Teaching: `room key=bloom` includes the room's station guide (`learn`) and its pads' notes;\n222\t  `guide term=kuwahara` / `guide search=shadow` read the field guide\n223\t  (crates/pav_core/src/field_guide.toml), `guide asks=true` lists every room's \"ask for it\"\n224\t  phrases.\n225\t- `course` shows the running course timer, gates, hits, falls, last result and best times;\n226\t  `feel` shows feel metrics (response ticks, time to top speed, stopping, turnaround, jump).\n227\t- Animation: `animsheet move=roundhouse` draws any move frame by frame (`hit=`, `side=-1` for the\n228\t  alternate swing), `animsheet clip=CMU/Cartwheel` any motion clip (`mirror=`, `upper=`,\n229\t  `travel=`; on the hero by default, `def=` for another look). `clips` lists the sets, `clips\n230\t  find=dance` searches names, tags and descriptions, `clips name=SET/Clip` shows one as readable\n231\t  key poses with its source and licence, `clips load=cmu` adds the on-disk CMU library.\n232\t  `clip_import from=<set.js|set.json|folder>` translates a set, `from=a.glb,b.glb sources=A,B\n233\t  catalog=anim/catalogs/mesh2motion.json set=MESH2MOTION` a glTF library (Rigify, Unreal-style or\n234\t  Mixamo rigs; `rm=` each file's root-motion twin, as Quaternius ships them, gives loops their\n235\t  speed), `from=lib.fbx` an FBX file (every animation stack a clip), `from=take.bvh at=2-9\n236\t  loop=true set=X` a BVH take (`way=back|left|right` for a loop that goes that way), and\n237\t  `catalog=anim/catalogs/cmu.json set=CMU` (a catalog with \"$pick\": cmu, 100style, bandai or\n238\t  lafan1) cuts its moments out of a capture database, downloading the takes; it checks the result\n239\t  reads back and reports the fit (`log=N` notes). `mocap` describes the open databases (CMU,\n240\t  100STYLE, Bandai Namco, LaFAN1, Mesh2Motion, Quaternius, Mixamo), `mocap find=limp` searches\n241\t  their takes, `mocap get=02_01,Zombie_FW` downloads (a 100STYLE or LaFAN1 take alone out of its\n242\t  archive; `get=cmu`: all 2,548 CMU takes), `mocap survey=ledger` / `survey=library` measures\n243\t  every CMU take into anim/cmu/takes.tsv / translates them into anim/cmu, and `mocap cut=13_17\n244\t  at=1.5-2.6 name=Jab set=MINE` (or `loop=true`: the best cycle; `way=`) fits one moment into\n245\t  anim/<set>.json. Room NPCs perform with `clips = [...]` / `moves = [...]`; any\n246\t  look's `idle_clip` plays while standing still and `walk_clip` (a walk loop that records its\n247\t  `speed`, e.g. STYLE100/Old_Walk) while walking, at the rate its stride matches the ground,\n248\t  `run_clip` above the pace between the two; `death_clip` is a captured fall and `attack_clips\n249\t  = { claw = \"QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch\" }` captured attacks by skill, timed so the clip's\n250\t  strike (shown by `clips name=`; `@seconds` after the name overrides it) lands on the hit, or\n251\t  a list of them, one per swing of the skill's combo; `attack_moves = { cleave = \"sweep\" }`\n252\t  swings a move of anim/moves.toml in place of the skill's own (a list per swing too);\n253\t  `dodge_clip` is a captured dodge in place of the tumble (bipeds: game/monsters.toml,\n254\t  bosses.toml and heroes.toml looks, and the genome's biped `gaits`, `idle_clips`,\n255\t  `death_clips`, `attack_clips`; `animsheet family=ghoul skill=claw` shows one);\n256\t  `anim.tempo` / `anim.mirror` steer performers.\n257\t- `camera_bench` renders the current moment from several camera presets/tilts in one PNG.\n258\t- `signal name=drop` fires spawners listening for a pad signal (no need to walk onto the pad).\n259\t- `filmstrip` tiles N frames (optionally while driving the player) into one PNG: the cheapest\n260\t  way to check motion and animation. `audio_capture` renders a session's sounds to .wav.\n261\t- `stream point=[x,y,z]` adds a streaming interest point (agents exploring the world).\n262\t- `input` drives the player: `move=[x,z]` world direction (x = east, z = south), `hold=`/`press=`\n263\t  buttons (jump, crouch, crawl, use, focus, interact, primary), `aim=[x,y,z]`, `ticks=N`.\n264\t- `record_save` + `replay` reproduce a session exactly (same machine/build) and check the hash:\n265\t  use them for bug reports. The game saves `replays/last.replay.json` from the tuning panel.\n266\t- One-shot calls accept `scene=`, `seed=` and `ticks=` to set up the session first.\n267\t- `pav repl` keeps one session across lines (lines are `tool key=value ...`; `#` = comment).\n268\t- Look at captures with your image-reading tool; prefer small sizes (e.g. `width=640 height=360`).\n269\t\n270\t## Browser and phones\n271\tHeadless Chromium can run the browser build (WebGPU on SwiftShader): launch with\n272\t`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`\n273\t(other flag sets show a blank canvas). `?room=NAME&seed=N` picks the start room.\n274\tPhones: emulate one in headless Chromium with Playwright (`viewport 844x390, isMobile, hasTouch,\n275\tdeviceScaleFactor: 1`; Chrome's DPR emulation leaves the canvas at CSS size) and drive it with\n276\tCDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`; SwiftShader frames take about a second, so send a tap's start and\n277\tend back to back.\n278\tFrom WSL2 you can launch the Windows build directly: `./target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe`.\n279\t\n280\t## Controls\n281\tKeyboard+mouse: WASD move, Space jump (hold = higher), C/Ctrl crouch, Z crawl toggle, F or left\n282\tclick throw bomb at the cursor, Shift walk slowly, walk into ladders to climb, jump at a ledge\n283\tand keep pushing toward it to grab it (push again/Space = pull up, C = drop), Space/C swim up/down,\n284\tcommitted model: C while running = dodge roll; right-drag rotate camera, wheel zoom, 1–8 camera\n285\tpresets. Gamepad: left stick move, right stick aim, A jump,\n286\tB crouch, Y crawl, X/RT bomb, LT slow, LB/RB rotate camera, D-pad zoom, Start menu, Back rewind.\n287\t\n288\tShardfall: WASD move, LMB/RMB/Q/E/R/F skills, Space dodge, 1 potion, Shift attack in place,\n289\tG use (vendor, stash, portal, gambler, alchemist, the way down, cursed chests), I/Tab\n290\tinventory, P passive tree, C character, K skills, M map, T town portal; gamepad\n291\tX/Y/B/RB/LB/RT skills, A dodge, D-pad up potion, D-pad right use, D-pad left map, D-pad down\n292\tpanels (LB/RB switch); in any window or the menu the stick drives a cursor (A click, X\n293\tright-click, hold Y shift, right stick scroll, B close). Controller flows can be scripted and\n294\tscreenshotted: `shardfall --pad-script FILE` (lines `<frames> [left=x,y] [right=x,y]\n295\t[hold=A,Y] [tap=DPadDown]`, see `PadScript` in input.rs).\n296\t\n297\tTouch (phones, tablets; the browser build): put a thumb down anywhere and drag to move (an\n298\tinvisible stick); attacks are automatic (the nearest foe in reach; a menu setting); the fan in\n299\tthe bottom right: dodge (big button), skills (tap: at the nearest foe · drag: aim, let go to\n300\tcast, back onto the button to cancel · hold: keep casting), potion, and a \"use\" button that\n301\tappears when something is in reach; top right: menu and bag. Swipe messages, banners and the\n302\tminimap away; tap the minimap for the big map; tap the game outside a window to close it.\n303\tGraphics quality (Auto/Low/Medium/High) and auto-attack are in the touch pause menu.\n304\t\n305\tH (world demo): how the room you are in works (the station guide: steps, pads, live settings,\n306\tuses, ask-for-it phrases, cost, the engine's code, words); outside rooms the field guide\n307\t(guide_ui.rs). Stepping on a pad with a note shows the note at the bottom for a while.\n308\tFixed system layer (never rebinds): Esc pause menu · F1 tuning panel · F2 rooms (teleport) ·\n309\tF3 boot diagnostics · F4 leave room · F5 reset room · F6 pause · F7 step · F8/F9 slower/faster ·\n310\tF10 edit mode (sandbox) · hold Backspace rewind · F11 fullscreen · F12 screenshot.\n311\tThe pause menu's *Look & filters* window (also atop the F1 panel) puts every filter on the whole\n312\tscene, the characters & objects or the environment, with sliders, presets and whole looks; it\n313\tis a layer over the scene's own settings, saved to `shardfall_looks.json` (look_ui.rs).\n314\tRooms may remap game keys while you are inside (`[keys]` in the room file); system keys never change.\n315\t\n316\t## Tests\n317\t`cargo test` includes `crates/pav_core/tests/gameplay.rs` (walk, jump onto a crate, climb the\n318\tladder, bomb the floor and drop through, crawl the tunnel, rewind repeatability, snapshot files),\n319\t`tests/world.rs` (pavilion layout, streaming, props persisting while dormant, room\n320\tenter/exit/reset, overrides, saved-object round trip), `tests/movement.rs` (courses, pads,\n321\tledge grab, swimming, pits, grid/committed models, projectiles, moving platforms, hazards),\n322\t`tests/physics.rs` (rope bridge, chain, soft bodies, conveyor, bounce, crumble/regrow, glass,\n323\tspawner pads, rewind with soft bodies; its room is `tests/physics_room.toml`, a compact example\n324\tof every physics feature) and `tests/rooms.rs` (every room file builds; courses complete).\n325\t`tests/motion.rs` (clips decode like the format's reference player, every embedded clip plays\n326\tcleanly, a set file round-trips, fades, chained moves, kicks, performers, idle clips, the hero's\n327\tcaptured death, walkers and villagers keeping their styles' pace); `tests/monsters.rs` also has\n328\ta ghoul shambling, running, clawing and falling in captured motion and generated bipeds drawing\n329\ttheirs from the genome; `crates/pav_tools/tests/mocap.rs`\n330\t(a glTF rig and a CMU take translate number for number like my-3D2dge's importer, whose output is\n331\tin tests/fixtures/mocap; the CMU survey measures a take as the committed ledger says; a BVH walk\n332\tcuts into a loop that closes; a sidestep take gives a loop each way, facing forward; an FBX file\n333\twritten by the test reads as a take); `tests/import.rs` (glTF and OBJ models built in code read\n334\tback exactly, mirrored nodes stay outward, texels give exact face colours, malformed files are\n335\terrors, normalisation, the `asset_import` tool), `tests/import_fit.rs` (a table folds into a top\n336\tand mirrored legs, a vase is a lathe, a blade an extrusion, a noisy blob a mesh part within budget;\n337\tthe engine reads every translation back; byte-identical twice; translate, check, compare and\n338\tsurvey through the tool), `tests/import_library.rs` (packs go to lib/ or local/ by licence\n339\twith their `PACK.json`, credits, index and catalog tags; unknown licences refused),\n340\t`tests/planted_defects.rs` (the store's five planted defects, each caught: size_band,\n341\tbelow_floor, socket_missing, a missing texture failing the import), `tests/store_rooms.rs` (the\n342\tLibrary Hall is current, the store rooms pass room_check, every id a sign names resolves, each\n343\tLimits sign is true, the Catalogue pages through every row with rewind and snapshots, the Store\n344\tShowcase shows every core material, the Clip Browser moves its whole cast together, Kenney Mini\n345\tDungeon through every step), `tests/figures.rs` (S3b: the KayKit adventurers check clean\n346\tas props and figures, every embedded clip poses three of them whole, finite and on the floor,\n347\tlimbs follow the puppet's side, a planted defect is caught, `assets find=knight`) and\n348\t`tests/import_khronos.rs` (opt-in,\n349\t`-- --ignored`: 12 Khronos sample models at a pinned commit). `pav_core/tests/prop_materials.rs`\n350\t(props wear library and inline materials, format 1's colours and revisions hold, unknown names,\n351\tone edit that adds and uses a material, snapshots) and `pav_tools/tests/material_preview.rs`\n352\t(a swatch renders headless with its layer lines).\n353\tThe game UI: `pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` (`ui` reads the HUD, windows and touch controls and\n354\tclicks a button; captures draw the UI).\n355\tGames on the hook: `pav_core/tests/games.rs` (the starter's bot wins on ten seeds, standing\n356\tstill loses, snapshot files, rewind and replays are exact, every game key names one scene)\n357\tand `pav_tools/tests/play.rs` (the `play` tool reports, drives and sweeps seeds).\n358\tShardfall: `tests/arpg.rs` (combat) and `tests/loot.rs` (drops, equipping, town trade, travel,\n359\trewind across travel, unique powers), `tests/skills.rs` (all 16 skills, tweaks, channels, the\n360\tpassive tree through commands, keystones, the bot spending points), `tests/monsters.rs`\n361\t(archetypes, broods, bombers, affixes, bosses through their phases, the Menagerie),\n362\t`tests/levels.rs` (every designed level has its mechanics, each mechanic works, endless\n363\tdepths, the sealed exit, waypoints, rewind in a level; dressing never moves a mechanic or a\n364\tmonster, is reproducible, keeps its snapshot budget and the paths; baked props collide, sleep\n365\tand restore), `tests/town.rs` (townsfolk, gambling,\n366\tbrewing, saves), `tests/feel.rs` (gibs, kill streaks, boss entrances), `tests/heroes.rs`\n367\t(playable characters: the hall, switching with a shared stash, strikes per combo swing,\n368\tcaptured dodges).\n369\tView: `pav_view/tests/pixel_art.rs`, `parts.rs` (characters & objects vs environment, filters per\n370\tpart, styles per part, styles/haze reach the renderer, transition loop), `look.rs` (look\n371\tsections, presets, whole looks), `water.rs` (ripples spread and fade, rain, pool strips merge)\n372\tand `learn.rs` (station guides and the field guide stay consistent with the engine);\n373\t`material_parity.rs` renders every material kernel on the GPU (lavapipe will do) and compares\n374\tit with the CPU reference.\n375\tExtend it when you add movement features; it is the cheapest way to catch feel regressions.\n376\tAlso, named for what they cover: `pav_core/tests/` `animation.rs`, `animation_preview.rs`,\n377\t`asset_library.rs`, `bench_holdout.rs`, `fx.rs`, `genre.rs`, `prop_families.rs`,\n378\t`prop_format2.rs`, `prop_instances.rs`, `prop_patch.rs`, `shipped_pack.rs` (the KayKit figures\n379\tload with no asset files), `vehicles.rs`; `pav_tools/tests/`\n380\t`animation_preview.rs`, `asset_errors.rs`, `asset_format2.rs`, `asset_library.rs`,\n381\t`asset_preview.rs`, `foundations.rs`, `reply_budget.rs`, `store.rs`.\n382\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"6565df47-d645-45be-98d8-8fdb49cd0079","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:57.932Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/REFERENCE.md","content":"# Reference\n\nThe detail behind `AGENTS.md`, read on demand: open the section you need, not the whole page.\n`pav help` lists every tool with its arguments.\n- [Code map](#code-map): what each crate and data folder holds.\n- [Studios](#studios): animation, objects and creatures, edited live.\n- [Tools](#tools): each tool family with examples.\n- [Browser and phones](#browser-and-phones): running the web build headless, emulating a phone.\n- [Controls](#controls): keyboard, gamepad, touch and the fixed system keys.\n- [Tests](#tests): what each suite covers.\n\n## Code map\n```\ncrates/\n  pav_core    simulation, no window/GPU/audio deps: Sim, entities, physics (rapier3d),\n              static regions (statics.rs: terrain chunks, rooms, hub; active or dormant;\n              blocks, decor and baked library props: drawn by the view's region cache, one\n              collider box each, no entity),\n              world.rs (pavilion layout, streaming, room tracking), room.rs (room files),\n              terrain.rs (procedural wilderness), tile levels (level.rs), characters\n              (character.rs: movement models instant/momentum/grid/committed, jump,\n              crouch/crawl, ladders, ledge grab/mantle, swimming, axis lock, moving platforms,\n              knockback, pushing shares momentum, bombs, ice slide), puppet (puppet.rs: body\n              plans biped/spider/lizard/beetle/blob/quadruped, procedural animation, hit recoil,\n              creature lunges, foot IK, legs that stride the way the body travels, idle breathing\n              and blinks, cutout look and camera cheats; the biped is a `Skel` of joints that the\n              procedural animation, moves and clips each produce and `dress` turns into parts),\n              moves.rs (attacks and gestures as data, anim/moves.toml: arcs around the shoulders,\n              wind-up from wherever the hands were, strikes with lunge/lean/twist/hop/spin,\n              follow-through; skills name a move, a look may name its own per skill and combo\n              swing: `attack_moves`), clips.rs (motion clips: readable key poses\n              translated from open animation libraries, retargeted onto the biped with IK,\n              crossfaded over the procedural animation, upper body only or mirrored; performers,\n              idle clips, walk clips played as fast as the character moves), anim.rs (the /anim files: embedded, live reload), rig.rs (creature feet that plant and step,\n              follow-the-leader spines, verlet tails/antennae), ai.rs (NPC brains: idle,\n              wander, patrol, circle, follow; they drive characters through InputFrames),\n              nav.rs (walkable grid from blocks and props, A* paths, flow fields),\n              games/ (the hook a new game implements, `Game`, and `GAMES`, the list that\n              makes each one a scene; starter.rs + starter.toml, the template:\n              docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md),\n              fxdef.rs (object lights / particle emitters / distortion, view-only),\n              vehicle.rs (drift car on rapier's raycast vehicle, arcade helicopter: flight only,\n              no weapons, damage or fuel), health.rs (shootable rapier objects: hp, score, boss\n              phases/bar, finish),\n              stealth.rs (guard sight cones with line of sight and an alert meter),\n              zones.rs (trigger zones + labels), course.rs (timers, gates, checkpoints, pits,\n              pads, camera cues, hits/respawn), behaviors.rs (movers, rotators, emitters,\n              spawners), projectile.rs (lightweight bullets), feel.rs (feel metrics),\n              softbody.rs (rapier soft bodies: jelly, balls, cloth, ropes), joints.rs (joints\n              owned by entities, recreated on wake), destruct.rs (crumbling/breakable tiles,\n              conveyors and bounce pads for props), history, params\n  pav_render  wgpu renderer (Vulkan/DX12): Scene description -> particles (compute) -> sun +\n              point-light shadow passes (shadows.rs) -> MSAA scene pass (+ GPU particles) ->\n              bloom chain and distortion (fx.rs) -> composite (outlines, screen-space GI,\n              tonemap, filter stack: pixelate/CRT/scanlines/dither/palettes/grading, split;\n              pixel art on part of the scene: objects flagged `flags::PIXEL`, chosen in the view\n              by `view.filter.pixel_target` = all/characters/hero/others/world/entity/objects/\n              environment; every filter can aim at a part: `flags::OBJECT` marks characters &\n              objects, the normal buffer carries it, `*_on` = all/objects/environment; painterly and\n              print styles: Kuwahara oil paint, CMYK halftone, ASCII, pencil sketch (`filter.stylize`);\n              hazy air: volumetric sun shafts ray-marched through the sun's shadow map and lamp\n              halos in closed form (`view.haze`, `shafts`, `halos`); screen transitions (iris,\n              diamonds, dissolve, mosaic, blinds, fade); wind in the vertex shader for instances\n              flagged `flags::SWAY` (leaves) / `flags::GRASS` (tufts that part around the player)).\n              Procedural meshes + analytic SDF spheres/capsules/rounded cones, SDF-font text in\n              the world (text.rs). Procedural materials: rows of a storage buffer read by one\n              kernel library (shaders/materials.wgsl, matched pixel for pixel by\n              `pav_core::material::eval`); `pav_view::materials` interns them into slots for\n              prop parts, static blocks (world-mapped) and decor. `render_scale` draws below the target's resolution and\n              upscale.rs stretches it over (phones). Offscreen capture -> PNG.\n  pav_view    sim frame -> render Scene: camera rig (tilt/yaw/distance/fov/ortho, all live),\n              look.rs + looks.toml (the Look & Filters layer: filter sections, presets, whole looks),\n              water.rs (water zones ripple: a CPU wave equation on a height grid, stirred by\n              whatever crosses the waterline, splashes, blasts and rain; drawn as a dynamic mesh),\n              assets.rs (`emit_asset`: a library asset drawn from game state each frame),\n              interpolation between ticks, visual settings (ViewSettings)\n  pav_audio   synthesized sound: oscillators/noise/envelopes/filters, event -> sound bank,\n              cpal output (optional), offline .wav rendering\n  pav_tools   agent layer: tool registry + `pav` CLI (one-shot, REPL) + MCP stdio server +\n              live bridge client (bridge.rs), and the motion importer (mocap/: glTF and FBX\n              libraries, CMU's ASF/AMC, BVH; Rigify, Unreal, Mixamo/MotionBuilder, 100STYLE and\n              Bandai Namco skeletons; loops cut at their best cycle; fitted into readable key\n              poses, number for number what my-3D2dge's own importer writes; the whole CMU\n              database surveyed and translated), and the asset importer (import/: what both\n              importers share, one `Scene` read from glTF/OBJ, normalisation, translation into\n              props with fidelity metrics, the licence gate that routes packs to lib/ or\n              local/; `asset_import`, `docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md`)\n  pav_app     the game (`shardfall` binary): window, boot diagnostics, input (keyboard/mouse,\n              gamepad via gilrs), system keys, tuning panel, pause menu, sim thread\n              (simhost.rs; stepped from the frame loop in the browser), live bridge server\n              (bridge.rs), egui input (uiinput.rs), graphics quality (quality.rs: render\n              scale, dynamic resolution). Builds natively and for wasm32 (WebGPU).\n  pav_ui      Shardfall's game UI in egui, drawn by the window and by the tools: the HUD\n              (arpg_ui.rs: orbs, skill bar, banners, minimap), the windows (arpg_items.rs:\n              inventory, shop, stash, character, skills; arpg_tree.rs: the passive tree), touch\n              screens (touch.rs: finger routing, invisible stick, button fan, auto-attack,\n              swipe-to-dismiss), and headless.rs (the same UI on a windowless context: a text\n              reading by window, clicks, and an egui-wgpu overlay painted over captures).\nanim/         animation data, embedded and hot-reloadable (`anim_reload`): moves.toml (the moves table)\n              and clip sets (*.json: QUATERNIUS, MESH2MOTION, CMU, STYLE100: 437 clips with credits).\n              anim/cmu/ holds every take of the CMU database (4,770 clips) and anim/100style/ the\n              100STYLE runs, backward walks and runs, sidesteps and idles (780 loops), on disk\n              only: `clips load=cmu`, `clips load=100style`. anim/local/ (git-ignored) holds what\n              is translated from libraries whose licences forbid sharing it (Bandai Namco, LaFAN1,\n              Mixamo): `clips load=local`. anim/catalogs/ says how each set is made (tags,\n              descriptions, sources, picks): `clip_import catalog=...` rebuilds it from the\n              libraries.\nrooms/        room data files (TOML: info card, station guide `[learn]`, wing, primary device, movement model, camera,\n              params, keys, entrance, ASCII tile layers + legend, [[object]]s). Every file\n              here is embedded in the exe at build time AND hot-reloaded at runtime.\n              `_template.toml` documents every field.\n```\n\n## Studios\nAnimation Studio: `scripts/animation-studio.sh` or `shardfall --animation-studio` opens an\nisolated preview and the live bridge. Use `.mcp.animation-studio.json` for visible MCP edits.\n`anim_edit` creates/copies/inspects/edits clips, with revisions and 32-step undo/redo;\n`anim_preview` plays, pauses, scrubs, and inspects their poses. Every accepted edit saves and\nupdates the live library. The preview preserves the game state. Native animation files also\nreload automatically. See `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`. REPLs accept structured JSON lines:\n`{\"tool\":\"anim_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"key\",\"name\":\"WORKSHOP/Wave\",\"time\":0.5,\"pose\":{\"armR\":[80,20,50,25,0]}}}`.\nUse the returned `revision` as `if_revision` on later edits. Copy source clips before editing;\nkeep local source copies and their history in `anim/local`.\n\nObject Studio: `scripts/asset-studio.sh` or `shardfall --asset-studio` opens reusable prop\nauthoring on the same live bridge (`.mcp.studio.json`). `assets find=words` searches templates\n(`BUILTIN/`), library packs (`LIB/pack/name`; `LIB/core` is embedded in every build, other packs\nload from disk natively, `assets/props/local/` is git-ignored) and saved definitions, ranked,\nwith `category= tags= tier= similar=` filters. `asset_edit` creates/copies/inspects/patches\nreadable JSON with stable part names, atomic batches, revisions, and 32-step history.\n`asset_preview` opens the isolated stage; `views=true` returns a framed 4-view contact sheet\n(`figure=true` adds a 1.8 m figure) and leaves the stage and camera as they were. `capture stats=only` returns render cost without\nan image. `asset_spawn` places one-root instances in the preserved scene. Edits refresh visuals\nand compound collision together. Native file changes reload after 250 ms of quiet. Saved\ndefinitions are `assets/props/workshop/*.json` (`PAV_ASSETS` overrides the props root).\n`studio_status ticket=N` confirms frame submission for live edits without a capture. The\nAnimations / Objects / Game tabs retain each workspace's controls and camera. See\n`docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` (tools and format) and `docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md` (the live studio).\nKeep procedural parts as text; use `if_revision` and batch related part changes in one `ops`\narray. Materials (planks, brick, cobbles … as per-pixel recipes, `docs/MATERIALS.md`): parts say\n`\"mat\":\"MAT/oak_planks\"` or a key in the asset's `materials`; `kind=material` on `assets`,\n`asset_edit` (workshop materials `MAT/workshop/x` in `assets/materials/workshop/`, `PAV_MATERIALS`\noverrides the root; revisions `mat1-`) and `asset_preview` (a swatch with each layer's legibility\nat the game camera). Game code draws units and scenery from its own state with library assets,\none call per thing per frame: `pav_view::assets::emit_asset(scene, \"BUILTIN/crate\",\nPlacement::at(pos).yaw(deg).id(id), seed, &palette)` (no physics needed; `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`,\n\"Library assets in game code\"). Game data and rooms may name only assets every build carries\n(embedded, or a shipped pack's: `props::store::SHIPPED`).\n\nCreature Studio: `scripts/creature-studio.sh` or `shardfall --creature-studio` opens the\nprocedural creature stage. `tools/creature-compiler` vendors the exact SpawnForge core/modules\npin and bundles it with `npm ci --ignore-scripts && npm run build` (run in that directory).\nKeep the pin and source hashes intact; do not resolve against a moving upstream checkout.\n`creature_catalog`, `creature_edit`, `creature_preview`, and `creature_status` expose theme,\ntemplate, blueprint, named-part and surface authoring through the same MCP bridge. Edits\nqueue asynchronous builds. Wait for `published`, `failed`, or `superseded`; only publication\ngets a frame ticket. Use the new source `revision` for the next edit, and `studio_status`\nfor actual frame submission. Failed/obsolete builds keep the last valid native mesh.\nSources, history and disposable caches are under `assets/creatures` (`PAV_CREATURES`\noverrides it). Node runs outside the simulation. The Windows package includes the bundle\nand portable Node. See `docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md` for native material limits and the tool\ncontract. This is an authoring/preview stage; gameplay spawning of these rigs is separate.\n\n## Tools\n- Import: `asset_import` alone lists the open model libraries; `get=kenney/mini_dungeon` downloads\n  a pack its catalog pins (`assets/catalogs/<lib>.json`) into .cache/assets, checked by SHA-256;\n  `from=<model> list=true` summarises a .glb/.gltf/.obj (parts, triangles, size in cm, materials,\n  main colours, warnings); `from=<model|folder|lib/pack>` translates into format-2 props\n  (primitives, plus one read-only vertex-coloured mesh part for what they cannot fit; `fit=prims|mesh`)\n  with the catalog's category and tags, routed by the licence gate: CC0/CC-BY packs to\n  `assets/props/lib/<pack>/` (committed, with `PACK.json`; then the index and `CREDITS.md`),\n  other licences, packs whose catalog says `\"local\"` and loose files to the git-ignored\n  `assets/props/local/<pack>/` (or `out=`), with their fidelity (six-view IoU, ΔE, Chamfer mm,\n  tier; `docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md`); `survey=<lib/pack|folder>` fits without writing\n  and fills the ledger (`assets/catalogs/<lib>/<pack>.tsv`, keeping each row's `note`; `fit=false`:\n  census only); `check=<asset.json> compare=true` measures a translation again and returns\n  source-over-translation views. `up= yaw= scale= place=` bring a model into the engine's frame\n  (a translation records them in `source.norm` for `check`).\n- Games on the hook (`pav_core::games`, `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`; scene `starter`): `play` gives\n  the running game's HUD lines, outcome and `status`; `play bot=true` lets its bot play on\n  (`ticks=`, default 60 s); `play bot=true seeds=10` plays fresh runs on seeds 1..10 and leaves\n  the session alone: `wins`, one `[seed, outcome, seconds]` row each, and the state of every\n  run not won.\n- Shardfall (scenes `town`, `arena`): `game` is the status, `autoplay seconds=30` lets a bot\n  fight, `loot_roll level=40 count=5000` summarises loot tables without playing, `give\n  unique=skyfall equip=true` hands over gear, `inventory` describes everything worn/carried,\n  `game_cmd do=sell id=12` does any menu action exactly as the player would (it rides in the\n  input frame, so replays include it). The game UI: `ui` reads what the player sees as text\n  (the HUD, each open window by title, touch controls with their rects); `ui open=inventory,tree`\n  / `close=all`, `device=touch width=844 height=390` (a phone), `hover=[x,y]` (a tooltip),\n  `click=[x,y]` (presses what is there; its commands run) and `image=true` (the game with the UI\n  over it). `capture` draws the UI too when a game runs (`ui=false` leaves it out); the windows\n  `ui` opened stay open for later captures. `tree find=fire`, `tree take=Unbowed` (allocates the\n  path), `tree_map` (PNG of the generated passive tree), `genome seed=7 parts=wings,horns`\n  (grow a creature), `turntable seed=7` / `family=` / `boss=` (render it from all sides),\n  `animsheet` (its attack frame by frame), `bestiary count=500` (generator variety), `boss`\n  (spawn a designed or generated boss). Playable characters (`game/heroes.toml`: the Wanderer,\n  Kestrel, Ysolde; the Hall of Heroes in town): `hero character=kestrel` plays as one (each keeps\n  their own hero; the stash is shared), `game_cmd do=character name=ysolde` as the player would\n  (in town), `turntable character=` / `animsheet character= skill=slash swing=3` show one. Levels: `level depth=17` (what a depth is: name,\n  palette, mechanics, boss; `to=` for a range), `level` (the live one: every feature with its\n  position and state), `levelmap depth=7 seed=3` (top-down PNG of a freshly built level, no\n  GPU), `go place=level depth=9` (travel there, waypoint unlocked), `goto_feature kind=keg`\n  (stand next to one), `game_cmd do=use spot=N` (the way down, a cursed chest);\n  `autoplay` walks levels to their exits by itself.\n- Building and judging content: `see` is a screenshot with numbered marks on monsters, the\n  hero, townsfolk, loot, spots and level pieces plus a legend (talk about \"mark 7\" and know\n  it's a rare Frost Ghoul at 40%); `campaign from=1 to=12 wall=300` lets the bot play down\n  through the levels and reports each (time, deaths, kills, levels gained): run it after data\n  changes; `turntable family=ghoul def={\"parts\":[{\"kind\":\"wings\"}],\"shirt\":\"#3050a0\"}` authors\n  a creature as JSON over any family/boss/genome (or `{\"body\":\"quadruped\",...}` for a new one)\n  and reports its anatomy; `theme_swatch depths=13-20` shows palettes; `levelmap nav=true`\n  shows what the AI thinks is walkable and its planned way out. Game data lives in `game/*.toml`\n  (`game_reload` re-reads it live; the tree is generated from `game/tree.toml`; levels from\n  `themes.toml` and `levels.toml`, dressed with LIB/core props from the sets in `props.toml`).\n- Looks: `look` lists the Look & Filters sections, presets and whole looks; `look name=HD-2D`,\n  `look section=pixel preset=Chunky on=objects` set the session's look layer (applied in every\n  capture); `look bench=all` renders this moment under every look in one numbered PNG. Filters\n  aim at `all`, `objects` (characters & objects) or `environment` through `view.*_on` /\n  `view.filter.*_on` / `pixel_target`, and `view.style_objects` / `view.style_environment`.\n- Teaching: `room key=bloom` includes the room's station guide (`learn`) and its pads' notes;\n  `guide term=kuwahara` / `guide search=shadow` read the field guide\n  (crates/pav_core/src/field_guide.toml), `guide asks=true` lists every room's \"ask for it\"\n  phrases.\n- `course` shows the running course timer, gates, hits, falls, last result and best times;\n  `feel` shows feel metrics (response ticks, time to top speed, stopping, turnaround, jump).\n- Animation: `animsheet move=roundhouse` draws any move frame by frame (`hit=`, `side=-1` for the\n  alternate swing), `animsheet clip=CMU/Cartwheel` any motion clip (`mirror=`, `upper=`,\n  `travel=`; on the hero by default, `def=` for another look). `clips` lists the sets, `clips\n  find=dance` searches names, tags and descriptions, `clips name=SET/Clip` shows one as readable\n  key poses with its source and licence, `clips load=cmu` adds the on-disk CMU library.\n  `clip_import from=<set.js|set.json|folder>` translates a set, `from=a.glb,b.glb sources=A,B\n  catalog=anim/catalogs/mesh2motion.json set=MESH2MOTION` a glTF library (Rigify, Unreal-style or\n  Mixamo rigs; `rm=` each file's root-motion twin, as Quaternius ships them, gives loops their\n  speed), `from=lib.fbx` an FBX file (every animation stack a clip), `from=take.bvh at=2-9\n  loop=true set=X` a BVH take (`way=back|left|right` for a loop that goes that way), and\n  `catalog=anim/catalogs/cmu.json set=CMU` (a catalog with \"$pick\": cmu, 100style, bandai or\n  lafan1) cuts its moments out of a capture database, downloading the takes; it checks the result\n  reads back and reports the fit (`log=N` notes). `mocap` describes the open databases (CMU,\n  100STYLE, Bandai Namco, LaFAN1, Mesh2Motion, Quaternius, Mixamo), `mocap find=limp` searches\n  their takes, `mocap get=02_01,Zombie_FW` downloads (a 100STYLE or LaFAN1 take alone out of its\n  archive; `get=cmu`: all 2,548 CMU takes), `mocap survey=ledger` / `survey=library` measures\n  every CMU take into anim/cmu/takes.tsv / translates them into anim/cmu, and `mocap cut=13_17\n  at=1.5-2.6 name=Jab set=MINE` (or `loop=true`: the best cycle; `way=`) fits one moment into\n  anim/<set>.json. Room NPCs perform with `clips = [...]` / `moves = [...]`; any\n  look's `idle_clip` plays while standing still and `walk_clip` (a walk loop that records its\n  `speed`, e.g. STYLE100/Old_Walk) while walking, at the rate its stride matches the ground,\n  `run_clip` above the pace between the two; `death_clip` is a captured fall and `attack_clips\n  = { claw = \"QUATERNIUS/Zombie_Scratch\" }` captured attacks by skill, timed so the clip's\n  strike (shown by `clips name=`; `@seconds` after the name overrides it) lands on the hit, or\n  a list of them, one per swing of the skill's combo; `attack_moves = { cleave = \"sweep\" }`\n  swings a move of anim/moves.toml in place of the skill's own (a list per swing too);\n  `dodge_clip` is a captured dodge in place of the tumble (bipeds: game/monsters.toml,\n  bosses.toml and heroes.toml looks, and the genome's biped `gaits`, `idle_clips`,\n  `death_clips`, `attack_clips`; `animsheet family=ghoul skill=claw` shows one);\n  `anim.tempo` / `anim.mirror` steer performers.\n- `camera_bench` renders the current moment from several camera presets/tilts in one PNG.\n- `signal name=drop` fires spawners listening for a pad signal (no need to walk onto the pad).\n- `filmstrip` tiles N frames (optionally while driving the player) into one PNG: the cheapest\n  way to check motion and animation. `audio_capture` renders a session's sounds to .wav.\n- `stream point=[x,y,z]` adds a streaming interest point (agents exploring the world).\n- `input` drives the player: `move=[x,z]` world direction (x = east, z = south), `hold=`/`press=`\n  buttons (jump, crouch, crawl, use, focus, interact, primary), `aim=[x,y,z]`, `ticks=N`.\n- `record_save` + `replay` reproduce a session exactly (same machine/build) and check the hash:\n  use them for bug reports. The game saves `replays/last.replay.json` from the tuning panel.\n- One-shot calls accept `scene=`, `seed=` and `ticks=` to set up the session first.\n- `pav repl` keeps one session across lines (lines are `tool key=value ...`; `#` = comment).\n- Look at captures with your image-reading tool; prefer small sizes (e.g. `width=640 height=360`).\n\n## Browser and phones\nHeadless Chromium can run the browser build (WebGPU on SwiftShader): launch with\n`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`\n(other flag sets show a blank canvas). `?room=NAME&seed=N` picks the start room.\nPhones: emulate one in headless Chromium with Playwright (`viewport 844x390, isMobile, hasTouch,\ndeviceScaleFactor: 1`; Chrome's DPR emulation leaves the canvas at CSS size) and drive it with\nCDP `Input.dispatchTouchEvent`; SwiftShader frames take about a second, so send a tap's start and\nend back to back.\nFrom WSL2 you can launch the Windows build directly: `./target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe`.\n\n## Controls\nKeyboard+mouse: WASD move, Space jump (hold = higher), C/Ctrl crouch, Z crawl toggle, F or left\nclick throw bomb at the cursor, Shift walk slowly, walk into ladders to climb, jump at a ledge\nand keep pushing toward it to grab it (push again/Space = pull up, C = drop), Space/C swim up/down,\ncommitted model: C while running = dodge roll; right-drag rotate camera, wheel zoom, 1–8 camera\npresets. Gamepad: left stick move, right stick aim, A jump,\nB crouch, Y crawl, X/RT bomb, LT slow, LB/RB rotate camera, D-pad zoom, Start menu, Back rewind.\n\nShardfall: WASD move, LMB/RMB/Q/E/R/F skills, Space dodge, 1 potion, Shift attack in place,\nG use (vendor, stash, portal, gambler, alchemist, the way down, cursed chests), I/Tab\ninventory, P passive tree, C character, K skills, M map, T town portal; gamepad\nX/Y/B/RB/LB/RT skills, A dodge, D-pad up potion, D-pad right use, D-pad left map, D-pad down\npanels (LB/RB switch); in any window or the menu the stick drives a cursor (A click, X\nright-click, hold Y shift, right stick scroll, B close). Controller flows can be scripted and\nscreenshotted: `shardfall --pad-script FILE` (lines `<frames> [left=x,y] [right=x,y]\n[hold=A,Y] [tap=DPadDown]`, see `PadScript` in input.rs).\n\nTouch (phones, tablets; the browser build): put a thumb down anywhere and drag to move (an\ninvisible stick); attacks are automatic (the nearest foe in reach; a menu setting); the fan in\nthe bottom right: dodge (big button), skills (tap: at the nearest foe · drag: aim, let go to\ncast, back onto the button to cancel · hold: keep casting), potion, and a \"use\" button that\nappears when something is in reach; top right: menu and bag. Swipe messages, banners and the\nminimap away; tap the minimap for the big map; tap the game outside a window to close it.\nGraphics quality (Auto/Low/Medium/High) and auto-attack are in the touch pause menu.\n\nH (world demo): how the room you are in works (the station guide: steps, pads, live settings,\nuses, ask-for-it phrases, cost, the engine's code, words); outside rooms the field guide\n(guide_ui.rs). Stepping on a pad with a note shows the note at the bottom for a while.\nFixed system layer (never rebinds): Esc pause menu · F1 tuning panel · F2 rooms (teleport) ·\nF3 boot diagnostics · F4 leave room · F5 reset room · F6 pause · F7 step · F8/F9 slower/faster ·\nF10 edit mode (sandbox) · hold Backspace rewind · F11 fullscreen · F12 screenshot.\nThe pause menu's *Look & filters* window (also atop the F1 panel) puts every filter on the whole\nscene, the characters & objects or the environment, with sliders, presets and whole looks; it\nis a layer over the scene's own settings, saved to `shardfall_looks.json` (look_ui.rs).\nRooms may remap game keys while you are inside (`[keys]` in the room file); system keys never change.\n\n## Tests\n`cargo test` includes `crates/pav_core/tests/gameplay.rs` (walk, jump onto a crate, climb the\nladder, bomb the floor and drop through, crawl the tunnel, rewind repeatability, snapshot files),\n`tests/world.rs` (pavilion layout, streaming, props persisting while dormant, room\nenter/exit/reset, overrides, saved-object round trip), `tests/movement.rs` (courses, pads,\nledge grab, swimming, pits, grid/committed models, projectiles, moving platforms, hazards),\n`tests/physics.rs` (rope bridge, chain, soft bodies, conveyor, bounce, crumble/regrow, glass,\nspawner pads, rewind with soft bodies; its room is `tests/physics_room.toml`, a compact example\nof every physics feature) and `tests/rooms.rs` (every room file builds; courses complete).\n`tests/motion.rs` (clips decode like the format's reference player, every embedded clip plays\ncleanly, a set file round-trips, fades, chained moves, kicks, performers, idle clips, the hero's\ncaptured death, walkers and villagers keeping their styles' pace); `tests/monsters.rs` also has\na ghoul shambling, running, clawing and falling in captured motion and generated bipeds drawing\ntheirs from the genome; `crates/pav_tools/tests/mocap.rs`\n(a glTF rig and a CMU take translate number for number like my-3D2dge's importer, whose output is\nin tests/fixtures/mocap; the CMU survey measures a take as the committed ledger says; a BVH walk\ncuts into a loop that closes; a sidestep take gives a loop each way, facing forward; an FBX file\nwritten by the test reads as a take); `tests/import.rs` (glTF and OBJ models built in code read\nback exactly, mirrored nodes stay outward, texels give exact face colours, malformed files are\nerrors, normalisation, the `asset_import` tool), `tests/import_fit.rs` (a table folds into a top\nand mirrored legs, a vase is a lathe, a blade an extrusion, a noisy blob a mesh part within budget;\nthe engine reads every translation back; byte-identical twice; translate, check, compare and\nsurvey through the tool), `tests/import_library.rs` (packs go to lib/ or local/ by licence\nwith their `PACK.json`, credits, index and catalog tags; unknown licences refused),\n`tests/planted_defects.rs` (the store's five planted defects, each caught: size_band,\nbelow_floor, socket_missing, a missing texture failing the import), `tests/store_rooms.rs` (the\nLibrary Hall is current, the store rooms pass room_check, every id a sign names resolves, each\nLimits sign is true, the Catalogue pages through every row with rewind and snapshots, the Store\nShowcase shows every core material, the Clip Browser moves its whole cast together, Kenney Mini\nDungeon through every step), `tests/figures.rs` (S3b: the KayKit adventurers check clean\nas props and figures, every embedded clip poses three of them whole, finite and on the floor,\nlimbs follow the puppet's side, a planted defect is caught, `assets find=knight`) and\n`tests/import_khronos.rs` (opt-in,\n`-- --ignored`: 12 Khronos sample models at a pinned commit). `pav_core/tests/prop_materials.rs`\n(props wear library and inline materials, format 1's colours and revisions hold, unknown names,\none edit that adds and uses a material, snapshots) and `pav_tools/tests/material_preview.rs`\n(a swatch renders headless with its layer lines).\nThe game UI: `pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` (`ui` reads the HUD, windows and touch controls and\nclicks a button; captures draw the UI).\nGames on the hook: `pav_core/tests/games.rs` (the starter's bot wins on ten seeds, standing\nstill loses, snapshot files, rewind and replays are exact, every game key names one scene)\nand `pav_tools/tests/play.rs` (the `play` tool reports, drives and sweeps seeds).\nShardfall: `tests/arpg.rs` (combat) and `tests/loot.rs` (drops, equipping, town trade, travel,\nrewind across travel, unique powers), `tests/skills.rs` (all 16 skills, tweaks, channels, the\npassive tree through commands, keystones, the bot spending points), `tests/monsters.rs`\n(archetypes, broods, bombers, affixes, bosses through their phases, the Menagerie),\n`tests/levels.rs` (every designed level has its mechanics, each mechanic works, endless\ndepths, the sealed exit, waypoints, rewind in a level; dressing never moves a mechanic or a\nmonster, is reproducible, keeps its snapshot budget and the paths; baked props collide, sleep\nand restore), `tests/town.rs` (townsfolk, gambling,\nbrewing, saves), `tests/feel.rs` (gibs, kill streaks, boss entrances), `tests/heroes.rs`\n(playable characters: the hall, switching with a shared stash, strikes per combo swing,\ncaptured dodges).\nView: `pav_view/tests/pixel_art.rs`, `parts.rs` (characters & objects vs environment, filters per\npart, styles per part, styles/haze reach the renderer, transition loop), `look.rs` (look\nsections, presets, whole looks), `water.rs` (ripples spread and fade, rain, pool strips merge)\nand `learn.rs` (station guides and the field guide stay consistent with the engine);\n`material_parity.rs` renders every material kernel on the GPU (lavapipe will do) and compares\nit with the CPU reference.\nExtend it when you add movement features; it is the cheapest way to catch feel regressions.\nAlso, named for what they cover: `pav_core/tests/` `animation.rs`, `animation_preview.rs`,\n`asset_library.rs`, `bench_holdout.rs`, `fx.rs`, `genre.rs`, `prop_families.rs`,\n`prop_format2.rs`, `prop_instances.rs`, `prop_patch.rs`, `shipped_pack.rs` (the KayKit figures\nload with no asset files), `vehicles.rs`; `pav_tools/tests/`\n`animation_preview.rs`, `asset_errors.rs`, `asset_format2.rs`, `asset_library.rs`,\n`asset_preview.rs`, `foundations.rs`, `reply_budget.rs`, `store.rs`.\n","numLines":382,"startLine":1,"totalLines":382}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019eJJv1xHhoNHzZ7Si7gt98","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013M49iiJbNu6P3tD9r1m1vc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/AGENTS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"46f2c074-c2a1-4e3a-8645-61c49f15d21d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:58.836Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013M49iiJbNu6P3tD9r1m1vc":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/AGENTS.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013M49iiJbNu6P3tD9r1m1vc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md — rulebook for coding agents\n2\t\n3\tMaking a new game on the engine? Read `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`: the \"Key rules\" below apply to\n4\tyour game, the maintainers' workflow (HISTORY, PROGRESS, PRs, escalations) doesn't.\n5\t\n6\tShardfall is a procedural hack-and-slash game built on the Pavilion engine, written in Rust. The\n7\tprinciples are in `docs/DOCTRINE.md`, which outranks everything else here. The current state is\n8\t`docs/PROGRESS.md` (one page). Read both before starting; Claude Code loads them, with this file,\n9\tthrough `CLAUDE.md`. The design is in `docs/DESIGN.md` (engine) and `docs/GAME.md` (Shardfall):\n10\tread them when your work touches the design. `docs/REFERENCE.md` holds the full code map, every\n11\ttool family with examples, the controls and what each test suite covers: open the section you\n12\tneed. The journal and past decisions are in `docs/HISTORY.md`, newest first: search it, don't\n13\tread it whole. For a standalone Linux source handoff, `START_HERE.md` covers setup and headless\n14\tCLI examples.\n15\t\n16\t## How the doctrine applies here\n17\tAdopted 2026-10-09, partway through development. Code from before then isn't rewritten to fit;\n18\tfix a mismatch when it gets in the way.\n19\t- **Platform (5, 10):** the development platform is Linux, where agents build and test. The\n20\t  user's Windows `.exe` and the browser build count as part of the target too: a problem the user\n21\t  can see gets fixed now. Replays are promised to match only on the machine that recorded them; to\n22\t  chase something the user saw, start from a snapshot taken just before it.\n23\t- **Renderer (6):** wgpu is the WebGPU implementation: Vulkan on Linux and Windows (DX12 as a\n24\t  Windows option), the browser's own WebGPU on the web, lavapipe where there's no GPU. GPU compute\n25\t  stays cosmetic. The game UI is egui.\n26\t- **API and internals (7, 8):** the game (`pav_core/src/arpg/`) still lives inside the engine\n27\t  crate, so the compiler doesn't enforce the line. The engine modules the game uses are its API:\n28\t  `sim`, `entity`, `frame`, `rng`, `input`, `params`, `statics`, `nav`, `zones`, `character`,\n29\t  `projectile`, `puppet`, `parts`, `moves`, `clips`, `shape`, `color`, `fxdef`, and `games` (the\n30\t  hook a new game implements: `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`). Everything else\n31\t  (renderer, physics wiring, synth, importers) is internals. If game work means reading\n32\t  internals, fix the API or the error message.\n33\t- **Versions (9):** current pins stay (Rust 1.98.1, wgpu 30, rapier 0.36, egui 0.36, glam 0.33,\n34\t  cpal 0.18). The rule applies to new dependencies and to upgrades.\n35\t- **Assets (4):** no image, model, texture or audio files; fonts are allowed. Animation and\n36\t  objects are readable text: key poses (`anim/*.json`, the format `clips.rs` documents, made with\n37\t  `clip_import`) and props made of named primitive parts (`assets/props`, `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`).\n38\t  Raw downloads (.glb, .gltf, .obj, .fbx, .bvh, .amc) go to `.cache/` (git-ignored); never commit\n39\t  them, or images. Keep each source's credit and licence. Libraries whose licences forbid sharing\n40\t  what is made from them (Bandai Namco, LaFAN1, Mixamo) are translated only into the git-ignored\n41\t  local tiers (`anim/local`, `assets/props/local`).\n42\t- **Escalation:** ask in chat and log it in `docs/ESCALATIONS.md`. If you can schedule a check-in\n43\t  (e.g. `send_later`), set one for 15 minutes and carry on with other work; if not, make the call,\n44\t  log it and continue.\n45\t- **Pavilion Lite** (`pavilion-lite/`) is frozen: its renderer runs on the CPU, not WebGPU (6),\n46\t  so it isn't developed further (`docs/ESCALATIONS.md`).\n47\t\n48\t## Working rules\n49\tUnder the doctrine, in priority order:\n50\t1. **Gameplay first, then robustness.**\n51\t2. **Use tools.** If a tool does a job faster, more accurately or cheaper over time, use or build one.\n52\t3. **It must still run well on a modern PC** (the user's RTX 3060 Ti and 4070 Super). Other\n53\t   optimization and compatibility wait (10).\n54\t4. **Approximations are fine if they feel right.** Feel beats physical accuracy.\n55\t5. **Check selectively.** Verify what often breaks or is expensive to debug; skip routine checks\n56\t   of things that almost never break. \"If it's broken, the user will say so\" is valid.\n57\t6. **Cost over speed.** Prefer the CLI/capture tools over reading lots of code.\n58\t\n59\t## Testing budget (prototype stage)\n60\tEvery engine here is a prototype with one user: spend on finding what clearly helps, not on\n61\tmeasuring exactly how much. Completion comes first: a test decides how something is built and is\n62\trecorded; it never stops, skips or reverts planned work.\n63\t- **Test only to change a decision.** Before a test, name the choice it decides and its cost in\n64\t  US$ as Claude Code bills it, subagents included. If no choice rides on it, or a wrong choice\n65\t  would cost less than the test, skip it. Afterwards, report what it cost.\n66\t- **Size the test to the gap.** Agent runs (benchmarks, judges, eval agents) start small: 3-5 per\n67\t  arm. A clear gap decides it: 2:1 or better in wins, or 25% or more in cost, model calls or\n68\t  errors.\n69\t- **Near 50/50, make the call.** If the first batch is within 60/40 (or 10%), stop: the options\n70\t  are about equally good, so the choice matters little (Fredkin's paradox). Take the simpler,\n71\t  cheaper or more reversible option, log the call and why, and move on. Between clear and close:\n72\t  at most one more small batch, then decide.\n73\t- **Close calls belong to tool tests.** Checks with no model calls (cargo tests, `pav` checks and\n74\t  captures, scripted counts) cost almost nothing per run and repeat exactly, so they may scale up\n75\t  to settle narrow margins. Even then, don't chase gains under 5%; timing differences under 10%\n76\t  are noise.\n77\t- Looks and feel are the expensive, noisy kind: prefer objective proxies; use agent judges only for\n78\t  large, obvious differences, few of them, several items per call; leave fine visual judgement to\n79\t  the user on a quick comparison page.\n80\t- Explore broadly: test distinct hypotheses, not variations of one. Don't add or keep code without\n81\t  a verified benefit.\n82\t- Count cost end to end, in US$, not one tool's traffic: every model call re-reads the agent's\n83\t  whole context.\n84\t- Assets made through the documented loop (a brief, `check` to zero findings, a 4-view sheet at\n85\t  the game camera, at most two fix rounds, `publish` with a review) need no human review: the user\n86\t  accepted 28 of 28 (2026-10-12). Show the user only edge cases, or complex ones you are unsure of.\n87\t- Per PR (from 2026-10-16):\n88\t  - Run the full checks (tests of the touched crates, clippy, fmt, the wasm check when the app\n89\t    builds the change) once, on the head you merge.\n90\t  - After a rebase or a small fix, run only the tests of what changed. A docs-only PR needs none.\n91\t  - Merge as soon as the checks pass; don't wait for a review (Codex has posted none since #45 on\n92\t    2026-10-12). A review that arrives later: fix its real findings in a follow-up PR.\n93\t  - Nothing deploys: there is no hosted site. After a merge that can change the game, build the\n94\t    single-file HTML and send it to the user (`CLAUDE.md`, \"Builds for playing and testing\").\n95\t\n96\t## Architecture\n97\tCrates (the full map, module by module: `docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Code map\"):\n98\t- `pav_core`: the simulation, with no window, GPU or audio dependencies: `Sim`, entities, physics\n99\t  (rapier3d), the world, rooms and terrain, characters and puppets, moves and clips, AI and nav,\n100\t  props and materials; the game lives in `src/arpg/`.\n101\t- `pav_render`: the wgpu renderer: shadows, bloom and post effects, the filter stack, procedural\n102\t  meshes and materials, offscreen capture to PNG.\n103\t- `pav_view`: sim frame -> render scene: the camera rig, looks and filters, water, `emit_asset`.\n104\t- `pav_audio`: synthesized sound: cpal output, offline .wav rendering.\n105\t- `pav_tools`: the agent layer: the tool registry, the `pav` CLI and REPL, the MCP server, the\n106\t  live bridge client, and the motion and asset importers.\n107\t- `pav_ui`: Shardfall's egui UI (HUD, inventory, passive tree, touch controls), drawn by the\n108\t  window and, headless, by the tools (`ui`, captures).\n109\t- `pav_app`: the game (`shardfall` binary): window, input, sim thread, live bridge server, the\n110\t  pavilion's egui UI; native and wasm32.\n111\t\n112\tData: `anim/` (moves and motion clips), `rooms/` (room files, embedded in the exe and hot-reloaded;\n113\t`_template.toml` documents every field), `game/` (Shardfall's data), `assets/` (props, materials,\n114\tmodel catalogs), `store/` (the asset store's tables).\n115\tData flow: `Sim::step(InputFrame)` (fixed tick, own thread) -> `Sim::frame()` -> `RenderFrame`\n116\t-> `pav_view::ViewBuilder::build` (interpolates prev/curr) -> `pav_render::Scene` -> `Renderer`.\n117\t\n118\tKey rules:\n119\t- `pav_core` must never depend on graphics, windowing or audio crates.\n120\t- Everything that changes during play lives in `SimState` (cloning it = snapshot). Keep it `Clone`.\n121\t- Same inputs and seed, same state (doctrine 5): randomness comes from `rng`, seeded (the sim's\n122\t  `Rng`, or its hash for seed-derived content), never from the clock; don't let\n123\t  `HashMap`/`HashSet` iteration order reach game state (use a `BTreeMap` or sort).\n124\t- Gameplay code reads plain struct fields; expose tunables via `impl Tunable` (see `params.rs`).\n125\t  Tunables are automatically in the tuning panel, the `params`/`set` tools and preset files.\n126\t- Colors in data are sRGB hex (`Color::hex(\"#e8704a\")`); internally linear.\n127\t- Physics precision switch: in `crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml` change `package = \"rapier3d\"` to\n128\t  `\"rapier3d-f64\"`.\n129\t\n130\t## Build, run, test\n131\t```sh\n132\tscripts/setup-linux.sh             # once per machine (apt packages, lavapipe, mingw, wine)\n133\tcargo build                        # everything (Linux)\n134\tcargo test                         # every crate's tests (`-p pav_core` for one crate)\n135\tcargo fmt --all --check            # formatting\n136\tcargo clippy -p pav_core --all-targets -- -D warnings  # lints, for each crate you touched\n137\tcargo run -p pav_app               # the game (needs a display; Xvfb works with lavapipe)\n138\tscripts/build-windows.sh           # -> target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe\n139\tscripts/smoke-windows.sh 25        # run the .exe under Wine+lavapipe, screenshot + log in out/smoke/\n140\tscripts/smoke-linux.sh 10          # same for the native Linux build\n141\tscripts/build-web.sh               # browser build -> target/web/ (serve over HTTP; Chrome/Edge)\n142\tscripts/build-web.sh --single-file # -> target/web/shardfall.html: one ~10 MB page, runs from file://\n143\tscripts/check-wgsl.sh              # after any WGSL change: Chromium's Tint compiles every module\n144\t```\n145\t`--single-file` packs web/index.html, the JS glue and the gzipped wasm into one page with no\n146\tother loads (`scripts/pack_single_html.py`; `--title --description --theme-color --scene NAME --out PATH`).\n147\tBrowser build: `cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")` code lives in `pav_app` (no threads, async GPU\n148\tsetup); other crates only skip disk access there (the browser has no files) or pick its GPU\n149\tbackend. Check it with `cargo clippy -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`. Headless\n150\tChromium runs it only with the right flags (WebGPU on SwiftShader); those and phone emulation are\n151\tin `docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Browser and phones\".\n152\tDisk: cloud containers have a fixed allowance. Dev builds use line-table debug info and no\n153\tincremental cache; if the disk fills up anyway, delete stale binaries in `target/debug/deps`\n154\t(or run `cargo clean`).\n155\t\n156\t## Agent CLI (`pav`) and MCP\n157\tEvery tool works headless (captures use lavapipe when there is no GPU). The same tools are an\n158\tMCP server: `.mcp.json` registers `pav mcp` (stdio), so Claude Code agents in this repo get\n159\tthem as `mcp__shardfall__*` tools (captures come back as images). `pav help` lists every tool\n160\tand its arguments; `docs/REFERENCE.md` (\"Tools\") shows each family with examples.\n161\t```sh\n162\tcargo run -q -p pav_tools --bin pav -- help\n163\tpav bench ticks=1200                          # ticks/sec\n164\tpav capture scene=test ticks=300 out=out/a.png\n165\tprintf 'step ticks=200\\ncamera preset=top\\ncapture out=out/b.png\\n' | pav repl\n166\tprintf 'input move=[1,0] ticks=30\\ninput press=jump move=[0,1] ticks=40\\nplayer\\n' | pav repl\n167\t```\n168\t- One-shot calls accept `scene=`, `seed=` and `ticks=` to set up the session first. `pav repl`\n169\t  keeps one session across lines (`tool key=value ...` or JSON lines\n170\t  `{\"tool\":\"name\",\"args\":{...}}`; `#` = comment).\n171\t- `input` drives the player: `move=[x,z]` world direction (x = east, z = south), `hold=`/`press=`\n172\t  buttons (jump, crouch, crawl, use, focus, interact, primary), `aim=[x,y,z]`, `ticks=N`.\n173\t- Look at captures with your image-reading tool; prefer small sizes (e.g. `width=640 height=360`).\n174\t  `filmstrip` tiles N frames into one PNG: the cheapest way to check motion and animation.\n175\t- `record_save` + `replay` reproduce a session exactly (same machine/build) and check the hash:\n176\t  use them for bug reports.\n177\t- Live bridge: start the game with `--bridge` (or `bridge = \"127.0.0.1:7878\"` in shardfall.toml),\n178\t  then `pav live` is a REPL into the running game and `pav mcp --live` an MCP server for it. Same\n179\t  tools; they act on what is on screen (captures render the game's camera on a second device).\n180\t- Studios edit on the live bridge, each with its own doc: Animation (`shardfall\n181\t  --animation-studio`, `.mcp.animation-studio.json`, `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`), Object\n182\t  (`--asset-studio`, `.mcp.studio.json`, `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` and `docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md`;\n183\t  materials `docs/MATERIALS.md`) and Creature (`--creature-studio`, `.mcp.studio.json`,\n184\t  `docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md`); `scripts/animation-studio.sh`, `asset-studio.sh` and\n185\t  `creature-studio.sh` build and open each. Pass the last reply's `revision` as `if_revision`,\n186\t  and copy a source clip or asset before changing it.\n187\t- Game data and rooms may name only assets every build carries: embedded (BUILTIN, LIB/core) or a\n188\t  shipped pack's (`props::store::SHIPPED`: the KayKit figures). Game code draws library assets\n189\t  from its own state with `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` (`docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`, \"Library\n190\t  assets in game code\").\n191\t- `tools/creature-compiler` vendors the exact SpawnForge pin: keep the pin and source hashes\n192\t  intact; don't resolve against a moving upstream checkout.\n193\t- Shardfall content: game data lives in `game/*.toml` (`game_reload` re-reads it live). Check a\n194\t  change with the tools: `see` (a screenshot with numbered marks and a legend), `levelmap`,\n195\t  `turntable`, `animsheet`, and `campaign from=1 to=12 wall=300` (the bot plays down through the\n196\t  levels and reports each; run it after data changes).\n197\t\n198\tAsset store (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md`): before making a prop or clip, `assets shelf=prop` (or `shelf=clip`) lists the best entries and `assets find=words` (`kind=clip` for motion) searches; a miss gives `none` and a route.\n199\tIn the Workshop wing, `library_hall` shows every standard object (generated: after publishing to core, rebuild and run `pav assets reindex=store` and `pav assets reindex=hall`), `limits` what the checks catch and miss, `catalogue` pages through every store row, `store_showcase` shows the materials; the animation wing's `clip_browser` plays every clip.\n200\t\n201\tTools: `scenes load step status entities npcs params set camera capture bench gpu player input\n202\tspawn despawn teleport rewind snapshot_save snapshot_load record_save replay rooms room goto\n203\troom_reset room_check room_reload stream signal filmstrip camera_bench course feel audio_capture`;\n204\tlooks `look`; teaching `guide`; games on the hook `play`; Shardfall `game hero monster autoplay skills game_reload\n205\tloot_roll give inventory game_cmd ui tree tree_map genome bestiary boss turntable animsheet level\n206\tlevelmap go goto_feature see campaign theme_swatch`; animation `clips clip_import mocap\n207\tanim_reload anim_edit anim_preview`; objects `assets asset_edit asset_preview asset_spawn\n208\tasset_import studio_status`; creatures `creature_catalog creature_edit creature_preview\n209\tcreature_status`.\n210\t\n211\t### Adding a tool\n212\t1. Write `fn t_name(s: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output>` in the tool family's module\n213\t   (`asset_tools.rs`, `game_tools.rs`, ...); it rejects unknown arguments, naming the nearest.\n214\t2. Add a `Tool { .. }` entry to `TOOLS` in `tools.rs` (help ≤ 50 tokens, each argument ≤ 12\n215\t   words). It is then in the CLI, REPL and MCP.\n216\t3. Put enums and op shapes in `schema()`; a new asset kind is a `KIND_ROUTES` row, not a new tool.\n217\t4. Add actions that change what the live studio shows to `live_feedback::changes_studio`.\n218\t5. Add a clause to the `mcp.rs` instructions if agents should find the tool first.\n219\t6. Test it on `Session::new(\"empty\", 1)`.\n220\t\n221\t### Adding a room (preferred: data only, no rebuild)\n222\tCopy `rooms/_template.toml` to `rooms/<key>.toml` and edit; the template documents every field\n223\t(`rooms/feel_lab.toml` and `crates/pav_core/tests/physics_room.toml` are full examples). The room\n224\tis placed on its wing's corridor automatically. Every room is a station of the world demo and\n225\tteaches: give it a `[learn]` block and a `note` on every pad that changes something\n226\t(`pav_view/tests/learn.rs` checks them; `rooms/bloom.toml` is the model). Check it with\n227\t`pav room_check path=rooms/<key>.toml`; look at it with `pav capture scene=<key>` (the room alone,\n228\tfast) or `printf 'load scene=world\\ngoto room=<key>\\ncapture\\n' | pav repl`. The running game\n229\thot-reloads room files. New *mechanics* are Rust (character.rs / sim.rs behaviours / entity\n230\tfields); keep rooms as data wherever possible.\n231\t\n232\t### Scenes\n233\t`world` (pavilion + rooms + streaming wilderness), `world/<room>` (start in a room),\n234\t`<room key>` (that room alone, no terrain), `test`, `empty`, and Shardfall's `town` (the game\n235\tstarts here by default; the saved hero is loaded into any game scene), `arena`, `lab` (the\n236\tMenagerie of creatures) and `level/<n>` (depth n: 1-12 designed, then the endless Depths).\n237\tGames built on the hook (`pav_core::games::GAMES`) are scenes by their key: `starter` today.\n238\tCode scenes live in `scenes.rs` (Shardfall places in `arpg/scene.rs`).\n239\t\n240\t## Tests\n241\t`cargo test` runs every suite; `cargo test -p <crate> --test <suite>` runs one. Suites live in\n242\t`crates/*/tests/`, named for what they cover (`docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Tests\", describes each).\n243\t`pav_core/tests/gameplay.rs` and `movement.rs` are the cheapest way to catch feel regressions:\n244\textend them when you add movement features. `pav_view/tests/material_parity.rs` needs a GPU (or\n245\tlavapipe); `pav_tools/tests/import_khronos.rs` is opt-in (`-- --ignored`).\n246\t\n247\t## Conventions\n248\t- Rust stable pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`; `Cargo.lock` committed; edition 2024.\n249\t- Finished work gets a dated entry at the top of `docs/HISTORY.md` (what changed, how it works,\n250\t  the decisions); then update `docs/PROGRESS.md`, which stays one page of current state.\n251\t- Decide anything that isn't genuinely the user's call; record the decision with its entry in\n252\t  `docs/HISTORY.md`. Escalate what the doctrine says to escalate, and log it in\n253\t  `docs/ESCALATIONS.md`.\n254\t- Finishing a task or milestone: commit, push, open a PR into `main`, merge it and delete the\n255\t  branch. This is standard procedure (the user's standing instruction, which counts as asking for\n256\t  the PR); don't ask first.\n257\t- The user plays the Windows build; the log file `shardfall.log` and `shardfall.toml` (startup\n258\t  settings, e.g. `backend = \"dx12\"`) sit next to the `.exe`.\n259\t- Keep this file short: under 32 KiB (Codex reads no further; `docs_limits.rs` checks it) and\n260\t  about 250 lines. Detail goes to `docs/REFERENCE.md` or a topic doc, with a pointer here.\n261\t\n262\t## Code Review Rules\n263\tFor reviewers (Codex when it runs, or `/code-review`). Flag a change that:\n264\t- breaks one of the \"Key rules\" under Architecture: a graphics, windowing or audio dependency in\n265\t  `pav_core`, play state outside a `Clone` `SimState`, results that can differ between runs on one\n266\t  machine (unseeded randomness, the clock, `HashMap`/`HashSet` iteration order);\n267\t- commits a binary asset other than a font, or content a licence keeps in the local tiers;\n268\t- makes threads, blocking calls or file access reachable on `wasm32`.\n269\tLeave style, wording and test coverage of routine code alone: this is a one-user prototype\n270\t(\"Working rules\" 5, \"Testing budget\").\n271\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"552e0ef4-8b80-43be-81a9-d767c074aad8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:58.851Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/AGENTS.md","content":"# AGENTS.md — rulebook for coding agents\n\nMaking a new game on the engine? Read `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`: the \"Key rules\" below apply to\nyour game, the maintainers' workflow (HISTORY, PROGRESS, PRs, escalations) doesn't.\n\nShardfall is a procedural hack-and-slash game built on the Pavilion engine, written in Rust. The\nprinciples are in `docs/DOCTRINE.md`, which outranks everything else here. The current state is\n`docs/PROGRESS.md` (one page). Read both before starting; Claude Code loads them, with this file,\nthrough `CLAUDE.md`. The design is in `docs/DESIGN.md` (engine) and `docs/GAME.md` (Shardfall):\nread them when your work touches the design. `docs/REFERENCE.md` holds the full code map, every\ntool family with examples, the controls and what each test suite covers: open the section you\nneed. The journal and past decisions are in `docs/HISTORY.md`, newest first: search it, don't\nread it whole. For a standalone Linux source handoff, `START_HERE.md` covers setup and headless\nCLI examples.\n\n## How the doctrine applies here\nAdopted 2026-10-09, partway through development. Code from before then isn't rewritten to fit;\nfix a mismatch when it gets in the way.\n- **Platform (5, 10):** the development platform is Linux, where agents build and test. The\n  user's Windows `.exe` and the browser build count as part of the target too: a problem the user\n  can see gets fixed now. Replays are promised to match only on the machine that recorded them; to\n  chase something the user saw, start from a snapshot taken just before it.\n- **Renderer (6):** wgpu is the WebGPU implementation: Vulkan on Linux and Windows (DX12 as a\n  Windows option), the browser's own WebGPU on the web, lavapipe where there's no GPU. GPU compute\n  stays cosmetic. The game UI is egui.\n- **API and internals (7, 8):** the game (`pav_core/src/arpg/`) still lives inside the engine\n  crate, so the compiler doesn't enforce the line. The engine modules the game uses are its API:\n  `sim`, `entity`, `frame`, `rng`, `input`, `params`, `statics`, `nav`, `zones`, `character`,\n  `projectile`, `puppet`, `parts`, `moves`, `clips`, `shape`, `color`, `fxdef`, and `games` (the\n  hook a new game implements: `docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`). Everything else\n  (renderer, physics wiring, synth, importers) is internals. If game work means reading\n  internals, fix the API or the error message.\n- **Versions (9):** current pins stay (Rust 1.98.1, wgpu 30, rapier 0.36, egui 0.36, glam 0.33,\n  cpal 0.18). The rule applies to new dependencies and to upgrades.\n- **Assets (4):** no image, model, texture or audio files; fonts are allowed. Animation and\n  objects are readable text: key poses (`anim/*.json`, the format `clips.rs` documents, made with\n  `clip_import`) and props made of named primitive parts (`assets/props`, `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`).\n  Raw downloads (.glb, .gltf, .obj, .fbx, .bvh, .amc) go to `.cache/` (git-ignored); never commit\n  them, or images. Keep each source's credit and licence. Libraries whose licences forbid sharing\n  what is made from them (Bandai Namco, LaFAN1, Mixamo) are translated only into the git-ignored\n  local tiers (`anim/local`, `assets/props/local`).\n- **Escalation:** ask in chat and log it in `docs/ESCALATIONS.md`. If you can schedule a check-in\n  (e.g. `send_later`), set one for 15 minutes and carry on with other work; if not, make the call,\n  log it and continue.\n- **Pavilion Lite** (`pavilion-lite/`) is frozen: its renderer runs on the CPU, not WebGPU (6),\n  so it isn't developed further (`docs/ESCALATIONS.md`).\n\n## Working rules\nUnder the doctrine, in priority order:\n1. **Gameplay first, then robustness.**\n2. **Use tools.** If a tool does a job faster, more accurately or cheaper over time, use or build one.\n3. **It must still run well on a modern PC** (the user's RTX 3060 Ti and 4070 Super). Other\n   optimization and compatibility wait (10).\n4. **Approximations are fine if they feel right.** Feel beats physical accuracy.\n5. **Check selectively.** Verify what often breaks or is expensive to debug; skip routine checks\n   of things that almost never break. \"If it's broken, the user will say so\" is valid.\n6. **Cost over speed.** Prefer the CLI/capture tools over reading lots of code.\n\n## Testing budget (prototype stage)\nEvery engine here is a prototype with one user: spend on finding what clearly helps, not on\nmeasuring exactly how much. Completion comes first: a test decides how something is built and is\nrecorded; it never stops, skips or reverts planned work.\n- **Test only to change a decision.** Before a test, name the choice it decides and its cost in\n  US$ as Claude Code bills it, subagents included. If no choice rides on it, or a wrong choice\n  would cost less than the test, skip it. Afterwards, report what it cost.\n- **Size the test to the gap.** Agent runs (benchmarks, judges, eval agents) start small: 3-5 per\n  arm. A clear gap decides it: 2:1 or better in wins, or 25% or more in cost, model calls or\n  errors.\n- **Near 50/50, make the call.** If the first batch is within 60/40 (or 10%), stop: the options\n  are about equally good, so the choice matters little (Fredkin's paradox). Take the simpler,\n  cheaper or more reversible option, log the call and why, and move on. Between clear and close:\n  at most one more small batch, then decide.\n- **Close calls belong to tool tests.** Checks with no model calls (cargo tests, `pav` checks and\n  captures, scripted counts) cost almost nothing per run and repeat exactly, so they may scale up\n  to settle narrow margins. Even then, don't chase gains under 5%; timing differences under 10%\n  are noise.\n- Looks and feel are the expensive, noisy kind: prefer objective proxies; use agent judges only for\n  large, obvious differences, few of them, several items per call; leave fine visual judgement to\n  the user on a quick comparison page.\n- Explore broadly: test distinct hypotheses, not variations of one. Don't add or keep code without\n  a verified benefit.\n- Count cost end to end, in US$, not one tool's traffic: every model call re-reads the agent's\n  whole context.\n- Assets made through the documented loop (a brief, `check` to zero findings, a 4-view sheet at\n  the game camera, at most two fix rounds, `publish` with a review) need no human review: the user\n  accepted 28 of 28 (2026-10-12). Show the user only edge cases, or complex ones you are unsure of.\n- Per PR (from 2026-10-16):\n  - Run the full checks (tests of the touched crates, clippy, fmt, the wasm check when the app\n    builds the change) once, on the head you merge.\n  - After a rebase or a small fix, run only the tests of what changed. A docs-only PR needs none.\n  - Merge as soon as the checks pass; don't wait for a review (Codex has posted none since #45 on\n    2026-10-12). A review that arrives later: fix its real findings in a follow-up PR.\n  - Nothing deploys: there is no hosted site. After a merge that can change the game, build the\n    single-file HTML and send it to the user (`CLAUDE.md`, \"Builds for playing and testing\").\n\n## Architecture\nCrates (the full map, module by module: `docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Code map\"):\n- `pav_core`: the simulation, with no window, GPU or audio dependencies: `Sim`, entities, physics\n  (rapier3d), the world, rooms and terrain, characters and puppets, moves and clips, AI and nav,\n  props and materials; the game lives in `src/arpg/`.\n- `pav_render`: the wgpu renderer: shadows, bloom and post effects, the filter stack, procedural\n  meshes and materials, offscreen capture to PNG.\n- `pav_view`: sim frame -> render scene: the camera rig, looks and filters, water, `emit_asset`.\n- `pav_audio`: synthesized sound: cpal output, offline .wav rendering.\n- `pav_tools`: the agent layer: the tool registry, the `pav` CLI and REPL, the MCP server, the\n  live bridge client, and the motion and asset importers.\n- `pav_ui`: Shardfall's egui UI (HUD, inventory, passive tree, touch controls), drawn by the\n  window and, headless, by the tools (`ui`, captures).\n- `pav_app`: the game (`shardfall` binary): window, input, sim thread, live bridge server, the\n  pavilion's egui UI; native and wasm32.\n\nData: `anim/` (moves and motion clips), `rooms/` (room files, embedded in the exe and hot-reloaded;\n`_template.toml` documents every field), `game/` (Shardfall's data), `assets/` (props, materials,\nmodel catalogs), `store/` (the asset store's tables).\nData flow: `Sim::step(InputFrame)` (fixed tick, own thread) -> `Sim::frame()` -> `RenderFrame`\n-> `pav_view::ViewBuilder::build` (interpolates prev/curr) -> `pav_render::Scene` -> `Renderer`.\n\nKey rules:\n- `pav_core` must never depend on graphics, windowing or audio crates.\n- Everything that changes during play lives in `SimState` (cloning it = snapshot). Keep it `Clone`.\n- Same inputs and seed, same state (doctrine 5): randomness comes from `rng`, seeded (the sim's\n  `Rng`, or its hash for seed-derived content), never from the clock; don't let\n  `HashMap`/`HashSet` iteration order reach game state (use a `BTreeMap` or sort).\n- Gameplay code reads plain struct fields; expose tunables via `impl Tunable` (see `params.rs`).\n  Tunables are automatically in the tuning panel, the `params`/`set` tools and preset files.\n- Colors in data are sRGB hex (`Color::hex(\"#e8704a\")`); internally linear.\n- Physics precision switch: in `crates/pav_core/Cargo.toml` change `package = \"rapier3d\"` to\n  `\"rapier3d-f64\"`.\n\n## Build, run, test\n```sh\nscripts/setup-linux.sh             # once per machine (apt packages, lavapipe, mingw, wine)\ncargo build                        # everything (Linux)\ncargo test                         # every crate's tests (`-p pav_core` for one crate)\ncargo fmt --all --check            # formatting\ncargo clippy -p pav_core --all-targets -- -D warnings  # lints, for each crate you touched\ncargo run -p pav_app               # the game (needs a display; Xvfb works with lavapipe)\nscripts/build-windows.sh           # -> target/x86_64-pc-windows-gnu/dist/shardfall.exe\nscripts/smoke-windows.sh 25        # run the .exe under Wine+lavapipe, screenshot + log in out/smoke/\nscripts/smoke-linux.sh 10          # same for the native Linux build\nscripts/build-web.sh               # browser build -> target/web/ (serve over HTTP; Chrome/Edge)\nscripts/build-web.sh --single-file # -> target/web/shardfall.html: one ~10 MB page, runs from file://\nscripts/check-wgsl.sh              # after any WGSL change: Chromium's Tint compiles every module\n```\n`--single-file` packs web/index.html, the JS glue and the gzipped wasm into one page with no\nother loads (`scripts/pack_single_html.py`; `--title --description --theme-color --scene NAME --out PATH`).\nBrowser build: `cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")` code lives in `pav_app` (no threads, async GPU\nsetup); other crates only skip disk access there (the browser has no files) or pick its GPU\nbackend. Check it with `cargo clippy -p pav_app --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`. Headless\nChromium runs it only with the right flags (WebGPU on SwiftShader); those and phone emulation are\nin `docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Browser and phones\".\nDisk: cloud containers have a fixed allowance. Dev builds use line-table debug info and no\nincremental cache; if the disk fills up anyway, delete stale binaries in `target/debug/deps`\n(or run `cargo clean`).\n\n## Agent CLI (`pav`) and MCP\nEvery tool works headless (captures use lavapipe when there is no GPU). The same tools are an\nMCP server: `.mcp.json` registers `pav mcp` (stdio), so Claude Code agents in this repo get\nthem as `mcp__shardfall__*` tools (captures come back as images). `pav help` lists every tool\nand its arguments; `docs/REFERENCE.md` (\"Tools\") shows each family with examples.\n```sh\ncargo run -q -p pav_tools --bin pav -- help\npav bench ticks=1200                          # ticks/sec\npav capture scene=test ticks=300 out=out/a.png\nprintf 'step ticks=200\\ncamera preset=top\\ncapture out=out/b.png\\n' | pav repl\nprintf 'input move=[1,0] ticks=30\\ninput press=jump move=[0,1] ticks=40\\nplayer\\n' | pav repl\n```\n- One-shot calls accept `scene=`, `seed=` and `ticks=` to set up the session first. `pav repl`\n  keeps one session across lines (`tool key=value ...` or JSON lines\n  `{\"tool\":\"name\",\"args\":{...}}`; `#` = comment).\n- `input` drives the player: `move=[x,z]` world direction (x = east, z = south), `hold=`/`press=`\n  buttons (jump, crouch, crawl, use, focus, interact, primary), `aim=[x,y,z]`, `ticks=N`.\n- Look at captures with your image-reading tool; prefer small sizes (e.g. `width=640 height=360`).\n  `filmstrip` tiles N frames into one PNG: the cheapest way to check motion and animation.\n- `record_save` + `replay` reproduce a session exactly (same machine/build) and check the hash:\n  use them for bug reports.\n- Live bridge: start the game with `--bridge` (or `bridge = \"127.0.0.1:7878\"` in shardfall.toml),\n  then `pav live` is a REPL into the running game and `pav mcp --live` an MCP server for it. Same\n  tools; they act on what is on screen (captures render the game's camera on a second device).\n- Studios edit on the live bridge, each with its own doc: Animation (`shardfall\n  --animation-studio`, `.mcp.animation-studio.json`, `docs/ANIMATION_STUDIO.md`), Object\n  (`--asset-studio`, `.mcp.studio.json`, `docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md` and `docs/ASSET_STUDIO_LIVE.md`;\n  materials `docs/MATERIALS.md`) and Creature (`--creature-studio`, `.mcp.studio.json`,\n  `docs/CREATURE_STUDIO.md`); `scripts/animation-studio.sh`, `asset-studio.sh` and\n  `creature-studio.sh` build and open each. Pass the last reply's `revision` as `if_revision`,\n  and copy a source clip or asset before changing it.\n- Game data and rooms may name only assets every build carries: embedded (BUILTIN, LIB/core) or a\n  shipped pack's (`props::store::SHIPPED`: the KayKit figures). Game code draws library assets\n  from its own state with `pav_view::assets::emit_asset` (`docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`, \"Library\n  assets in game code\").\n- `tools/creature-compiler` vendors the exact SpawnForge pin: keep the pin and source hashes\n  intact; don't resolve against a moving upstream checkout.\n- Shardfall content: game data lives in `game/*.toml` (`game_reload` re-reads it live). Check a\n  change with the tools: `see` (a screenshot with numbered marks and a legend), `levelmap`,\n  `turntable`, `animsheet`, and `campaign from=1 to=12 wall=300` (the bot plays down through the\n  levels and reports each; run it after data changes).\n\nAsset store (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md`): before making a prop or clip, `assets shelf=prop` (or `shelf=clip`) lists the best entries and `assets find=words` (`kind=clip` for motion) searches; a miss gives `none` and a route.\nIn the Workshop wing, `library_hall` shows every standard object (generated: after publishing to core, rebuild and run `pav assets reindex=store` and `pav assets reindex=hall`), `limits` what the checks catch and miss, `catalogue` pages through every store row, `store_showcase` shows the materials; the animation wing's `clip_browser` plays every clip.\n\nTools: `scenes load step status entities npcs params set camera capture bench gpu player input\nspawn despawn teleport rewind snapshot_save snapshot_load record_save replay rooms room goto\nroom_reset room_check room_reload stream signal filmstrip camera_bench course feel audio_capture`;\nlooks `look`; teaching `guide`; games on the hook `play`; Shardfall `game hero monster autoplay skills game_reload\nloot_roll give inventory game_cmd ui tree tree_map genome bestiary boss turntable animsheet level\nlevelmap go goto_feature see campaign theme_swatch`; animation `clips clip_import mocap\nanim_reload anim_edit anim_preview`; objects `assets asset_edit asset_preview asset_spawn\nasset_import studio_status`; creatures `creature_catalog creature_edit creature_preview\ncreature_status`.\n\n### Adding a tool\n1. Write `fn t_name(s: &mut Session, a: &Args) -> Result<Output>` in the tool family's module\n   (`asset_tools.rs`, `game_tools.rs`, ...); it rejects unknown arguments, naming the nearest.\n2. Add a `Tool { .. }` entry to `TOOLS` in `tools.rs` (help ≤ 50 tokens, each argument ≤ 12\n   words). It is then in the CLI, REPL and MCP.\n3. Put enums and op shapes in `schema()`; a new asset kind is a `KIND_ROUTES` row, not a new tool.\n4. Add actions that change what the live studio shows to `live_feedback::changes_studio`.\n5. Add a clause to the `mcp.rs` instructions if agents should find the tool first.\n6. Test it on `Session::new(\"empty\", 1)`.\n\n### Adding a room (preferred: data only, no rebuild)\nCopy `rooms/_template.toml` to `rooms/<key>.toml` and edit; the template documents every field\n(`rooms/feel_lab.toml` and `crates/pav_core/tests/physics_room.toml` are full examples). The room\nis placed on its wing's corridor automatically. Every room is a station of the world demo and\nteaches: give it a `[learn]` block and a `note` on every pad that changes something\n(`pav_view/tests/learn.rs` checks them; `rooms/bloom.toml` is the model). Check it with\n`pav room_check path=rooms/<key>.toml`; look at it with `pav capture scene=<key>` (the room alone,\nfast) or `printf 'load scene=world\\ngoto room=<key>\\ncapture\\n' | pav repl`. The running game\nhot-reloads room files. New *mechanics* are Rust (character.rs / sim.rs behaviours / entity\nfields); keep rooms as data wherever possible.\n\n### Scenes\n`world` (pavilion + rooms + streaming wilderness), `world/<room>` (start in a room),\n`<room key>` (that room alone, no terrain), `test`, `empty`, and Shardfall's `town` (the game\nstarts here by default; the saved hero is loaded into any game scene), `arena`, `lab` (the\nMenagerie of creatures) and `level/<n>` (depth n: 1-12 designed, then the endless Depths).\nGames built on the hook (`pav_core::games::GAMES`) are scenes by their key: `starter` today.\nCode scenes live in `scenes.rs` (Shardfall places in `arpg/scene.rs`).\n\n## Tests\n`cargo test` runs every suite; `cargo test -p <crate> --test <suite>` runs one. Suites live in\n`crates/*/tests/`, named for what they cover (`docs/REFERENCE.md`, \"Tests\", describes each).\n`pav_core/tests/gameplay.rs` and `movement.rs` are the cheapest way to catch feel regressions:\nextend them when you add movement features. `pav_view/tests/material_parity.rs` needs a GPU (or\nlavapipe); `pav_tools/tests/import_khronos.rs` is opt-in (`-- --ignored`).\n\n## Conventions\n- Rust stable pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml`; `Cargo.lock` committed; edition 2024.\n- Finished work gets a dated entry at the top of `docs/HISTORY.md` (what changed, how it works,\n  the decisions); then update `docs/PROGRESS.md`, which stays one page of current state.\n- Decide anything that isn't genuinely the user's call; record the decision with its entry in\n  `docs/HISTORY.md`. Escalate what the doctrine says to escalate, and log it in\n  `docs/ESCALATIONS.md`.\n- Finishing a task or milestone: commit, push, open a PR into `main`, merge it and delete the\n  branch. This is standard procedure (the user's standing instruction, which counts as asking for\n  the PR); don't ask first.\n- The user plays the Windows build; the log file `shardfall.log` and `shardfall.toml` (startup\n  settings, e.g. `backend = \"dx12\"`) sit next to the `.exe`.\n- Keep this file short: under 32 KiB (Codex reads no further; `docs_limits.rs` checks it) and\n  about 250 lines. Detail goes to `docs/REFERENCE.md` or a topic doc, with a pointer here.\n\n## Code Review Rules\nFor reviewers (Codex when it runs, or `/code-review`). Flag a change that:\n- breaks one of the \"Key rules\" under Architecture: a graphics, windowing or audio dependency in\n  `pav_core`, play state outside a `Clone` `SimState`, results that can differ between runs on one\n  machine (unseeded randomness, the clock, `HashMap`/`HashSet` iteration order);\n- commits a binary asset other than a font, or content a licence keeps in the local tiers;\n- makes threads, blocking calls or file access reachable on `wasm32`.\nLeave style, wording and test coverage of routine code alone: this is a one-user prototype\n(\"Working rules\" 5, \"Testing budget\").\n","numLines":271,"startLine":1,"totalLines":271}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013M49iiJbNu6P3tD9r1m1vc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RbJZU5ftmiGLHvXTeXEJKj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S5-riftlight.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"880a3de9-c987-451a-a1f8-820f88766bfc","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:59.540Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RbJZU5ftmiGLHvXTeXEJKj":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S5-riftlight.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbJZU5ftmiGLHvXTeXEJKj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Hand-off: the asset store's S5 sprite trial in riftlight\n2\t\n3\tStart a Claude Code session in **michaelcrosato/riftlight** and give it everything below the line.\n4\tShardfall's side of S5 is merged (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §11, §13, §15 in\n5\tmichaelcrosato/shardfall): the three briefs and Shardfall's arm, 3D props drawn through the\n6\t`pixel_art` filter. This session builds the sprite side and runs the trial. Its result is recorded\n7\tin Shardfall as \"pending: riftlight session\" until a Shardfall session copies it into\n8\t`docs/HISTORY.md`.\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t**Task: run the sprite trial. Can sprites stored as text work without looking odd, against\n13\tcode-drawn art and against Shardfall's pixel-filtered 3D props, on the same three briefs?**\n14\t\n15\tRead Shardfall's §11 (\"2D\"); fetch only that file:\n16\t`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/main/docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` (pin the\n17\tcommit you read: `git ls-remote https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall main`).\n18\tThe briefs are in `scripts/asset_bench/s5_briefs.toml` at the same commit: P1 a dungeon treasure\n19\tnook, P2 a village well corner, P3 a forest camp, each a 5 x 5 m object scene seen from a high\n20\tcamera, characters left out.\n21\t\n22\tBuild in riftlight (its own conventions, tests and PR flow):\n23\t1. **Sprite rows and a reader.** Palette-indexed pixel rows with a legend pointing at tone slots;\n24\t   per game one pixels-per-metre value, one palette, nearest filtering, integer scale, pivot at the\n25\t   feet. Measure the tokens of a 32x32 sprite this way (o200k); §11 estimated about 424-451.\n26\t   Unknown formats and fields are refused.\n27\t2. **Edit operations, each checked by a render diff:** recolour, mirror, outline, shift, paste,\n28\t   remap palette, integer scale. An agent edits sprites only through these.\n29\t3. **The mixing check** with 5 planted faults: mixed pixel densities side by side, a non-integer\n30\t   scale, bilinear filtering, a clashing palette, and one more you choose. Pass: 5 of 5 caught.\n31\t4. **A harness** whose runs use a blind author definition written with it (a `.claude/agents/`\n32\t   file with `omitClaudeMd: true`), recording each run's model calls and US$ (riftlight's own cost\n33\t   method, or Shardfall's `bench.py cost` approach: transcript usage priced per model).\n34\t5. **Three arms on the three briefs:**\n35\t   - **imported sprites:** Kenney 1-Bit Pack (CC0). This arm waits for the repository owner's own\n36\t     approval comment on riftlight #49. An agent never posts, drafts or links that approval; until\n37\t     it exists, record the arm \"pending user\" and build the rest;\n38\t   - **code-drawn art:** the agent draws each scene's objects in code (riftlight's own drawing);\n39\t   - **Shardfall's arm:** already rendered. The images are on the user's S5 review page\n40\t     (https://claude.ai/artifact/NAqUvr4ZyFVw3yfTmkeekr, private to the user); ask the user for the three PNGs (or a Shardfall session can regenerate them\n41\t     with `scripts/asset_bench/bench.py store-render --gate S5` after `store-prepare --gate S5 --briefs-file\n42\t     scripts/asset_bench/s5_briefs.toml` and the three author runs).\n43\t   Agent edits: 10 edit tasks through the operations; pass when the render diff holds in at least\n44\t   8 of 10.\n45\t6. **A both-orders review page** for the user: per brief, each pair of arms shown left/right and\n46\t   then right/left (sprites against each other arm), verdicts left, right or same. Leave fine\n47\t   visual judgement to the user; no agent judges.\n48\t\n49\t**Success (all four, §11):** sprites win at least 2 of 3 briefs against each other arm in both\n50\torders on the user's page; they need no more model calls than the cheaper other arm; the import\n51\tcheck catches 5 of 5 planted mixing faults; agent edits pass the render diff in at least 8 of 10.\n52\t**Kill:** any one fails. The code merges either way; on a kill, sprites stay out of any store\n53\tdefaults and shelf.\n54\t\n55\t**Test limit:** S5's whole testing budget is $25 and 3 hours (Shardfall spent $0.11 of it on its three author runs).\n56\tState each batch's US$ before it runs; at the limit, stop testing, record the result on the runs\n57\tdone, and keep building.\n58\t\n59\t**Report back** (paste into a Shardfall session): the four criteria with their numbers, the arms'\n60\tmodel calls and US$, whether #49's approval existed, the page link, and the PR link.\n61\t\n62\tRules: write only to riftlight. Don't clone Shardfall; fetch the named files only. Keep each\n63\tsource's licence and credit (Kenney, CC0).\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"beed4d02-94ef-4300-9d7c-d3398e0af3ef","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:21:59.553Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S5-riftlight.md","content":"# Hand-off: the asset store's S5 sprite trial in riftlight\n\nStart a Claude Code session in **michaelcrosato/riftlight** and give it everything below the line.\nShardfall's side of S5 is merged (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §11, §13, §15 in\nmichaelcrosato/shardfall): the three briefs and Shardfall's arm, 3D props drawn through the\n`pixel_art` filter. This session builds the sprite side and runs the trial. Its result is recorded\nin Shardfall as \"pending: riftlight session\" until a Shardfall session copies it into\n`docs/HISTORY.md`.\n\n---\n\n**Task: run the sprite trial. Can sprites stored as text work without looking odd, against\ncode-drawn art and against Shardfall's pixel-filtered 3D props, on the same three briefs?**\n\nRead Shardfall's §11 (\"2D\"); fetch only that file:\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/main/docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` (pin the\ncommit you read: `git ls-remote https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall main`).\nThe briefs are in `scripts/asset_bench/s5_briefs.toml` at the same commit: P1 a dungeon treasure\nnook, P2 a village well corner, P3 a forest camp, each a 5 x 5 m object scene seen from a high\ncamera, characters left out.\n\nBuild in riftlight (its own conventions, tests and PR flow):\n1. **Sprite rows and a reader.** Palette-indexed pixel rows with a legend pointing at tone slots;\n   per game one pixels-per-metre value, one palette, nearest filtering, integer scale, pivot at the\n   feet. Measure the tokens of a 32x32 sprite this way (o200k); §11 estimated about 424-451.\n   Unknown formats and fields are refused.\n2. **Edit operations, each checked by a render diff:** recolour, mirror, outline, shift, paste,\n   remap palette, integer scale. An agent edits sprites only through these.\n3. **The mixing check** with 5 planted faults: mixed pixel densities side by side, a non-integer\n   scale, bilinear filtering, a clashing palette, and one more you choose. Pass: 5 of 5 caught.\n4. **A harness** whose runs use a blind author definition written with it (a `.claude/agents/`\n   file with `omitClaudeMd: true`), recording each run's model calls and US$ (riftlight's own cost\n   method, or Shardfall's `bench.py cost` approach: transcript usage priced per model).\n5. **Three arms on the three briefs:**\n   - **imported sprites:** Kenney 1-Bit Pack (CC0). This arm waits for the repository owner's own\n     approval comment on riftlight #49. An agent never posts, drafts or links that approval; until\n     it exists, record the arm \"pending user\" and build the rest;\n   - **code-drawn art:** the agent draws each scene's objects in code (riftlight's own drawing);\n   - **Shardfall's arm:** already rendered. The images are on the user's S5 review page\n     (https://claude.ai/artifact/NAqUvr4ZyFVw3yfTmkeekr, private to the user); ask the user for the three PNGs (or a Shardfall session can regenerate them\n     with `scripts/asset_bench/bench.py store-render --gate S5` after `store-prepare --gate S5 --briefs-file\n     scripts/asset_bench/s5_briefs.toml` and the three author runs).\n   Agent edits: 10 edit tasks through the operations; pass when the render diff holds in at least\n   8 of 10.\n6. **A both-orders review page** for the user: per brief, each pair of arms shown left/right and\n   then right/left (sprites against each other arm), verdicts left, right or same. Leave fine\n   visual judgement to the user; no agent judges.\n\n**Success (all four, §11):** sprites win at least 2 of 3 briefs against each other arm in both\norders on the user's page; they need no more model calls than the cheaper other arm; the import\ncheck catches 5 of 5 planted mixing faults; agent edits pass the render diff in at least 8 of 10.\n**Kill:** any one fails. The code merges either way; on a kill, sprites stay out of any store\ndefaults and shelf.\n\n**Test limit:** S5's whole testing budget is $25 and 3 hours (Shardfall spent $0.11 of it on its three author runs).\nState each batch's US$ before it runs; at the limit, stop testing, record the result on the runs\ndone, and keep building.\n\n**Report back** (paste into a Shardfall session): the four criteria with their numbers, the arms'\nmodel calls and US$, whether #49's approval existed, the page link, and the PR link.\n\nRules: write only to riftlight. Don't clone Shardfall; fetch the named files only. Keep each\nsource's licence and credit (Kenney, CC0).\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RbJZU5ftmiGLHvXTeXEJKj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9AMVUkNHEspxeTD9W6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QseXgAU7jLPgRGZXakqkU7","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S4-my-3dge.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38449,"cache_read_input_tokens":98985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38449},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"99b6349a-59bc-49d0-842e-215551571bbe","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:01.059Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9AMBNW8UnAw6giG9mj","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QseXgAU7jLPgRGZXakqkU7":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S4-my-3dge.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QseXgAU7jLPgRGZXakqkU7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Hand-off: the asset store's S4 in my-3dge (clips from Shardfall's store rows)\n2\t\n3\tStart a Claude Code session in **michaelcrosato/my-3dge** and give it everything below the line.\n4\tShardfall's side of S4 is merged (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §13, §15 in michaelcrosato/shardfall);\n5\tthis session runs the second engine's side. Its result is recorded in Shardfall as \"pending:\n6\tmy-3dge session\" until a Shardfall session copies it into `docs/HISTORY.md`.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t**Task: read ten CC0 clips from Shardfall's asset store rows and check that my-3dge decodes them\n11\tto the same body points Shardfall does.**\n12\t\n13\tShardfall (public: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall) keeps a store of clips, props and\n14\tmaterials, one row per entry in `store/STORE.tsv`. Your repo's `tools/anim/shardfall.ts` already\n15\treads 8 of Shardfall's clip set files, pinned at Shardfall commit `fa2dab6`.\n16\t\n17\t1. **Move the pin** to Shardfall's newest `main` commit (`git ls-remote\n18\t   https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall main`); every commit since S4's merge carries the\n19\t   fixture. Fetch only the files you need from\n20\t   `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/<commit>/<path>`: `store/STORE.tsv`,\n21\t   `store/fixtures/clip_points.json`, and the set files named in STORE.tsv's `# Clip sets:` line\n22\t   (`anim/mesh2motion.json` is new to you; `anim/quaternius.json` you already read). Pin each by\n23\t   SHA-256 the way your reader pins the others.\n24\t2. **Read the ten rows** the fixture lists (`clips[].id`): six MESH2MOTION clips (new to you) and\n25\t   four QUATERNIUS ones. For each, go id → set file (STORE.tsv's `# Clip sets:` line maps\n26\t   `SET` → `anim/<file>`) → clip. The rows say `clip` and `CC0-1.0`; keep each set's `credit` and\n27\t   `sources[].license` with what you import. Set files are format 1 (Shardfall's `clips.rs`\n28\t   documents it; its `legend` field explains every number): angles are whole degrees, hips are in\n29\t   percent of standing hip height. Your decoder converts degrees; refuse unknown formats and\n30\t   fields as your reader already does.\n31\t3. **Decode and compare.** For each clip and each of the fixture's sample times `t`, decode the\n32\t   key pose at `t` (interpolated between keys as your reader does; looping clips wrap) onto the\n33\t   body the clip was measured on: the set file's `sources.<clip.src>.rest`. That gives the 36\n34\t   body points the fixture names (`points`), in mm, in the rig's frame (forward, right, up).\n35\t   Shardfall's decoder (`crates/pav_tools/src/mocap/readable.rs`, `decode_pose`) is a port of\n36\t   my-3D2dge's `src/mocap/readable.js`, so the numbers should agree closely.\n37\t4. **The rule (fixed when S4 started):** per clip, the mean distance between your points and the\n38\t   fixture's over all samples and points is at most **1 mm**, and the worst at most **5 mm**\n39\t   (`fit_matches` and `tolerance_mm` in the fixture). Report per clip: mean and worst mm, pass or\n40\t   fail; for a failure, the first point and sample that differ most and your best guess why\n41\t   (axis order, sign, degree conversion, interpolation, rest frame).\n42\t5. **Play them.** Load the ten clips into your clip library through the same path as the 8 sets,\n43\t   so they appear wherever your engine lists clips, with their credit lines.\n44\t6. Add a test that holds the comparison (so a later pin move re-checks it), commit, and open a PR\n45\t   in my-3dge following its own conventions.\n46\t\n47\t**Report back** (paste into a Shardfall session, which records it in its `docs/HISTORY.md`): the\n48\tShardfall commit you pinned, the ten clips' mean/worst mm and pass/fail, how many passed, what you\n49\tchanged in the reader, and the PR link.\n50\t\n51\tRules: write only to my-3dge. Don't clone Shardfall; fetch the named files only. Credit: the\n52\tclips are CC0 1.0 (Mesh2Motion's contributors; Quaternius, Universal Animation Library).\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"c8300f45-74ae-420a-bddd-5f08f3f314d2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:22:01.079Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/shardfall/docs/handoffs/S4-my-3dge.md","content":"# Hand-off: the asset store's S4 in my-3dge (clips from Shardfall's store rows)\n\nStart a Claude Code session in **michaelcrosato/my-3dge** and give it everything below the line.\nShardfall's side of S4 is merged (`docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md` §13, §15 in michaelcrosato/shardfall);\nthis session runs the second engine's side. Its result is recorded in Shardfall as \"pending:\nmy-3dge session\" until a Shardfall session copies it into `docs/HISTORY.md`.\n\n---\n\n**Task: read ten CC0 clips from Shardfall's asset store rows and check that my-3dge decodes them\nto the same body points Shardfall does.**\n\nShardfall (public: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall) keeps a store of clips, props and\nmaterials, one row per entry in `store/STORE.tsv`. Your repo's `tools/anim/shardfall.ts` already\nreads 8 of Shardfall's clip set files, pinned at Shardfall commit `fa2dab6`.\n\n1. **Move the pin** to Shardfall's newest `main` commit (`git ls-remote\n   https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall main`); every commit since S4's merge carries the\n   fixture. Fetch only the files you need from\n   `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/<commit>/<path>`: `store/STORE.tsv`,\n   `store/fixtures/clip_points.json`, and the set files named in STORE.tsv's `# Clip sets:` line\n   (`anim/mesh2motion.json` is new to you; `anim/quaternius.json` you already read). Pin each by\n   SHA-256 the way your reader pins the others.\n2. **Read the ten rows** the fixture lists (`clips[].id`): six MESH2MOTION clips (new to you) and\n   four QUATERNIUS ones. For each, go id → set file (STORE.tsv's `# Clip sets:` line maps\n   `SET` → `anim/<file>`) → clip. The rows say `clip` and `CC0-1.0`; keep each set's `credit` and\n   `sources[].license` with what you import. Set files are format 1 (Shardfall's `clips.rs`\n   documents it; its `legend` field explains every number): angles are whole degrees, hips are in\n   percent of standing hip height. Your decoder converts degrees; refuse unknown formats and\n   fields as your reader already does.\n3. **Decode and compare.** For each clip and each of the fixture's sample times `t`, decode the\n   key pose at `t` (interpolated between keys as your reader does; looping clips wrap) onto the\n   body the clip was measured on: the set file's `sources.<clip.src>.rest`. That gives the 36\n   body points the fixture names (`points`), in mm, in the rig's frame (forward, right, up).\n   Shardfall's decoder (`crates/pav_tools/src/mocap/readable.rs`, `decode_pose`) is a port of\n   my-3D2dge's `src/mocap/readable.js`, so the numbers should agree closely.\n4. **The rule (fixed when S4 started):** per clip, the mean distance between your points and the\n   fixture's over all samples and points is at most **1 mm**, and the worst at most **5 mm**\n   (`fit_matches` and `tolerance_mm` in the fixture). Report per clip: mean and worst mm, pass or\n   fail; for a failure, the first point and sample that differ most and your best guess why\n   (axis order, sign, degree conversion, interpolation, rest frame).\n5. **Play them.** Load the ten clips into your clip library through the same path as the 8 sets,\n   so they appear wherever your engine lists clips, with their credit lines.\n6. Add a test that holds the comparison (so a later pin move re-checks it), commit, and open a PR\n   in my-3dge following its own conventions.\n\n**Report back** (paste into a Shardfall session, which records it in its `docs/HISTORY.md`): the\nShardfall commit you pinned, the ten clips' mean/worst mm and pass/fail, how many passed, what you\nchanged in the reader, and the PR link.\n\nRules: write only to my-3dge. Don't clone Shardfall; fetch the named files only. Credit: the\nclips are CC0 1.0 (Mesh2Motion's contributors; Quaternius, Universal Animation Library).\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QseXgAU7jLPgRGZXakqkU7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
