{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9TDUFuGDPW9MVDsHYH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WYWrntKR6v2vJMf9rAH8LA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/ai-hub; sed -n 335,356p $H/README.md; sed -n 510,530p $H/README.md; grep -n \"hub:players\\|hub:couch\\|players\" $H/README.md | head -30; sed -n 60,70p $H/lib/hub/round.js","description":"Read how the hub describes couch co-op and player counts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25999,"cache_read_input_tokens":226060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25999},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"8abf42cc-2180-4cfa-a2f7-52239aba7ee0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:47.385Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9TDDNq78h3yJbUQTZ9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WYWrntKR6v2vJMf9rAH8LA":{"command":"H=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/.scout/ai-hub; sed -n 335,356p $H/README.md; sed -n 510,530p $H/README.md; grep -n \"hub:players\\|hub:couch\\|players\" $H/README.md | head -30; sed -n 60,70p $H/lib/hub/round.js","description":"Read how the hub describes couch co-op and player counts"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WYWrntKR6v2vJMf9rAH8LA","type":"tool_result","content":"  a message with the link in it; it finds the ten-character code), and *Try a\n  session on this computer*, in up to four tabs with the hub's practice games.\n- **Made for game night**: the games built for sessions by hand (Blaze Cup,\n  Merry-Go-Kart 64, Grand Theft Motto III, Arwingdings, Brine Line 64,\n  Urethane, Slick & Skid; `SPOTLIGHT` in `assets/js/friends/together.js`),\n  else the newest shared worlds.\n- **How a session works**, in three steps, and the **ways to win**.\n- **Games to play together**: every game that plays in a session, filed by\n  how it plays — *One world for everyone* (shared world), *Race each other's\n  ghosts* (ghost), *Same start, side by side* (parallel) — and *Couch co-op*,\n  the games that seat several players on one screen by themselves (their\n  `players`). The toolbar narrows them by the party's size (2, 3, 4), the way\n  it plays, a session round's length and a search; each choice shows how\n  many games it leaves. A browser with no WebGPU is told how many of them need\n  it, and those cards say so.\n- **A game's page** (`/friends#/g/<slug>`): how it plays together, its goal,\n  controls, seats and round length, and the ways to start it: *Host with this\n  game* (a session that opens with it, then deals the rest), *Try it on this\n  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\n  *Play on this screen*.\n\n### The Couch — `/couch`\n```\npnpm dev\nhttp://localhost:7417/lib/hub/harness.html?game=/games/mygame.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n```\n\n`node scripts/hub-check.mjs games/mygame.html` runs the automatic conformance\nchecks with Playwright: a parallel game at 1 and 2 players, a ghost game or a\nshared world at 2, 3 and 4 on a bad network (within the seats it declares),\neach with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\nverdict into `data/overrides.json`, where a failing game gets `\"session\": \"0\"`\nand is never dealt. The three examples in `lib/hub/examples/` (**Starfall**,\nparallel; **Comet Dash**, ghost; **Star Arena**, a shared world) are the hub's\nreference games and pass it; the protocol page does not link them, so no agent\ncopies them.\n\n### Bringing the library to sessions\n\nTwo scripts keep thousands of games on the protocol without editing them by\nhand:\n\n```bash\n288:(*4 players* finds every game that seats four). Whatever is filtering the wall\n345:  the games that seat several players on one screen by themselves (their\n346:  `players`). The toolbar narrows them by the party's size (2, 3, 4), the way\n364:model that made three or more, *Originals*, *Couch co-op* (several players on\n404:tag:pixel   type:demo   origin:original   players:2   players:multi\n467:no way for players to message each other; they talk in an app of their own.\n481:- **Ghost**: parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n498:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n512:http://localhost:7417/lib/hub/harness.html?game=/games/mygame.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n516:checks with Playwright: a parallel game at 1 and 2 players, a ghost game or a\n563:  `hub-check --retrofit` judge it: two players with one leaving, then the game\n578:The session itself: players pick a generated name, take one of four seats,\n583:players present can play (it seats them, and every seat's browser can run\n586:filters say; a pick that does not seat the players yet keeps its place until\n635:- Game traffic goes straight between the players' browsers (a WebRTC mesh,\n696:- Peer-to-peer play shows players' IP addresses to each other (`/privacy/`\n750:| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\nexport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n  const typical = Number(minutes);\n  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n}\n\n/**\n * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n * place.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"4af3b2ee-80fe-4519-94c9-8cad93cc944c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:47.412Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  a message with the link in it; it finds the ten-character code), and *Try a\n  session on this computer*, in up to four tabs with the hub's practice games.\n- **Made for game night**: the games built for sessions by hand (Blaze Cup,\n  Merry-Go-Kart 64, Grand Theft Motto III, Arwingdings, Brine Line 64,\n  Urethane, Slick & Skid; `SPOTLIGHT` in `assets/js/friends/together.js`),\n  else the newest shared worlds.\n- **How a session works**, in three steps, and the **ways to win**.\n- **Games to play together**: every game that plays in a session, filed by\n  how it plays — *One world for everyone* (shared world), *Race each other's\n  ghosts* (ghost), *Same start, side by side* (parallel) — and *Couch co-op*,\n  the games that seat several players on one screen by themselves (their\n  `players`). The toolbar narrows them by the party's size (2, 3, 4), the way\n  it plays, a session round's length and a search; each choice shows how\n  many games it leaves. A browser with no WebGPU is told how many of them need\n  it, and those cards say so.\n- **A game's page** (`/friends#/g/<slug>`): how it plays together, its goal,\n  controls, seats and round length, and the ways to start it: *Host with this\n  game* (a session that opens with it, then deals the rest), *Try it on this\n  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\n  *Play on this screen*.\n\n### The Couch — `/couch`\n```\npnpm dev\nhttp://localhost:7417/lib/hub/harness.html?game=/games/mygame.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n```\n\n`node scripts/hub-check.mjs games/mygame.html` runs the automatic conformance\nchecks with Playwright: a parallel game at 1 and 2 players, a ghost game or a\nshared world at 2, 3 and 4 on a bad network (within the seats it declares),\neach with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\nverdict into `data/overrides.json`, where a failing game gets `\"session\": \"0\"`\nand is never dealt. The three examples in `lib/hub/examples/` (**Starfall**,\nparallel; **Comet Dash**, ghost; **Star Arena**, a shared world) are the hub's\nreference games and pass it; the protocol page does not link them, so no agent\ncopies them.\n\n### Bringing the library to sessions\n\nTwo scripts keep thousands of games on the protocol without editing them by\nhand:\n\n```bash\n288:(*4 players* finds every game that seats four). Whatever is filtering the wall\n345:  the games that seat several players on one screen by themselves (their\n346:  `players`). The toolbar narrows them by the party's size (2, 3, 4), the way\n364:model that made three or more, *Originals*, *Couch co-op* (several players on\n404:tag:pixel   type:demo   origin:original   players:2   players:multi\n467:no way for players to message each other; they talk in an app of their own.\n481:- **Ghost**: parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n498:(`1–4 players · Parallel · about 4 min`), and the Catalogue finds them all\n512:http://localhost:7417/lib/hub/harness.html?game=/games/mygame.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n516:checks with Playwright: a parallel game at 1 and 2 players, a ghost game or a\n563:  `hub-check --retrofit` judge it: two players with one leaving, then the game\n578:The session itself: players pick a generated name, take one of four seats,\n583:players present can play (it seats them, and every seat's browser can run\n586:filters say; a pick that does not seat the players yet keeps its place until\n635:- Game traffic goes straight between the players' browsers (a WebRTC mesh,\n696:- Peer-to-peer play shows players' IP addresses to each other (`/privacy/`\n750:| `players` | `1–2`, `1–4`… only when a game has co-op or versus | the Players rail: *Single player*, or *Multiplayer*, which drops a menu of head counts (*4 players* finds every game that seats four). A game with no `players` is single player |\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */\nexport function limitFor(minutes, { maxRoundMs = TIMINGS.maxRoundMs } = {}) {\n  const typical = Number(minutes);\n  if (!(typical > 0)) return maxRoundMs;\n  return Math.min(maxRoundMs, Math.round(typical * 1.5 * 60_000));\n}\n\n/**\n * Parallel and ghost order: finishers by time, then the rest by score,\n * then anyone who reported nothing, tied last. Equal times or scores share a\n * place.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WYWrntKR6v2vJMf9rAH8LA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
