{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CKPaTK6JS3Mte8v4b8yumM","type":"tool_result","content":"pav — Shardfall agent CLI\n\nUsage: pav <tool> [key=value ...] | pav repl [--stop-on-error] | pav live [addr] [--stop-on-error] | pav mcp [scene] | pav mcp --live [addr] | pav help\n\nTools:\n  scenes     List built-in scenes.  \n  load       Start a fresh simulation of a scene.  scene=<string> seed=<integer>\n  step       Advance the simulation N ticks as fast as possible.  ticks=<integer>\n  status     Tick, time, entity/block counts and state hash.  \n  entities   List entities (id, name, position).  name=<string>\n  params     List tunable parameters (sim.*, camera.*, view.*) with values and ranges.  prefix=<string>\n  set        Set a parameter: path=value.  path=<string> value=<string>\n  camera     Apply a camera preset (no args lists them).  preset=<string>\n  capture    Render a screenshot (PNG) with the software/real GPU.  out=<string> width=<integer> height=<integer> stats=<string> ui=<boolean>\n  bench      Measure simulation ticks per second.  ticks=<integer>\n  gpu        Describe the GPU adapter used for captures.  \n  player     Player state: feet position, velocity, grounded, posture, climbing.  \n  input      Drive the player: hold a move direction/buttons for N ticks (press = only on the first tick).  move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> ticks=<integer>\n  spawn      Spawn a prop.  shape=<string> size=<array> pos=<array> color=<string> body=<string> name=<string>\n  despawn    Remove an entity.  id=<integer>\n  teleport   Move an entity (default: the player; for characters pos = feet).  id=<integer> pos=<array>\n  rewind     Go back in time: ticks=N back, or to tick=T. Starts a new timeline.  ticks=<integer> tick=<integer>\n  snapshot_save Save the full state to a file.  path=<string>\n  snapshot_load Load a state file.  path=<string>\n  record_save Save the inputs since the scene started as a replay file (JSON).  path=<string>\n  rooms      List rooms in the world (key, name, wing, bounds, entrance).  \n  room       Info card of a room (default: the one the player is in).  key=<string>\n  guide      The field guide: words the station guides use (term=, search=), or every room's ask-for-it phrases (asks=true).  term=<string> search=<string> asks=<boolean>\n  goto       Teleport the player into a room (room=key), to the plaza (room=hub) or to a position.  room=<string> pos=<array>\n  room_reset Rebuild a room from its definition (default: current room).  key=<string>\n  room_check Validate a room file without loading it. Returns errors with line/column.  path=<string>\n  room_reload Re-read room files from the rooms directory and rebuild changed rooms (hot reload).  \n  stream     Streaming state: active/dormant regions. point=[x,y,z] adds an interest point, clear=true removes them.  point=<array> clear=<boolean>\n  filmstrip  Capture N frames, `every` ticks apart (optionally driving the player), tiled into one PNG.  frames=<integer> every=<integer> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> out=<string>\n  camera_bench Render the current moment from several camera setups, tiled into one PNG.  presets=<string> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> out=<string>\n  npcs       Non-player characters and creatures: body plan, feet, velocity, brain, steps taken, flinch.  name=<string>\n  signal     Send a pad signal (spawners listening for it fire on the next tick), then step 1 tick.  name=<string>\n  course     Course state: current run (timer, gates, hits, falls), last result, best times, checkpoint.  \n  feel       Feel metrics of the player: response ticks, time to top speed, stopping, turnaround, last jump.  \n  audio_capture Run N ticks (optionally driving the player) and render the game's sounds to a .wav file.  ticks=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> out=<string>\n  replay     Rebuild the scene from a replay file, run all its inputs and verify the final state hash.  path=<string>\n  game       Shardfall status: the hero (level, life, gold, skills), monsters by family and rarity, the wave.  \n  hero       Change the hero: play as another character (character=KEY: game/heroes.toml; each keeps their own hero, the stash is shared), level, gold, xp to add, a skill on a bar slot (slot=0..5 skill=key), full heal.  character=<string> level=<integer> gold=<integer> xp=<number> slot=<integer> skill=<string> heal=<boolean>\n  monster    Spawn monsters of a family near the hero (or at pos). Lists families with no arguments.  family=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> count=<integer> pos=<array> aggro=<boolean>\n  play       A games/ game's HUD, outcome and status.  bot=<boolean> ticks=<integer> seeds=<integer>\n  autoplay   Let a bot play for N seconds (fight, skills, potions, dodge telegraphs); reports kills, deaths, damage taken, xp, gold.  seconds=<number> goal=<array>\n  skills     Every skill (hero and monster) with its numbers, from game/skills.toml.  key=<string>\n  game_reload Re-read the game data folder (./game or $PAV_GAME) for live editing; reports errors.  \n  loot_roll  Roll items without playing (item level, rarity, slot, count): full tooltips, or a summary of many rolls (rarity spread, affix frequency, value ranges) to check loot tables.  level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> count=<integer> bonus=<number> seed=<integer>\n  give       Give the hero an item: a unique by key, or a rolled item (level, rarity, slot); optionally wear it at once.  unique=<string> base=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> equip=<boolean>\n  inventory  The hero's worn gear, bag and stash with every item described, gold, and the vendor's wares in town.  brief=<boolean>\n  game_cmd   A menu action as the player does it (in the input frame: replays include it): pickup|equip|unequip|drop|sell|buy|stash|take|sell_all|bar|travel|use|auto_loot|sort|character with id/slot/skill/place/spot/name.  do=<string> id=<integer> slot=<string> skill=<string> place=<string> depth=<integer> spot=<integer> rarity=<integer> name=<string>\n  ui         The game UI as the player sees it: HUD, windows and touch controls as text; image=true draws it over the game.  open=<string> close=<string> device=<string> hover=<array> click=<array> width=<integer> height=<integer> image=<boolean> out=<string>\n  tree_map   Draw the passive tree (and the first Astral rings) to a PNG: sectors coloured, notables/keystones/masteries ringed, skill nodes blue-ringed, the hero's allocation highlighted.  size=<integer> rings=<integer> out=<string>\n  tree       The hero's passive tree: points, what the allocation gives; find nodes (find=fire or find=keystone), take=NAME allocates the shortest path to a node, refund=, respec=true, mastery=NAME option=N.  find=<string> take=<string> refund=<string> respec=<boolean> mastery=<string> option=<integer> astral=<boolean>\n  genome     Grow a creature from a seed (Spore-style genome: body, parts, palette, archetype, skills, name); body=/archetype=/element= fix those; spawn=true puts it in the game.  seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> spawn=<boolean>\n  bestiary   Generate many genomes and summarise the spread (bodies, archetypes, elements, parts, distinct names) with examples: checks the generator's variety.  count=<integer> seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string>\n  boss       List the designed bosses, or spawn one (key=hollow_king) or a generated one (seed=N) near the hero.  key=<string> seed=<integer> level=<integer>\n  turntable  Render a creature alone from several angles into one PNG: seed= (genome, with body/archetype/element), family=, boss=, character=, or the hero; def= lays JSON puppet fields over it. Reports its anatomy.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> def=<object> angles=<integer> size=<integer> out=<string>\n  animsheet  Render a creature (default: the hero) acting, frame by frame, into one PNG: skill= (swing= a combo's later swing), move= (anim/moves.toml) or clip=; def={\"figure\":NAME} draws an imported body.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> skill=<string> swing=<integer> move=<string> hit=<number> side=<number> clip=<string> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> def=<object> frames=<integer> tilt=<number> size=<integer> out=<string>\n  clips      The motion clip library (anim/*.json: animation translated from open libraries, as readable key poses): no args lists the sets; find=WORDS searches names, tags and descriptions; name=SET/Clip shows one clip as readable text with its source and license; set=NAME lists a set; load=FOLDER adds an on-disk library (cmu: every CMU take; 100style: its runs and idle loops; local: your translations that may not be shared). Play one with animsheet clip=.  find=<string> name=<string> set=<string> load=<string> limit=<integer>\n  clip_import Translate an animation library into a clip set (anim/<set>.json: key poses, credits). from= .glb (Rigify/Unreal/Mixamo rigs; sources= ids), .fbx (each stack a clip), .bvh (at=, loop=, way=), set files or a folder. catalog= (anim/catalogs/*.json) tags and credits; with \"$pick\" and no from= it cuts CMU, 100STYLE, Bandai Namco or LaFAN1 moments (the last two to anim/local).  from=<string> catalog=<string> set=<string> sources=<string> rest=<string> rm=<string> title=<string> credit=<string> clips=<string> tol=<number> fps=<number> blade=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> log=<integer> name=<string> units=<number> list=<boolean> out=<string> ledger=<string>\n  asset_import Model libraries (glTF, OBJ) to format-2 props; rigs to figures. No args: libraries. get=lib/pack downloads; from=FILE|DIR|lib/pack translates (list=true: summary); survey= writes a ledger; check=FILE measures.  get=<string> survey=<string> from=<string> list=<boolean> fit=<string> check=<string> compare=<boolean> up=<string> yaw=<number> scale=<number> place=<string> out=<string> limit=<integer>\n  mocap      Open motion-capture databases, translated on demand; no args lists them. find=WORDS searches takes; get=IDS downloads (cmu: all); cut=TAKE fits a moment into a set. survey= measures or translates CMU takes.  find=<string> lib=<string> get=<string> survey=<string> subjects=<string> cut=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> name=<string> set=<string> tags=<string> desc=<string> tol=<number> limit=<integer> out=<string>\n  anim_reload Re-read anim/ from disk: the moves table (moves.toml) and the clip sets. Invalid files keep the old data and report the error.  \n  anim_edit  Create, copy, inspect, and edit readable animation clips. Edits are validated, saved to WORKSHOP (WORKSHOP_LOCAL for local sources) and shown in the live preview; sources and credits are kept. Inspect first, then pass its if_revision. Undo/redo keep 32 changes.  action=<string> name=<string> from=<string> duration=<number> loop=<boolean> time=<number> pose=<object> clip=<object> factor=<number> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean>\n  anim_preview View an animation in an isolated studio with the game's renderer; the game resumes when it closes. clip=SET/Clip or move=NAME. Same-name edits keep the clock and camera. No args: preview state; action=pose: the sampled pose. capture/filmstrip show the studio.  clip=<string> move=<string> playing=<boolean> time=<number> step=<integer> speed=<number> repeat=<boolean> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> side=<number> hit=<number> action=<string> close=<boolean>\n  assets     Find assets by words or likeness; kind=clip|creature|material; shelf=prop|clip.  kind=<string> find=<string> category=<string> tags=<string> tier=<string> similar=<string> limit=<integer> page=<integer> reindex=<string> shelf=<string>\n  asset_edit Create, copy, inspect or edit objects made of named primitive parts. patch: one atomic ops batch, one undo step; pass if_revision. action=schema is the field guide.  kind=<string> action=<string> name=<string> from=<string> template=<string> description=<string> asset=<object> ops=<array> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean> legend=<boolean> bounds=<boolean> resolved=<boolean> topic=<string> format=<integer> dry_run=<boolean> target=<string> all=<boolean> review=<string>\n  asset_preview Show an object on the isolated stage (the world pauses): name selects, fit frames, turntable spins, close returns. views= returns one framed PNG of several sides.  kind=<string> action=<string> name=<string> close=<boolean> playing=<boolean> time=<number> step=<integer> speed=<number> turntable=<boolean> yaw=<number> scale=<number> seed=<integer> params=<object> views=<array> elevation=<number> tile=<integer> figure=<boolean> compare=<string> view=<string>\n  creature_catalog Discover the pinned local SpawnForge generator: templates, body modules, wings, tails, parts, animation and surface parameters (local; never launches Node). Use its named paths in creature_edit patch ops.  kind=<string> module=<string> find=<string> schema=<boolean>\n  creature_edit Create and revise procedural rigged creatures: create (bundled template, blueprint or seeded theme), patch (atomic named-path SpawnForge ops), surface (skin), copy, inspect, replace, undo, redo, rebuild. Pass if_revision from inspect or the last job. Builds are asynchronous: poll creature_status until published or failed before judging a capture; a failed or superseded job keeps the last good stage. The CLI waits.  action=<string> name=<string> template=<string> theme=<string> seed=<integer> constraints=<object> blueprint=<object> from=<string> quality=<string> ops=<array> skin=<object> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean>\n  creature_preview View compiled creatures with the game's renderer (other studios are kept). action=open resumes or opens a stage; select name, play/pause, scrub, step, turntable, fit; action=pose returns joints. Uncompiled sources need creature_edit action=rebuild.  action=<string> name=<string> clip=<string> time=<number> playing=<boolean> speed=<number> looping=<boolean> turntable=<boolean> yaw=<number> scale=<number> step=<integer> close=<boolean>\n  creature_status Read this session's build jobs without waiting: queued, building, ready (saved, unpublished), published (revision, diff, timings, warnings, feedback ticket), failed or superseded. No args lists recent jobs, authored assets and the preview.  job=<integer> name=<string>\n  asset_spawn Place, list, move or remove object instances in the world. Edits to an asset refresh its placed copies.  action=<string> name=<string> id=<integer> pos=<array> yaw=<number> scale=<number> collide=<boolean> room=<string|integer|null> seed=<integer> roles=<object> params=<object>\n  studio_status The active studio, and whether a live edit's frame was drawn (ticket from its feedback). Cheap: no image.  ticket=<integer>\n  level      Shardfall levels: depth= says what a depth is (name, theme, mechanics, boss, monster level; to= a range); no args: the live level (features with positions and state, spots, exit).  depth=<integer> to=<integer> rooms=<boolean>\n  levelmap   Top-down PNG map of a level: the current one, or a fresh one built for depth= (and seed=). Rooms, corridors, every mechanic's pieces, monster packs, the boss, exit and portal.  depth=<integer> seed=<integer> size=<integer> nav=<boolean> out=<string>\n  go         Travel at once: place=town|arena|lab|level (depth= for levels; unlocks the waypoint).  place=<string> depth=<integer>\n  goto_feature Put the hero next to a level feature: kind=shrine|keg|spikes|gate|wind|totem|lava|ice|crumble|well|chest|bubble|exit|portal (n= picks which one).  kind=<string> n=<integer> offset=<array>\n  see        Screenshot with numbered marks on what matters (monsters, hero, townsfolk, loot, spots, level pieces; characters and named objects outside the game) plus a legend: what each number is, its kind, name, rarity, life, distance, world position.  width=<integer> height=<integer> max=<integer> only=<string> out=<string>\n  campaign   Balance pass: the bot plays down through the levels (from= a depth, to= the last) for up to seconds= of game time and reports each finished level: minutes, kills, deaths, damage taken, hero level in/out, gold.  from=<integer> to=<integer> seconds=<number> hero_level=<integer> wall=<number>\n  theme_swatch PNG of every level theme's palette (floor, wall, pillar, accent, light, sky); depths=13-20 adds the blended palettes of those endless depths.  depths=<string> out=<string>\n  look       Looks and filter presets (the Look & Filters menu): name= a whole look, section= with preset= / on= / enabled=, reset=true, compare=0.5 (filters on the right only). bench=all or a list of looks renders this moment in each. No args lists them.  name=<string> section=<string> preset=<string> on=<string> enabled=<boolean> reset=<boolean> compare=<number> bench=<string> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> out=<string>\n\nOne-shot calls accept scene=, seed= and ticks= to set up the session before the tool runs.\nREPLs also accept JSON lines: {\"tool\":\"anim_preview\",\"args\":{\"clip\":\"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\"}}\nUse --stop-on-error with REPL input files to stop before later commands can change data after a failed command.\nFor live animation editing, start shardfall --animation-studio, then use pav mcp --live or pav live.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"d3d1acb9-470b-42a3-a780-ca9bce318a42","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:25:49.129Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"pav — Shardfall agent CLI\n\nUsage: pav <tool> [key=value ...] | pav repl [--stop-on-error] | pav live [addr] [--stop-on-error] | pav mcp [scene] | pav mcp --live [addr] | pav help\n\nTools:\n  scenes     List built-in scenes.  \n  load       Start a fresh simulation of a scene.  scene=<string> seed=<integer>\n  step       Advance the simulation N ticks as fast as possible.  ticks=<integer>\n  status     Tick, time, entity/block counts and state hash.  \n  entities   List entities (id, name, position).  name=<string>\n  params     List tunable parameters (sim.*, camera.*, view.*) with values and ranges.  prefix=<string>\n  set        Set a parameter: path=value.  path=<string> value=<string>\n  camera     Apply a camera preset (no args lists them).  preset=<string>\n  capture    Render a screenshot (PNG) with the software/real GPU.  out=<string> width=<integer> height=<integer> stats=<string> ui=<boolean>\n  bench      Measure simulation ticks per second.  ticks=<integer>\n  gpu        Describe the GPU adapter used for captures.  \n  player     Player state: feet position, velocity, grounded, posture, climbing.  \n  input      Drive the player: hold a move direction/buttons for N ticks (press = only on the first tick).  move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> ticks=<integer>\n  spawn      Spawn a prop.  shape=<string> size=<array> pos=<array> color=<string> body=<string> name=<string>\n  despawn    Remove an entity.  id=<integer>\n  teleport   Move an entity (default: the player; for characters pos = feet).  id=<integer> pos=<array>\n  rewind     Go back in time: ticks=N back, or to tick=T. Starts a new timeline.  ticks=<integer> tick=<integer>\n  snapshot_save Save the full state to a file.  path=<string>\n  snapshot_load Load a state file.  path=<string>\n  record_save Save the inputs since the scene started as a replay file (JSON).  path=<string>\n  rooms      List rooms in the world (key, name, wing, bounds, entrance).  \n  room       Info card of a room (default: the one the player is in).  key=<string>\n  guide      The field guide: words the station guides use (term=, search=), or every room's ask-for-it phrases (asks=true).  term=<string> search=<string> asks=<boolean>\n  goto       Teleport the player into a room (room=key), to the plaza (room=hub) or to a position.  room=<string> pos=<array>\n  room_reset Rebuild a room from its definition (default: current room).  key=<string>\n  room_check Validate a room file without loading it. Returns errors with line/column.  path=<string>\n  room_reload Re-read room files from the rooms directory and rebuild changed rooms (hot reload).  \n  stream     Streaming state: active/dormant regions. point=[x,y,z] adds an interest point, clear=true removes them.  point=<array> clear=<boolean>\n  filmstrip  Capture N frames, `every` ticks apart (optionally driving the player), tiled into one PNG.  frames=<integer> every=<integer> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> out=<string>\n  camera_bench Render the current moment from several camera setups, tiled into one PNG.  presets=<string> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> out=<string>\n  npcs       Non-player characters and creatures: body plan, feet, velocity, brain, steps taken, flinch.  name=<string>\n  signal     Send a pad signal (spawners listening for it fire on the next tick), then step 1 tick.  name=<string>\n  course     Course state: current run (timer, gates, hits, falls), last result, best times, checkpoint.  \n  feel       Feel metrics of the player: response ticks, time to top speed, stopping, turnaround, last jump.  \n  audio_capture Run N ticks (optionally driving the player) and render the game's sounds to a .wav file.  ticks=<integer> move=<array> hold=<string> press=<string> aim=<array> out=<string>\n  replay     Rebuild the scene from a replay file, run all its inputs and verify the final state hash.  path=<string>\n  game       Shardfall status: the hero (level, life, gold, skills), monsters by family and rarity, the wave.  \n  hero       Change the hero: play as another character (character=KEY: game/heroes.toml; each keeps their own hero, the stash is shared), level, gold, xp to add, a skill on a bar slot (slot=0..5 skill=key), full heal.  character=<string> level=<integer> gold=<integer> xp=<number> slot=<integer> skill=<string> heal=<boolean>\n  monster    Spawn monsters of a family near the hero (or at pos). Lists families with no arguments.  family=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> count=<integer> pos=<array> aggro=<boolean>\n  play       A games/ game's HUD, outcome and status.  bot=<boolean> ticks=<integer> seeds=<integer>\n  autoplay   Let a bot play for N seconds (fight, skills, potions, dodge telegraphs); reports kills, deaths, damage taken, xp, gold.  seconds=<number> goal=<array>\n  skills     Every skill (hero and monster) with its numbers, from game/skills.toml.  key=<string>\n  game_reload Re-read the game data folder (./game or $PAV_GAME) for live editing; reports errors.  \n  loot_roll  Roll items without playing (item level, rarity, slot, count): full tooltips, or a summary of many rolls (rarity spread, affix frequency, value ranges) to check loot tables.  level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> count=<integer> bonus=<number> seed=<integer>\n  give       Give the hero an item: a unique by key, or a rolled item (level, rarity, slot); optionally wear it at once.  unique=<string> base=<string> level=<integer> rarity=<string> slot=<string> equip=<boolean>\n  inventory  The hero's worn gear, bag and stash with every item described, gold, and the vendor's wares in town.  brief=<boolean>\n  game_cmd   A menu action as the player does it (in the input frame: replays include it): pickup|equip|unequip|drop|sell|buy|stash|take|sell_all|bar|travel|use|auto_loot|sort|character with id/slot/skill/place/spot/name.  do=<string> id=<integer> slot=<string> skill=<string> place=<string> depth=<integer> spot=<integer> rarity=<integer> name=<string>\n  ui         The game UI as the player sees it: HUD, windows and touch controls as text; image=true draws it over the game.  open=<string> close=<string> device=<string> hover=<array> click=<array> width=<integer> height=<integer> image=<boolean> out=<string>\n  tree_map   Draw the passive tree (and the first Astral rings) to a PNG: sectors coloured, notables/keystones/masteries ringed, skill nodes blue-ringed, the hero's allocation highlighted.  size=<integer> rings=<integer> out=<string>\n  tree       The hero's passive tree: points, what the allocation gives; find nodes (find=fire or find=keystone), take=NAME allocates the shortest path to a node, refund=, respec=true, mastery=NAME option=N.  find=<string> take=<string> refund=<string> respec=<boolean> mastery=<string> option=<integer> astral=<boolean>\n  genome     Grow a creature from a seed (Spore-style genome: body, parts, palette, archetype, skills, name); body=/archetype=/element= fix those; spawn=true puts it in the game.  seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> spawn=<boolean>\n  bestiary   Generate many genomes and summarise the spread (bodies, archetypes, elements, parts, distinct names) with examples: checks the generator's variety.  count=<integer> seed=<integer> level=<integer> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string>\n  boss       List the designed bosses, or spawn one (key=hollow_king) or a generated one (seed=N) near the hero.  key=<string> seed=<integer> level=<integer>\n  turntable  Render a creature alone from several angles into one PNG: seed= (genome, with body/archetype/element), family=, boss=, character=, or the hero; def= lays JSON puppet fields over it. Reports its anatomy.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> body=<string> archetype=<string> element=<string> parts=<string> def=<object> angles=<integer> size=<integer> out=<string>\n  animsheet  Render a creature (default: the hero) acting, frame by frame, into one PNG: skill= (swing= a combo's later swing), move= (anim/moves.toml) or clip=; def={\"figure\":NAME} draws an imported body.  character=<string> seed=<integer> family=<string> boss=<string> skill=<string> swing=<integer> move=<string> hit=<number> side=<number> clip=<string> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> def=<object> frames=<integer> tilt=<number> size=<integer> out=<string>\n  clips      The motion clip library (anim/*.json: animation translated from open libraries, as readable key poses): no args lists the sets; find=WORDS searches names, tags and descriptions; name=SET/Clip shows one clip as readable text with its source and license; set=NAME lists a set; load=FOLDER adds an on-disk library (cmu: every CMU take; 100style: its runs and idle loops; local: your translations that may not be shared). Play one with animsheet clip=.  find=<string> name=<string> set=<string> load=<string> limit=<integer>\n  clip_import Translate an animation library into a clip set (anim/<set>.json: key poses, credits). from= .glb (Rigify/Unreal/Mixamo rigs; sources= ids), .fbx (each stack a clip), .bvh (at=, loop=, way=), set files or a folder. catalog= (anim/catalogs/*.json) tags and credits; with \"$pick\" and no from= it cuts CMU, 100STYLE, Bandai Namco or LaFAN1 moments (the last two to anim/local).  from=<string> catalog=<string> set=<string> sources=<string> rest=<string> rm=<string> title=<string> credit=<string> clips=<string> tol=<number> fps=<number> blade=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> log=<integer> name=<string> units=<number> list=<boolean> out=<string> ledger=<string>\n  asset_import Model libraries (glTF, OBJ) to format-2 props; rigs to figures. No args: libraries. get=lib/pack downloads; from=FILE|DIR|lib/pack translates (list=true: summary); survey= writes a ledger; check=FILE measures.  get=<string> survey=<string> from=<string> list=<boolean> fit=<string> check=<string> compare=<boolean> up=<string> yaw=<number> scale=<number> place=<string> out=<string> limit=<integer>\n  mocap      Open motion-capture databases, translated on demand; no args lists them. find=WORDS searches takes; get=IDS downloads (cmu: all); cut=TAKE fits a moment into a set. survey= measures or translates CMU takes.  find=<string> lib=<string> get=<string> survey=<string> subjects=<string> cut=<string> at=<string> loop=<boolean> min_cycle=<number> way=<string> name=<string> set=<string> tags=<string> desc=<string> tol=<number> limit=<integer> out=<string>\n  anim_reload Re-read anim/ from disk: the moves table (moves.toml) and the clip sets. Invalid files keep the old data and report the error.  \n  anim_edit  Create, copy, inspect, and edit readable animation clips. Edits are validated, saved to WORKSHOP (WORKSHOP_LOCAL for local sources) and shown in the live preview; sources and credits are kept. Inspect first, then pass its if_revision. Undo/redo keep 32 changes.  action=<string> name=<string> from=<string> duration=<number> loop=<boolean> time=<number> pose=<object> clip=<object> factor=<number> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean>\n  anim_preview View an animation in an isolated studio with the game's renderer; the game resumes when it closes. clip=SET/Clip or move=NAME. Same-name edits keep the clock and camera. No args: preview state; action=pose: the sampled pose. capture/filmstrip show the studio.  clip=<string> move=<string> playing=<boolean> time=<number> step=<integer> speed=<number> repeat=<boolean> mirror=<boolean> upper=<boolean> travel=<boolean> side=<number> hit=<number> action=<string> close=<boolean>\n  assets     Find assets by words or likeness; kind=clip|creature|material; shelf=prop|clip.  kind=<string> find=<string> category=<string> tags=<string> tier=<string> similar=<string> limit=<integer> page=<integer> reindex=<string> shelf=<string>\n  asset_edit Create, copy, inspect or edit objects made of named primitive parts. patch: one atomic ops batch, one undo step; pass if_revision. action=schema is the field guide.  kind=<string> action=<string> name=<string> from=<string> template=<string> description=<string> asset=<object> ops=<array> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean> legend=<boolean> bounds=<boolean> resolved=<boolean> topic=<string> format=<integer> dry_run=<boolean> target=<string> all=<boolean> review=<string>\n  asset_preview Show an object on the isolated stage (the world pauses): name selects, fit frames, turntable spins, close returns. views= returns one framed PNG of several sides.  kind=<string> action=<string> name=<string> close=<boolean> playing=<boolean> time=<number> step=<integer> speed=<number> turntable=<boolean> yaw=<number> scale=<number> seed=<integer> params=<object> views=<array> elevation=<number> tile=<integer> figure=<boolean> compare=<string> view=<string>\n  creature_catalog Discover the pinned local SpawnForge generator: templates, body modules, wings, tails, parts, animation and surface parameters (local; never launches Node). Use its named paths in creature_edit patch ops.  kind=<string> module=<string> find=<string> schema=<boolean>\n  creature_edit Create and revise procedural rigged creatures: create (bundled template, blueprint or seeded theme), patch (atomic named-path SpawnForge ops), surface (skin), copy, inspect, replace, undo, redo, rebuild. Pass if_revision from inspect or the last job. Builds are asynchronous: poll creature_status until published or failed before judging a capture; a failed or superseded job keeps the last good stage. The CLI waits.  action=<string> name=<string> template=<string> theme=<string> seed=<integer> constraints=<object> blueprint=<object> from=<string> quality=<string> ops=<array> skin=<object> if_revision=<string> preview=<boolean>\n  creature_preview View compiled creatures with the game's renderer (other studios are kept). action=open resumes or opens a stage; select name, play/pause, scrub, step, turntable, fit; action=pose returns joints. Uncompiled sources need creature_edit action=rebuild.  action=<string> name=<string> clip=<string> time=<number> playing=<boolean> speed=<number> looping=<boolean> turntable=<boolean> yaw=<number> scale=<number> step=<integer> close=<boolean>\n  creature_status Read this session's build jobs without waiting: queued, building, ready (saved, unpublished), published (revision, diff, timings, warnings, feedback ticket), failed or superseded. No args lists recent jobs, authored assets and the preview.  job=<integer> name=<string>\n  asset_spawn Place, list, move or remove object instances in the world. Edits to an asset refresh its placed copies.  action=<string> name=<string> id=<integer> pos=<array> yaw=<number> scale=<number> collide=<boolean> room=<string|integer|null> seed=<integer> roles=<object> params=<object>\n  studio_status The active studio, and whether a live edit's frame was drawn (ticket from its feedback). Cheap: no image.  ticket=<integer>\n  level      Shardfall levels: depth= says what a depth is (name, theme, mechanics, boss, monster level; to= a range); no args: the live level (features with positions and state, spots, exit).  depth=<integer> to=<integer> rooms=<boolean>\n  levelmap   Top-down PNG map of a level: the current one, or a fresh one built for depth= (and seed=). Rooms, corridors, every mechanic's pieces, monster packs, the boss, exit and portal.  depth=<integer> seed=<integer> size=<integer> nav=<boolean> out=<string>\n  go         Travel at once: place=town|arena|lab|level (depth= for levels; unlocks the waypoint).  place=<string> depth=<integer>\n  goto_feature Put the hero next to a level feature: kind=shrine|keg|spikes|gate|wind|totem|lava|ice|crumble|well|chest|bubble|exit|portal (n= picks which one).  kind=<string> n=<integer> offset=<array>\n  see        Screenshot with numbered marks on what matters (monsters, hero, townsfolk, loot, spots, level pieces; characters and named objects outside the game) plus a legend: what each number is, its kind, name, rarity, life, distance, world position.  width=<integer> height=<integer> max=<integer> only=<string> out=<string>\n  campaign   Balance pass: the bot plays down through the levels (from= a depth, to= the last) for up to seconds= of game time and reports each finished level: minutes, kills, deaths, damage taken, hero level in/out, gold.  from=<integer> to=<integer> seconds=<number> hero_level=<integer> wall=<number>\n  theme_swatch PNG of every level theme's palette (floor, wall, pillar, accent, light, sky); depths=13-20 adds the blended palettes of those endless depths.  depths=<string> out=<string>\n  look       Looks and filter presets (the Look & Filters menu): name= a whole look, section= with preset= / on= / enabled=, reset=true, compare=0.5 (filters on the right only). bench=all or a list of looks renders this moment in each. No args lists them.  name=<string> section=<string> preset=<string> on=<string> enabled=<boolean> reset=<boolean> compare=<number> bench=<string> columns=<integer> width=<integer> height=<integer> out=<string>\n\nOne-shot calls accept scene=, seed= and ticks= to set up the session before the tool runs.\nREPLs also accept JSON lines: {\"tool\":\"anim_preview\",\"args\":{\"clip\":\"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\"}}\nUse --stop-on-error with REPL input files to stop before later commands can change data after a failed command.\nFor live animation editing, start shardfall --animation-studio, then use pav mcp --live or pav live.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CKPaTK6JS3Mte8v4b8yumM","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
