{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BdRATzZbRVCmqTTxVxuc8C","type":"tool_result","content":"2 Pixel heroes — A clean, sharp world; the characters and objects are outlined pixel art.\n3 HD-2D — Pixel-art characters and objects in a soft, glowing 3D world with dark corners.\n4 Pixel world, crisp heroes — The environment is pixel art; the characters and objects stay sharp, lit and inked.\n5 Game Boy world — The environment in four Game Boy greens; the characters and objects in full colour with in\n6 Game Boy — Everything in four greens, pixelated and dithered.\n7 16-bit — The whole scene as 16-bit pixel art with a slightly vivid grade.\n8 Cartoon — Cel shading everywhere, bold ink outlines and vivid colour.\n9 Comic noir — A black-and-white world; the characters and objects keep their colour, inked.\n10 Flat paper — Flat colours, thin outlines and a faded grade, like a printed page.\n11 Arcade CRT — Low resolution on a curved tube with scanlines, glow and colour fringes.\n12 Hologram heroes — Characters and objects flicker like holograms: cool, scanlined and fringed. The world stay\n13 Posterized world — The environment in a few flat shades with flat shading; lit characters and objects in full\n14 Oil painting — The whole scene in oil paint: flat strokes, brush streaks, canvas.\n15 Painted world, crisp heroes — A painted backdrop; the characters and objects stay sharp, lit and inked on top of it.\n16 Comic book — Printed dots on the world, inked cel-shaded heroes, punchy colour.\n17 Newspaper — Black dots on cream paper, everything.\n18 Hacker terminal — The game as green characters on a curved, scanlined screen.\n19 Sketchbook — Pencil hatching and contours on paper.\n20 Sketched world, painted heroes — A coloured-pencil world; the characters and objects in oil paint.\n21 Sunbeams — Dusty air, sunlight streaming through the gaps, a soft glow.\n22 Lamplit fog — A foggy night where every lamp glows in the air.\n# Presets for the Look & Filters menu (and the `look` agent tool).\n#\n# [[preset]]  one filter's settings: `section` is pixel, shading, outlines, stylize, palette,\n#             grading, scanlines, grain, screen, glow or air; `set` holds view paths (as in `pav params\n#             prefix=view`, without `view.`) and only paths of that section. A filter preset\n#             never changes which part of the scene the filter is on (the *_on / *_target keys),\n#             so picking \"Chunky\" keeps pixel art on the characters if that is where it was.\n# [[look]]    a whole look: it switches on every section it names a path of (starting from the\n#             defaults) and switches the others off, so the scene's own settings show there.\n#\n# Parts of the scene: \"all\", \"objects\" (characters and objects: anything that moves, fights or\n# can be picked up) and \"environment\" (level geometry, fixed scenery, the sky).\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pixel art\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"Fine\"\nabout = \"3 px blocks, no outline\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 3.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 0.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = false }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"Classic\"\nabout = \"4 px blocks with a dark outline\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 4.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 0.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"Bold\"\nabout = \"5 px blocks with a dark outline\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 5.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 0.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"Chunky\"\nabout = \"6 px blocks with a dark outline\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 6.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 0.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"16-bit\"\nabout = \"4 px blocks, 24 shades per channel\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 4.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 24.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"8-bit\"\nabout = \"6 px blocks, 8 shades per channel\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 6.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 8.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"pixel\"\nname = \"Giant\"\nabout = \"10 px blocks\"\nset = { \"filter.pixel_art\" = 10.0, \"filter.pixel_levels\" = 0.0, \"filter.pixel_outline\" = true }\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shading\n[[preset]]\nsection = \"shading\"\nname = \"As authored\"\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:373:    /// Screen-space global illumination (bounce light + ambient occlusion), 0 = off.\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:400:    pub cutaway: CutawaySettings,\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:446:            cutaway: CutawaySettings::default(),\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:509:        v.float(\"gi\", &mut self.gi, 0.0, 2.0, \"Screen-space global illumination: bounce light and occlusion (0 = off)\");\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:538:        nested(v, \"cutaway\", &mut self.cutaway);\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:1103:        let c = &settings.cutaway;\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:1109:        scene.cutaway = rs::Cutaway {\ncrates/pav_view/src/build.rs:1711:    // Characters are never sliced by the cutaway.\n12:    // Core materials: assets/materials/*.json and pb/*.json, keyed by their name (\"oak_planks\",\n14:    let materials = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../assets/materials\");\n17:        let dir = materials.join(sub);\n28:    let out = std::path::Path::new(&std::env::var(\"OUT_DIR\").unwrap()).join(\"materials.rs\");\n38:    // Object assets, the embedded tier (docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md §9.1): the templates and the\n39:    // core library (assets, meshes, index.tsv), keyed by their path under assets/props, plus the\n44:    let props = std::path::Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"../../assets/props\");\n46:    for folder in [\"templates\", \"lib/core\", \"lib/kaykit_adventurers\"] {","i