{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ZJPkhCodjCmmXvVBn19KZ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"error\":\"unknown look '\\\"Painted' (looks: Pixel heroes, HD-2D, Pixel world, crisp heroes, Game Boy world, Game Boy, 16-bit, Cartoon, Comic noir, Flat paper, Arcade CRT, Hologram heroes, Posterized wo\n{\"height\":540,\"path\":\"out/look15.png\",\"render_ms\":669,\"tick\":360,\"width\":960}\n{\"current\":{\"on\":[],\"settings\":{}},\"did\":[\"reset: every section shows the scene's own settings\"]}\n{\"current\":{\"on\":[{\"preset\":\"Cartoon\",\"section\":\"shading\"},{\"preset\":\"Ink\",\"section\":\"outlines\"},{\"preset\":null,\"section\":\"grading\"}],\"settings\":{\"cel_bands\":2,\"filter.brightness\":1,\"filter.contrast\":\n{\"height\":540,\"path\":\"out/look8.png\",\"render_ms\":260,\"tick\":360,\"width\":960}\n106:keeps that asset's lineage, so publishing it back adds knobs without making it a fork of itself.\n122:publish keep it, a patch cannot set it, and a copy of a format-1 template stays format 1 without one.\n135:`asset_edit action=publish name=x if_revision=R review=\"ok: …\"` puts a workshop asset into LIB/core\n95:`asset = \"LIB/core/x:low\"` with `params = { height = 70 }`. Example:\n100:vegetation) that transform into the rest; `assets shelf=prop` lists them first (LIB/core\n102:(`asset_spawn name=LIB/core/chair:stool`), knob values (`params={\"height\":45}`), a palette for\n105:core asset under its own name (`copy from=LIB/core/table name=table`) is its next revision: it\n118:assets/props/workshop/name.json; a metre template's copy is in metres: send\n126:BUILTIN/name (templates) and LIB/core/name are embedded in every build, the browser's too. A\n132:A pack's PACK.json holds its licence (lib/ takes CC0 and CC-BY, lib/core CC0 only); reindexing a\n135:`asset_edit action=publish name=x if_revision=R review=\"ok: …\"` puts a workshop asset into LIB/core\n137:chars), a category, 2-6 tags, references to BUILTIN or LIB/core only, core or inline materials\n138:(not MAT/workshop/), and at most 400 tokens\n140:dungeon). It writes lib/core/x.json, its index row and a review.tsv line at this revision (an\n161:`weapon = { kind = \"staff\", asset = \"LIB/core/mage_staff\" }` holds the object by its grip socket\n150:use pav_view::assets::{emit_asset, Palette, Placement};\n151-let at = Placement::at(unit.pos).yaw(unit.heading_deg).id(unit.id); // .scale(1.5), .rot(quat)\n152:emit_asset(scene, \"BUILTIN/crate\", at, unit.id % 8, &Palette::new())?; // any name assets lists\n153-```\n154-\n155-It draws what a placed copy draws (parts, glow, lights; not `fx` particles). The seed picks the\n156-variant (0 as authored; keep to a few seeds per asset); the palette colours `$roles`\n157-({\"$wall\":\"#5a6b7c\"}); `id` keeps each unit's outline its own. Unknown names fail with the\n158-nearest one. Units need no physics: the game owns their positions.\n159-\n160-Characters use sockets through their looks and room data: a biped's\n161-`weapon = { kind = \"staff\", asset = \"LIB/core/mage_staff\" }` holds the object by its grip socket\n162-(+y along the weapon; the kind still sets reach and swings), and a room performer with\n163-`seat = \"<object>\"` sits on that object's sit socket (rooms/library_hall.toml). A room object's\n164-`patch = [ops]` places a one-off variant of an embedded asset (rooms/limits.toml).\n# The agent asset store\n\nFoundational assets for games on the engine: objects (props), motion clips and materials, each\nin its own text format, with generated rows saying what it is, where it came from and how far it\nis trusted. Start from an entry instead of from nothing. Design: docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md.\n\n## Find\n\n- `assets find=\"wooden table\"`: object rows `name cat size_cm tier mesh tok tags desc`, best\n  first. Plurals and synonyms match (`store/synonyms.tsv`); filters `category=`, `tags=`\n  (`@sit` is a socket), `tier=standard`, `similar=NAME`.\n- `assets find=walk kind=clip` and `assets find=planks kind=material` search clips and materials.\n- A miss says `none` with the nearest rows and a route (what to make, or where else to look) and\n  is logged to `store/misses.tsv`.\n- `store/STORE.tsv` lists every entry of every kind in one table (generated; search, don't read\n  it whole).\n\n## The shelf\n\n`assets shelf=prop` and `assets shelf=clip`: the best entries of a kind, one call, about 1,500\ntokens; read it before a scene that needs several things. Props lead with the foundations\n(`store/foundations.tsv`): place a variant (`asset_spawn name=LIB/core/table:wide`) before\nmaking one.\n\n## Tiers\n\n| Tier | Where | Means |\n|---|---|---|\n| standard | `LIB/core`, the templates, embedded clip sets, core materials | in every build; rooms and game data may name it |\n| checked | packs on disk (`LIB/<pack>`) | no `check` findings, described, 2-6 tags, within its token cap, ≤ 30% mesh |\n| disk | packs on disk | translated, but not yet checked |\n\nOnly standard entries may be named by game data and rooms. Standard holds CC0 and own work;\nCC-BY (100STYLE) and CMU clips stay `checked`.\n\n## Licences\n\nThe store admits CC0-1.0, CC-BY-3.0 and 4.0 (credit carried) and, for clips, CMU's terms\n(`store/licences.tsv`). Own work is CC0-1.0. Everything else is excluded: no row, no copy.\n`assets/props/local` and `anim/local` hold sources that may not be shared; the store never","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"86a928e8-7dbd-41ea-b0f3-256459f482d4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:46:50.805Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"error\":\"unknown look '\\\"Painted' (looks: Pixel heroes, HD-2D, Pixel world, crisp heroes, Game Boy world, Game Boy, 16-bit, Cartoon, Comic noir, Flat paper, Arcade CRT, Hologram heroes, Posterized wo\n{\"height\":540,\"path\":\"out/look15.png\",\"render_ms\":669,\"tick\":360,\"width\":960}\n{\"current\":{\"on\":[],\"settings\":{}},\"did\":[\"reset: every