{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCBTN5WPD4WxksHdTNr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DVqpYFKVaFSh7LqVghvGvb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work && cat > .scout/tests/edit_plan.py <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, (s.count(old), old[:70])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# §1 banned-word exemption\nrep(\"\"\"Colossus. A test greps for all of these (§13).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Colossus. A test greps for all of these, whole words and case-sensitive (§13). The About & Credits screen\nis exempt where it names the source and the engine.\"\"\")\n\n# §2 sim speed: measured, not guessed\nrep(\"\"\"| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. The sim runs about 4,000 ticks/s, so a 90-minute game is roughly 80 s of bot time |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `campaign`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. `bench`: 500–2,000 ticks/s on busy levels. **`campaign`: 2.4 game minutes in 14 s, about 10× real time** in a dev build, so a bot needs about 9 minutes for a 90-minute chapter |\"\"\")\n\n# §3 coop wording\nrep(\"\"\"smaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read the plan's §3 table when you reach M2, since it\nlists every place that assumes one hero.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"smaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read that document's §3 table when you reach M2: it\nlists every place that assumes one hero (its line numbers are old, so grep).\n\n**Later chapters must be possible by data:** zones, quests, dialogue, monsters, loot, music and attract all live\nin `game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\"\"\")\n\n# §3 fetch list\nrep(\"\"\"Fetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read that\nfolder's `README.md` once (you need all of it).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Fetch `README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read the\n`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\nmachine apply throughout.\"\"\")\n\n# §3 old suites\nrep(\"\"\"dependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"dependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\n\n**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n`feel`, `heroes`) and `crates/pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` name its content. They are your regression net through M2.\nRewrite or delete each as its content goes. You don't need to run the engine's other suites.\"\"\")\n\n# §4 tome skip\nrep(\"\"\"**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, Options skips):\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, stopped from the Journal):\"\"\")\n\n# §5 saving\nrep(\"\"\"- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n  starts fresh and never crashes. Roster of heroes; coffin, Tally and gold... **gold is per hero**, the\n  coffin and the Tally are shared.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n  starts fresh and never crashes. A roster of heroes, each with their own gold and gear; the coffin and\n  the Tally are shared.\"\"\")\n\n# §6 tone unlocks\nrep(\"\"\"ailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\nmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown; tones at L1, L6, L12 for\nthe first rite of each, and rite level + 2, + 6, + 10 otherwise. Swapping is free anywhere but the middle\nof a fight (3 s out of combat).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"ailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\nmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown. A rite's first tone unlocks\nwith it, its second 3 levels later and its third 6 levels later (never past L20). Swapping is free once\nyou've been out of combat for 3 s.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket), `pitch_flask`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket on a `wand`-kind weapon), `pitch_flask`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool:shovel`, already in the store).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool` with `head=shovel`, already in the store).\"\"\")\n\n# §8 boss entrance\nrep(\"\"\"Each has a designed arena, an entrance (`feel.rs`' boss entrance), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Each has a designed arena, an entrance (the engine's boss entrance beat), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\"\"\")\n\n# §9 touch route, attract\nrep(\"\"\"still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Settings work by tap. A pad connecting or a key press restores\n  the normal Title.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Taps reach the focus layer as clicks, so Settings work by tap. A pad\n  connecting or a key press restores the normal Title.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"1. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish; Hob shouts; the coffin opens.\n2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam.\n4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n7. The Bellwether: the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\nIt must show every class, every zone, an elite, a boss, co-op and the menus' look. It never touches saves.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"1. Potter's Field: a hero claws out of the grave. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish, Hob shouts, the coffin opens.\n2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam; the Gear screen as the bot equips it.\n4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n7. The Great Belfry, then the Bellwether: wind, the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\n\nIts job is to show as much of the game as it can. It never touches saves.\"\"\")\n\n# §10 phrase\nrep(\"\"\"candlelight in it. Check with `look bench`, and a Graphics option leaves it on by default.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"candlelight in it. Compare with `look bench`.\"\"\")\n\n# §12 metas\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">   <!-- players on one screen: \"1\" if Co-op on This Screen is cut -->\n```\"\"\")\n# §12 shim\nrep(\"\"\"const hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null });\nif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n  hub.info = info;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"const hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null, waiting: AIHub.active });\nif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n  hub.waiting = false;\n  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n  hub.info = info;\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [info.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Rust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): reads `__hub.info` at boot, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\nbuilt, with no key press),\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Rust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): at boot, holds on a plain \"Connecting\" while `__hub.waiting` is true (the hub answers within 10 s; `info` stays null if there is none, and\nthe game then starts normally). Then it reads `__hub.info`, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\nbuilt, with no key press),\"\"\")\n\n# §13 playthrough\nrep(\"\"\"| `core` playthrough | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. Costs about 2 minutes a run. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `playthrough` (its own group: slow) | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**, with a new `pav` tool: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. About 10× real time, so about 9 minutes a run in a dev build: build `pav` with `--release`, run classes as separate processes, and rerun only after world, quest or balance changes. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|playthrough|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.**\"\"\")\n\n# §16 players\nrep(\"\"\"Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4 (1–4 only if couch or hub play shipped, which it will); controls in one line;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls in one line;\"\"\")\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\nprint('ok', len(s.split()), 'words', len(s), 'chars')\nPY\npython3 .scout/tests/edit_plan.py","description":"Apply review corrections to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7874,"cache_read_input_tokens":451392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7874},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"09f19507-6e6f-4ce3-bfe9-cfe48e3e7101","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:08.905Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCBT6hkwfBt2xaoRYcw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DVqpYFKVaFSh7LqVghvGvb":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work && cat > .scout/tests/edit_plan.py <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, (s.count(old), old[:70])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# §1 banned-word exemption\nrep(\"\"\"Colossus. A test greps for all of these (§13).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Colossus. A test greps for all of these, whole words and case-sensitive (§13). The About & Credits screen\nis exempt where it names the source and the engine.\"\"\")\n\n# §2 sim speed: measured, not guessed\nrep(\"\"\"| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. The sim runs about 4,000 ticks/s, so a 90-minute game is roughly 80 s of bot time |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `campaign`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. `bench`: 500–2,000 ticks/s on busy levels. **`campaign`: 2.4 game minutes in 14 s, about 10× real time** in a dev build, so a bot needs about 9 minutes for a 90-minute chapter |\"\"\")\n\n# §3 coop wording\nrep(\"\"\"smaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read the plan's §3 table when you reach M2, since it\nlists every place that assumes one hero.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"smaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read that document's §3 table when you reach M2: it\nlists every place that assumes one hero (its line numbers are old, so grep).\n\n**Later chapters must be possible by data:** zones, quests, dialogue, monsters, loot, music and attract all live\nin `game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\"\"\")\n\n# §3 fetch list\nrep(\"\"\"Fetch `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read that\nfolder's `README.md` once (you need all of it).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Fetch `README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read the\n`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\nmachine apply throughout.\"\"\")\n\n# §3 old suites\nrep(\"\"\"dependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"dependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\n\n**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n`feel`, `heroes`) and `crates/pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` name its content. They are your regression net through M2.\nRewrite or delete each as its content goes. You don't need to run the engine's other suites.\"\"\")\n\n# §4 tome skip\nrep(\"\"\"**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, Options skips):\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, stopped from the Journal):\"\"\")\n\n# §5 saving\nrep(\"\"\"- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n  starts fresh and never crashes. Roster of heroes; coffin, Tally and gold... **gold is per hero**, the\n  coffin and the Tally are shared.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n  starts fresh and never crashes. A roster of heroes, each with their own gold and gear; the coffin and\n  the Tally are shared.\"\"\")\n\n# §6 tone unlocks\nrep(\"\"\"ailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\nmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown; tones at L1, L6, L12 for\nthe first rite of each, and rite level + 2, + 6, + 10 otherwise. Swapping is free anywhere but the middle\nof a fight (3 s out of combat).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"ailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\nmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown. A rite's first tone unlocks\nwith it, its second 3 levels later and its third 6 levels later (never past L20). Swapping is free once\nyou've been out of combat for 3 s.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket), `pitch_flask`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket on a `wand`-kind weapon), `pitch_flask`.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool:shovel`, already in the store).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool` with `head=shovel`, already in the store).\"\"\")\n\n# §8 boss entrance\nrep(\"\"\"Each has a designed arena, an entrance (`feel.rs`' boss entrance), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Each has a designed arena, an entrance (the engine's boss entrance beat), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\"\"\")\n\n# §9 touch route, attract\nrep(\"\"\"still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Settings work by tap. A pad connecting or a key press restores\n  the normal Title.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Taps reach the focus layer as clicks, so Settings work by tap. A pad\n  connecting or a key press restores the normal Title.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"1. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish; Hob shouts; the coffin opens.\n2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam.\n4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n7. The Bellwether: the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\nIt must show every class, every zone, an elite, a boss, co-op and the menus' look. It never touches saves.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"1. Potter's Field: a hero claws out of the grave. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish, Hob shouts, the coffin opens.\n2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam; the Gear screen as the bot equips it.\n4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n7. The Great Belfry, then the Bellwether: wind, the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\n\nIts job is to show as much of the game as it can. It never touches saves.\"\"\")\n\n# §10 phrase\nrep(\"\"\"candlelight in it. Check with `look bench`, and a Graphics option leaves it on by default.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"candlelight in it. Compare with `look bench`.\"\"\")\n\n# §12 metas\nrep(\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\"\"\",\n\"\"\"<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">   <!-- players on one screen: \"1\" if Co-op on This Screen is cut -->\n```\"\"\")\n# §12 shim\nrep(\"\"\"const hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null });\nif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n  hub.info = info;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"const hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null, waiting: AIHub.active });\nif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n  hub.waiting = false;\n  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n  hub.info = info;\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [info.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\"\"\",\n\"\"\"    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Rust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): reads `__hub.info` at boot, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\nbuilt, with no key press),\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Rust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): at boot, holds on a plain \"Connecting\" while `__hub.waiting` is true (the hub answers within 10 s; `info` stays null if there is none, and\nthe game then starts normally). Then it reads `__hub.info`, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\nbuilt, with no key press),\"\"\")\n\n# §13 playthrough\nrep(\"\"\"| `core` playthrough | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. Costs about 2 minutes a run. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `playthrough` (its own group: slow) | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**, with a new `pav` tool: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. About 10× real time, so about 9 minutes a run in a dev build: build `pav` with `--release`, run classes as separate processes, and rerun only after world, quest or balance changes. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.**\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|playthrough|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.**\"\"\")\n\n# §16 players\nrep(\"\"\"Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4 (1–4 only if couch or hub play shipped, which it will); controls in one line;\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls in one line;\"\"\")\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\nprint('ok', len(s.split()), 'words', len(s), 'chars')\nPY\npython3 .scout/tests/edit_plan.py","description":"Apply review corrections to the plan"}}}
