","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:33.973Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCEZ5hfVZeUSGbeyPfp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01URuBx2BHmqeaMKiGELmTNs":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work && cat > .scout/tests/edit_paths.py <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, re\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\n# Engine-internal paths: make them relative to the dev folder.\ns, n1 = re.subn(r\"`(crates|docs|game|scripts|web|anim|assets|store|rooms)/\", r\"`engine/\\1/\", s)\ns, n2 = re.subn(r\"`(pav_ui|pav_app|pav_view|pav_audio|pav_render|pav_tools)/\", r\"`engine/crates/\\1/\", s)\ns, n3 = re.subn(r\"`AGENTS\\.md`\", \"`engine/AGENTS.md`\", s)\ns, n4 = re.subn(r\"`props/store\\.rs`\", \"`engine/crates/pav_core/src/props/store.rs`\", s)\ns, n5 = re.subn(r\"`pack_single_html\\.py`\", \"`engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py`\", s)\ns, n6 = re.subn(r\"`build-web\\.sh`\", \"`engine/scripts/build-web.sh`\", s)\nprint(n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,n6)\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\nPY\npython3 .scout/tests/edit_paths.py; grep -n \"exit-interview\\|GameTitle\\|claude-opus\\|20261104\\|211941\\|planner-exit\" PLAN.md | head; grep -n '`\\(world\\|arpg\\|mechanics\\|levelgen\\|build\\.rs\\|boot\\.rs\\|save\\.rs\\|settings\\.rs\\|hall\\.rs\\|destruct\\.rs\\|touch\\.rs\\)[^`]*`' PLAN.md | cut -c1-170 | head -30","description":"Make engine paths relative to the dev folder and scan for leaks"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01URuBx2BHmqeaMKiGELmTNs":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01URuBx2BHmqeaMKiGELmTNs","type":"tool_result","content":"61 4 1 1 2 1\n112:guide's \"Limits today\" (text-only HUD, closed sound list, no per-game camera) are things `arpg/`\n115:So you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\n118:Keep the module name `arpg`; internal identifiers don't matter, player-facing text does.\n156:`arpg/world.rs` or `app.rs` whole; grep them.\n162:**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n170:| `arpg/stats.rs`, `combat.rs`, `items.rs`, `loot.rs`, `powers.rs` | Keep, extend (§7) |\n171:| `arpg/skills.rs` | Keep. `Tweak`s become Tones. Add `summon` and `trap` behaviours |\n172:| `arpg/genome.rs`, `brain.rs`, `boss.rs` | Keep. Designed families and bosses first (§8); the genome feeds the Undertoll |\n173:| `arpg/levelgen.rs`, `world.rs`, `world/dress.rs`, `mechanics.rs` | Keep. Add an open-air grammar; re-theme mechanics (§8) |\n174:| `arpg/scene.rs` (`build_town`), `hall.rs` | Rebuild Vespergate. `hall.rs` becomes the class-select stage |\n175:| `arpg/tree.rs`, `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/arpg_tree.rs`, `engine/game/tree.toml` | **Remove.** Vows and the Tally replace the tree |\n176:| `arpg/bot.rs` | Keep and teach everything: quests, classes, ropes. It drives tests and attract |\n177:| New: `arpg/quest.rs`, `arpg/dialogue.rs`, `arpg/net.rs`, `arpg/attract.rs`, `arpg/follower.rs` | §4, §9, §12 |\n179:| `engine/crates/pav_ui/` | Keep `headless.rs` and the `Device` idea. Replace `arpg_ui.rs`, `arpg_items.rs` with the screens of §9. **Remove `touch.rs` controls** |\n196:- **Change the `localStorage` key prefix** in `engine/crates/pav_app/src/save.rs` and `settings.rs` to one unique to\n198:- Replace user-facing engine strings: \"Shardfall crashed\" in `boot.rs`, room and scene lists, control cards.\n340:- **Hits:** keep `arpg`'s hit-stop (30–70 ms by weight), shake, flash, knockback, gibs. Deaths fling\n345:  what stands under them. Use `destruct.rs`, the keg code and physics props. Each floor needs at least\n641:- **Class select:** four pedestals in a crypt, each hero performing a showreel (`hall.rs`). Left and right\n678:### Attract mode (`engine/game/attract.toml`, `arpg/attract.rs`)\n697:  `balance.*`, extending `arpg::Difficulty`, so they're also in `pav params`:\n882:**Put all of this logic in `arpg/net.rs`, pure:** a per-tick `NetInbox` and `NetOutbox`, no IO, so tests run 2–4 full `Sim`s in one process with a `SimNet` of seeded \n928:| **M7** | Multiplayer: `arpg/net.rs`, mirror mode, `SimNet`, `coop` tool, the Vigil, `hub.rs`, server role, Co-op on This Screen | `net` and `hub` pass |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"7ceae7b0-095e-4b0f-9af4-0d0d3803ce47","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:34.020Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"61 4 1 1 2 1\n112:guide's \"Limits today\" (text-only HUD, closed sound list, no per-game camera) are things `arpg/`\n115:So you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\n118:Keep the module name `arpg`; internal identifiers don't matter, player-facing text does.\n156:`arpg/world.rs` or `app.rs` whole; grep them.\n162:**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n170:| `arpg/stats.rs`, `combat.rs`, `items.rs`, `loot.rs`, `powers.rs` | Keep, extend (§7) |\n171:| `arpg/skills.rs` | Keep. `Tweak`s become Tones. Add `summon` and `trap` behaviours |\n172:| `arpg/genome.rs`, `brain.rs`, `boss.rs` | Keep. Designed families and bosses first (§8); the genome feeds the Undertoll |\n173:| `arpg/levelgen.rs`, `world.rs`, `world/dress.rs`, `mechanics.rs` | Keep. Add an open-air grammar; re-theme mechanics (§8) |\n174:| `arpg/scene.rs` (`build_town`), `hall.rs` | Rebuild Vespergate. `hall.rs` becomes the class-select stage |\n175:| `arpg/tree.rs`, `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/arpg_tree.rs`, `engine/game/tree.toml` | **Remove.** Vows and the Tally replace the tree |\n176:| `arpg/bot.rs` | Keep and teach everything: quests, classes, ropes. It drives tests and attract |\n177:| New: `arpg/quest.rs`, `arpg/dialogue.rs`, `arpg/net.rs`, `arpg/attract.rs`, `arpg/follower.rs` | §4, §9, §12 |\n179:| `engine/crates/pav_ui/` | Keep `headless.rs` and the `Device` idea. Replace `arpg_ui.rs`, `arpg_items.rs` with the screens of §9. **Remove `touch.rs` controls** |\n196:- **Change the `localStorage` key prefix** in `engine/crates/pav_app/src/save.rs` and `settings.rs` to one unique to\n198:- Replace user-facing engine strings: \"Shardfall crashed\" in `boot.rs`, room and scene lists, control cards.\n340:- **Hits:** keep `arpg`'s hit-stop (30–70 ms by weight), shake, flash, knockback, gibs. Deaths fling\n345:  what stands under them. Use `destruct.rs`, the keg code and physics props. Each floor needs at least\n641:- **Class select:** four pedestals in a crypt, each hero performing a showreel (`hall.rs`). Left and right\n678:### Attract mode (`engine/game/attract.toml`, `arpg/attract.rs`)\n697:  `balance.*`, extending `arpg::Difficulty`, so they're also in `pav params`:\n882:**Put all of this logic in `arpg/net.rs`, pure:** a per-tick `NetInbox` and `NetOutbox`, no IO, so tests run 2–4 full `Sim`s in one process with a `SimNet` of seeded \n928:| **M7** | Multiplayer: `arpg/net.rs`, mirror mode, `SimNet`, `coop` tool, the Vigil, `hub.rs`, server role, Co-op on This Screen | `net` and `hub` pass |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01URuBx2BHmqeaMKiGELmTNs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCEZNKYv6huzGdK3dTr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012XZfNqXQYsSg8LgRxRa8gi","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","limit":215},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5464,"cache_read_input_tokens":459266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5464},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"d38559b6-f6ae-4a22-9792-93c2614ee41b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:34.977Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCEZ5hfVZeUSGbeyPfp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012XZfNqXQYsSg8LgRxRa8gi":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","limit":215}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012XZfNqXQYsSg8LgRxRa8gi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN: a bell-haunted co-op action RPG\n2\t\n3\tYou will build this game without the person who wrote this plan, so it decides as much as it can.\n4\t\n5\t- **Authority:** TASK.md first, then this plan, then the engine's docs.\n6\t- **Names here are final. Numbers here are starting values:** tune them with bots and the sliders.\n7\t- **Where the plan is silent, decide and keep going.** Don't stop to ask.\n8\t- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder TASK.md names. `engine/` is the engine's clone inside it.\n9\t- **The title** is yours: do TASK.md's title step first. Keep it in one place\n10\t  (`engine/game/about.toml`, `title`) and read it from there on the title screen, in the page's\n11\t  `<title>` and on the About screen. No world text depends on it. The title is a joke on the cover;\n12\t  the world has its own names (§4).\n13\t- **Keep it shippable:** from M1 on, a working single HTML file can be built at any moment.\n14\t\n15\tMap: §1 the game · §2 what was checked · §3 code · §4 story · §5 play · §6 classes · §7 items and\n16\ttown · §8 zones, monsters, bosses · §9 screens · §10 art and animation · §11 audio · §12 multiplayer\n17\t· §13 testing · §14 build order · §15 cut list · §16 finishing · §17 coverage of TASK.md.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## 1. The game\n22\t\n23\t**Pitch.** For nine hundred years a great bell kept the dead of the vale of Aubrenne asleep. Forty\n24\tnights ago it cracked. You are one of the Unshriven: a corpse that got up because neither the Choir\n25\tabove nor the Discord below would have you. Wade through the risen in crowds, drown in loot, build a\n26\thero from six skills and the tones they are struck in, and climb the broken belfry to silence what\n27\thas been tolling all along.\n28\t\n29\t**Genre:** action RPG, hack-and-slash with loot, 1–4 players co-op.\n30\t**Perspective:** a fixed high three-quarter camera in perspective (§10). The player never rotates it.\n31\t\n32\t**Pillars**\n33\t1. **Every press kills something.** Instant response, crowds that burst, hit-stop, flung corpses,\n34\t   collapsing scenery.\n35\t2. **Loot is half the plot.** Showers of it, colour you can read from the sofa, and rules-bending\n36\t   relics that change how a hero plays.\n37\t3. **Six buttons, endless builds.** Six rites, three tones each, three vows. Swap freely, no respec fee.\n38\t4. **Doom with a straight face and a dry joke.** Grand narration, gloating villains, gallows humour\n39\t   in town.\n40\t5. **Sound is the world.** Bells are the setting, the telegraph, the music and the enemy.\n41\t6. **Made for a TV at ten feet.** Big type, one thing focused at a time, no data walls.\n42\t\n43\t**What we take from the source, and what stands in for it.** Mechanics, structure and tone carry\n44\tover. Every name, character, level, tune and picture is ours.\n45\t\n46\t| The source's signature | Our version |\n47\t|---|---|\n48\t| A cosmic war spilling onto a doomed gothic land | The Choir against the Discord, over the vale of Aubrenne |\n49\t| A hero who turns out to be more than either side | The Unshriven, refused by both |\n50\t| An omen that starts it all | A cracked bell, not a falling star |\n51\t| Doom-laden narrator, villains gloating in your head | The narrator, the Prioress in your head, a tax-collecting undead knight |\n52\t| Skills bent by a modifier | Rites and Tones |\n53\t| Life from kills, one slow potion | Blood motes and Sexton's Gin |\n54\t| Colour-coded loot rain, set items, legendary powers | Relics, Regalia, the Reliquary |\n55\t| Elite packs with stacked affixes | Accursed and Damned packs (§8) |\n56\t| Timed randomized dungeon with a progress bar | The Undertoll and its Peal |\n57\t| Post-cap endless levels | The Sexton's Tally |\n58\t| Thief monster that flees with treasure, secret joke level | The Magpie, the Bishop's Geese |\n59\t| Lore read aloud while you fight | Tomes, in gibberish voice with subtitles |\n60\t\n61\t**Originality rule.** This is a new game in the genre, not a recreation. Don't use the source's\n62\tnames, characters, places, story beats, level layouts, music, UI art or look, renamed or not. These\n63\tnever appear in player-facing text or data: Diablo (except the Source line on the About screen and\n64\twhatever riff the title makes), Sanctuary, Tristram, Cain, Deckard, Leah, Adria, Tyrael, Imperius,\n65\tAuriel, Malthael, Belial, Azmodan, Mephisto, Baal, Andariel, Leoric, Maghda, Nephalem, Horadric,\n66\tHoradrim, Kanai, Westmarch, Caldeum, Arreat, Pandemonium, Haedrig, Shen, Myriam, Kormac, Lyndon,\n67\tEirena, Kulle, Greater Rift, Nephalem Rift, Paragon, Torment, Treasure Goblin, Whimsyshire,\n68\tBarbarian, Demon Hunter, Witch Doctor, Wizard, Crusader, Necromancer, \"stay awhile and listen\",\n69\t\"fresh meat\". Shardfall's own content goes too: Shardfall, Emberwatch, Pavilion, Hilda, Odo, Wren,\n70\tBrannoc, Biscuit, Kestrel, Ysolde, Wanderer, Hollow King, Cinder Wyrm, Mother of Swarms, Frostbound\n71\tColossus. A test greps for all of these, whole words and case-sensitive (§13). The About & Credits screen\n72\tis exempt where it names the source and the engine.\n73\t\n74\t---\n75\t\n76\t## 2. What was checked on this computer\n77\t\n78\tThe planner ran these on 2026-11-04 from a fresh clone. Trust them, and re-run M0's versions.\n79\t\n80\t| Check | Result |\n81\t|---|---|\n82\t| `git clone --depth 1` of the engine, `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav` | Works. 3 min 10 s clean with 6 jobs. Toolchain 1.98.1 picked up by itself |\n83\t| `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file ...` | Works. About 2 min. One 11.4 MB page (wasm 28 MB, 8.4 MB gzipped). `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129 matches the lockfile |\n84\t| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `campaign`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. `bench`: 500–2,000 ticks/s on busy levels. **`campaign`: 2.4 game minutes in 14 s, about 10× real time** in a dev build, so a bot needs about 9 minutes for a 90-minute chapter |\n85\t| The page from `file://` in headless Chromium, with **`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`** | Runs and screenshots show the game. Boots in 1.3 s. **Only 2–3 fps at any viewport, and the sim is throttled to about 5 ticks/s** |\n86\t| The same page with TASK.md's flag list (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, no `--use-vulkan=swiftshader`) | **GPU device lost, blank canvas.** Use the flags above; they are also what `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` says |\n87\t| `navigator.getGamepads` stub in the wasm build | gilrs reads it. The stick moves the hero, `buttons[9]` opens the menu, prompts switch to pad |\n88\t| The page with `session.js` pasted first in `<head>`, the metas and the JS shim of §12, in `harness.html` with real wasm copies, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss | **Passes:** 2 players, 4 players, 3 players `scenario=host-leave`, 2 players `scenario=server`, each in under 20 s. Protocol work must live in JS timers, as the shim does, not in the frame loop |\n89\t\n90\tTraps found while checking, each of which cost time:\n91\t- `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` piped to a script **buffers its port line, so\n92\t  `readline()` hangs for ever**. Use `python3 -u -m http.server ...`.\n93\t- `python3 -I` hides Playwright on this machine. Run your own test scripts with plain `python3`.\n94\t- `pav repl` splits lines on spaces. For an argument with spaces send a JSON line:\n95\t  `{\"tool\":\"look\",\"args\":{\"name\":\"Comic noir\"}}`.\n96\t- When stopping processes, match by PID you recorded. A `pgrep -f` pattern also matches your own shell.\n97\t\n98\t**What this means for testing:** the browser is too slow to play in. Play and balance headless with\n99\t`pav` and `cargo test`, where it is faster than real time. Use the browser only to prove screens\n100\tappear, input routes and the hub protocol holds (§13).\n101\t\n102\t---\n103\t\n104\t## 3. Foundation: the code\n105\t\n106\t### The decision: fork Shardfall's game module, in place\n107\t`engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` says to start from the starter game and skip Shardfall's code. That is right for\n108\tother genres. **For this game, don't.** This game is an action RPG, and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/`\n109\talready has what the starter would make you rewrite: actors, stats, damage, ailments, skills as data,\n110\titems, affixes, powers, a monster generator, boss phases, level generation, level mechanics, a town,\n111\tsaving, a capable bot, a game UI, loot beams, telegraphs, floaters and about 25 agent tools. The\n112\tguide's \"Limits today\" (text-only HUD, closed sound list, no per-game camera) are things `arpg/`\n113\talready got past.\n114\t\n115\tSo you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\n116\tyou change anything. **It must still be a new game:** a player who knows Shardfall must not recognise\n117\ta name, monster, level, screen or line. Keep systems, replace all content, and replace the UI layer.\n118\tKeep the module name `arpg`; internal identifiers don't matter, player-facing text does.\n119\t\n120\tStill follow the guide's \"Rules that keep it working\" and AGENTS.md's \"Key rules\": same inputs and\n121\tseed give the same game, all state lives in `SimState`, `pav_core` has no window, GPU or audio code,\n122\tno threads, blocking calls or files on wasm.\n123\t\n124\t`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` is marked \"on hold\": that is about the maintainers' larger design. §12 here is a\n125\tsmaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read that document's §3 table when you reach M2: it\n126\tlists every place that assumes one hero (its line numbers are old, so grep).\n127\t\n128\t**Later chapters must be possible by data:** zones, quests, dialogue, monsters, loot, music and attract all live\n129\tin `engine/game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\n130\t\n131\t### Setup (M0)\n132\t```sh\n133\tgit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine\n134\tcd engine\n135\tgit rev-parse HEAD                                    # goes on the About screen\n136\tCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav\n137\t./target/debug/pav play scene=starter bot=true seeds=3\n138\tCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene town --title \"Probe\" --out ../probe.html\n139\t```\n140\tFetch `README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n141\t`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read the\n142\t`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\n143\tmachine apply throughout.\n144\t\n145\tDev folder layout:\n146\t```\n147\tengine/          the engine and the game: you change it freely\n148\ttools/check.sh   the one test command (§13), with Python helpers beside it\n149\ttools/hub/       the hub's session client and harness\n150\tshots/           captures for what a script can't judge\n151\t```\n152\t\n153\t**Read:** `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`, the \"Key rules\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`, `engine/docs/GAME.md`, `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md`\n154\t\"Tools\" (search it), `engine/rooms/_template.toml` (search it). **Skip:** `engine/docs/HISTORY.md` (300 KB),\n155\t`engine/docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md`, `engine/docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md`, `pavilion-lite/`, `engine/anim/cmu/`. Don't read\n156\t`arpg/world.rs` or `app.rs` whole; grep them.\n157\t\n158\t**Rhythm:** a Rust change rebuilds `pav` in about 2 minutes, so batch edits. Balance and content live\n159\tin `engine/game/*.toml`: `game_reload` re-reads them with no rebuild. Use `pav repl` for sessions. Adding a\n160\tdependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `engine/scripts/build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\n161\t\n162\t**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n163\t`feel`, `heroes`) and `engine/crates/pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` name its content. They are your regression net through M2.\n164\tRewrite or delete each as its content goes. You don't need to run the engine's other suites.\n165\t\n166\t### Code map: what happens to each part\n167\t| Part | Do |\n168\t|---|---|\n169\t| `engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/mod.rs` (`Game`), `cmd.rs` (`GameCmd`, `Place`) | Keep. Refactor one hero into `HeroSlot`s (M2). New `Place`s: Title, Town, Zone floors via `Level(n)`, Undertoll. Every menu action stays a `GameCmd` |\n170\t| `arpg/stats.rs`, `combat.rs`, `items.rs`, `loot.rs`, `powers.rs` | Keep, extend (§7) |\n171\t| `arpg/skills.rs` | Keep. `Tweak`s become Tones. Add `summon` and `trap` behaviours |\n172\t| `arpg/genome.rs`, `brain.rs`, `boss.rs` | Keep. Designed families and bosses first (§8); the genome feeds the Undertoll |\n173\t| `arpg/levelgen.rs`, `world.rs`, `world/dress.rs`, `mechanics.rs` | Keep. Add an open-air grammar; re-theme mechanics (§8) |\n174\t| `arpg/scene.rs` (`build_town`), `hall.rs` | Rebuild Vespergate. `hall.rs` becomes the class-select stage |\n175\t| `arpg/tree.rs`, `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/arpg_tree.rs`, `engine/game/tree.toml` | **Remove.** Vows and the Tally replace the tree |\n176\t| `arpg/bot.rs` | Keep and teach everything: quests, classes, ropes. It drives tests and attract |\n177\t| New: `arpg/quest.rs`, `arpg/dialogue.rs`, `arpg/net.rs`, `arpg/attract.rs`, `arpg/follower.rs` | §4, §9, §12 |\n178\t| `engine/game/*.toml` | Replace all content. New files: `quests`, `dialogue`, `lore`, `gems`, `regalia`, `vows`, `attract`, `about`, `sfx`, `voices`, `music` |\n179\t| `engine/crates/pav_ui/` | Keep `headless.rs` and the `Device` idea. Replace `arpg_ui.rs`, `arpg_items.rs` with the screens of §9. **Remove `touch.rs` controls** |\n180\t| `engine/crates/pav_app/src/ui.rs`, `input.rs`, `uiinput.rs`, `app.rs` | Replace the tech-demo pause menu and stick cursor. Fixed system keys (F1–F12, hold Backspace rewind) work **only with Dev Mode on** and never in a session |\n181\t| `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs`, `looks.toml` | Keep, extend: new effects, the game's look (§10) |\n182\t| `engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs` | Extend: data-driven sounds, music bus, voices (§11) |\n183\t| `engine/web/index.html`, `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` | Paste the session client, add metas and shim (§12); drop the phone-only code and hint |\n184\t\n185\tMore engine traps:\n186\t- **Game data may name only assets every build carries:** `BUILTIN/`, `LIB/core/`,\n187\t  `LIB/kaykit_adventurers/`. `LIB/quaternius_medieval_village/*` and `LIB/kenney_mini_dungeon/*` are\n188\t  on disk only and **would fail in the browser**. To use one, add its pack to the list in\n189\t  `engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs` and to `SHIPPED` in `engine/crates/pav_core/src/props/store.rs` together.\n190\t- New props: `asset_edit` makes them, `asset_edit action=publish ... ` puts them in `LIB/core` (token\n191\t  caps apply; `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`), and a rebuild embeds them. Clips: any `.json` directly in\n192\t  `engine/anim/` is embedded.\n193\t- `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` **refuses wasm-bindgen snippets**, so no `inline_js`. Call page functions with\n194\t  `#[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = ...)]`. Glue can't contain `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`.\n195\t- `build-web.sh --out` is relative to where you ran it from.\n196\t- **Change the `localStorage` key prefix** in `engine/crates/pav_app/src/save.rs` and `settings.rs` to one unique to\n197\t  this game. On the hub's site all games share an origin, so Shardfall's keys would collide.\n198\t- Replace user-facing engine strings: \"Shardfall crashed\" in `boot.rs`, room and scene lists, control cards.\n199\t- Don't spend time shrinking the page or optimizing: TASK.md puts that out of scope.\n200\t\n201\t---\n202\t\n203\t## 4. World and story\n204\t\n205\t**Setting.** The vale of Aubrenne, a rainy, tired gothic country of parish churches and low hills.\n206\tAbove it sits **the Choir**, a host of faceless, perfect beings of light and song, who are cruel in the\n207\tway ledgers are cruel. Below it writhes **the Discord**, the host that wants everything loud and\n208\tnothing kept. Their war was fought to a truce nine centuries ago and sealed under a bell.\n209\t\n210\t**Old Compline** is that bell. Every dusk it tolled, and the dead stayed down. Forty nights ago it\n211\tcracked. Now the dusk toll comes out wrong, and what is buried climbs up.\n212\t\n213\t**The Unshriven** are those who died in the bell's first silence and were refused by both sides. Death\n214\twon't keep you, which is why you respawn and why you are stronger than you should be.\n215\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"9c0ed65f-bec2-4ee3-a789-5298e786fd26","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:34.985Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN: a bell-haunted co-op action RPG\n\nYou will build this game without the person who wrote this plan, so it decides as much as it can.\n\n- **Authority:** TASK.md first, then this plan, then the engine's docs.\n- **Names here are final. Numbers here are starting values:** tune them with bots and the sliders.\n- **Where the plan is silent, decide and keep going.** Don't stop to ask.\n- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder TASK.md names. `engine/` is the engine's clone inside it.\n- **The title** is yours: do TASK.md's title step first. Keep it in one place\n  (`engine/game/about.toml`, `title`) and read it from there on the title screen, in the page's\n  `<title>` and on the About screen. No world text depends on it. The title is a joke on the cover;\n  the world has its own names (§4).\n- **Keep it shippable:** from M1 on, a working single HTML file can be built at any moment.\n\nMap: §1 the game · §2 what was checked · §3 code · §4 story · §5 play · §6 classes · §7 items and\ntown · §8 zones, monsters, bosses · §9 screens · §10 art and animation · §11 audio · §12 multiplayer\n· §13 testing · §14 build order · §15 cut list · §16 finishing · §17 coverage of TASK.md.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n**Pitch.** For nine hundred years a great bell kept the dead of the vale of Aubrenne asleep. Forty\nnights ago it cracked. You are one of the Unshriven: a corpse that got up because neither the Choir\nabove nor the Discord below would have you. Wade through the risen in crowds, drown in loot, build a\nhero from six skills and the tones they are struck in, and climb the broken belfry to silence what\nhas been tolling all along.\n\n**Genre:** action RPG, hack-and-slash with loot, 1–4 players co-op.\n**Perspective:** a fixed high three-quarter camera in perspective (§10). The player never rotates it.\n\n**Pillars**\n1. **Every press kills something.** Instant response, crowds that burst, hit-stop, flung corpses,\n   collapsing scenery.\n2. **Loot is half the plot.** Showers of it, colour you can read from the sofa, and rules-bending\n   relics that change how a hero plays.\n3. **Six buttons, endless builds.** Six rites, three tones each, three vows. Swap freely, no respec fee.\n4. **Doom with a straight face and a dry joke.** Grand narration, gloating villains, gallows humour\n   in town.\n5. **Sound is the world.** Bells are the setting, the telegraph, the music and the enemy.\n6. **Made for a TV at ten feet.** Big type, one thing focused at a time, no data walls.\n\n**What we take from the source, and what stands in for it.** Mechanics, structure and tone carry\nover. Every name, character, level, tune and picture is ours.\n\n| The source's signature | Our version |\n|---|---|\n| A cosmic war spilling onto a doomed gothic land | The Choir against the Discord, over the vale of Aubrenne |\n| A hero who turns out to be more than either side | The Unshriven, refused by both |\n| An omen that starts it all | A cracked bell, not a falling star |\n| Doom-laden narrator, villains gloating in your head | The narrator, the Prioress in your head, a tax-collecting undead knight |\n| Skills bent by a modifier | Rites and Tones |\n| Life from kills, one slow potion | Blood motes and Sexton's Gin |\n| Colour-coded loot rain, set items, legendary powers | Relics, Regalia, the Reliquary |\n| Elite packs with stacked affixes | Accursed and Damned packs (§8) |\n| Timed randomized dungeon with a progress bar | The Undertoll and its Peal |\n| Post-cap endless levels | The Sexton's Tally |\n| Thief monster that flees with treasure, secret joke level | The Magpie, the Bishop's Geese |\n| Lore read aloud while you fight | Tomes, in gibberish voice with subtitles |\n\n**Originality rule.** This is a new game in the genre, not a recreation. Don't use the source's\nnames, characters, places, story beats, level layouts, music, UI art or look, renamed or not. These\nnever appear in player-facing text or data: Diablo (except the Source line on the About screen and\nwhatever riff the title makes), Sanctuary, Tristram, Cain, Deckard, Leah, Adria, Tyrael, Imperius,\nAuriel, Malthael, Belial, Azmodan, Mephisto, Baal, Andariel, Leoric, Maghda, Nephalem, Horadric,\nHoradrim, Kanai, Westmarch, Caldeum, Arreat, Pandemonium, Haedrig, Shen, Myriam, Kormac, Lyndon,\nEirena, Kulle, Greater Rift, Nephalem Rift, Paragon, Torment, Treasure Goblin, Whimsyshire,\nBarbarian, Demon Hunter, Witch Doctor, Wizard, Crusader, Necromancer, \"stay awhile and listen\",\n\"fresh meat\". Shardfall's own content goes too: Shardfall, Emberwatch, Pavilion, Hilda, Odo, Wren,\nBrannoc, Biscuit, Kestrel, Ysolde, Wanderer, Hollow King, Cinder Wyrm, Mother of Swarms, Frostbound\nColossus. A test greps for all of these, whole words and case-sensitive (§13). The About & Credits screen\nis exempt where it names the source and the engine.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What was checked on this computer\n\nThe planner ran these on 2026-11-04 from a fresh clone. Trust them, and re-run M0's versions.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `git clone --depth 1` of the engine, `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav` | Works. 3 min 10 s clean with 6 jobs. Toolchain 1.98.1 picked up by itself |\n| `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file ...` | Works. About 2 min. One 11.4 MB page (wasm 28 MB, 8.4 MB gzipped). `wasm-bindgen` 0.2.129 matches the lockfile |\n| `pav` headless: `capture`, `autoplay`, `see`, `look bench`, `campaign`, `play` | Work. A 960×540 capture takes 0.3–1 s on the CPU. `bench`: 500–2,000 ticks/s on busy levels. **`campaign`: 2.4 game minutes in 14 s, about 10× real time** in a dev build, so a bot needs about 9 minutes for a 90-minute chapter |\n| The page from `file://` in headless Chromium, with **`--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`** | Runs and screenshots show the game. Boots in 1.3 s. **Only 2–3 fps at any viewport, and the sim is throttled to about 5 ticks/s** |\n| The same page with TASK.md's flag list (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, no `--use-vulkan=swiftshader`) | **GPU device lost, blank canvas.** Use the flags above; they are also what `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md` says |\n| `navigator.getGamepads` stub in the wasm build | gilrs reads it. The stick moves the hero, `buttons[9]` opens the menu, prompts switch to pad |\n| The page with `session.js` pasted first in `<head>`, the metas and the JS shim of §12, in `harness.html` with real wasm copies, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss | **Passes:** 2 players, 4 players, 3 players `scenario=host-leave`, 2 players `scenario=server`, each in under 20 s. Protocol work must live in JS timers, as the shim does, not in the frame loop |\n\nTraps found while checking, each of which cost time:\n- `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` piped to a script **buffers its port line, so\n  `readline()` hangs for ever**. Use `python3 -u -m http.server ...`.\n- `python3 -I` hides Playwright on this machine. Run your own test scripts with plain `python3`.\n- `pav repl` splits lines on spaces. For an argument with spaces send a JSON line:\n  `{\"tool\":\"look\",\"args\":{\"name\":\"Comic noir\"}}`.\n- When stopping processes, match by PID you recorded. A `pgrep -f` pattern also matches your own shell.\n\n**What this means for testing:** the browser is too slow to play in. Play and balance headless with\n`pav` and `cargo test`, where it is faster than real time. Use the browser only to prove screens\nappear, input routes and the hub protocol holds (§13).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Foundation: the code\n\n### The decision: fork Shardfall's game module, in place\n`engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md` says to start from the starter game and skip Shardfall's code. That is right for\nother genres. **For this game, don't.** This game is an action RPG, and `engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/`\nalready has what the starter would make you rewrite: actors, stats, damage, ailments, skills as data,\nitems, affixes, powers, a monster generator, boss phases, level generation, level mechanics, a town,\nsaving, a capable bot, a game UI, loot beams, telegraphs, floaters and about 25 agent tools. The\nguide's \"Limits today\" (text-only HUD, closed sound list, no per-game camera) are things `arpg/`\nalready got past.\n\nSo you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\nyou change anything. **It must still be a new game:** a player who knows Shardfall must not recognise\na name, monster, level, screen or line. Keep systems, replace all content, and replace the UI layer.\nKeep the module name `arpg`; internal identifiers don't matter, player-facing text does.\n\nStill follow the guide's \"Rules that keep it working\" and AGENTS.md's \"Key rules\": same inputs and\nseed give the same game, all state lives in `SimState`, `pav_core` has no window, GPU or audio code,\nno threads, blocking calls or files on wasm.\n\n`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` is marked \"on hold\": that is about the maintainers' larger design. §12 here is a\nsmaller design over the hub, and you do build it. Read that document's §3 table when you reach M2: it\nlists every place that assumes one hero (its line numbers are old, so grep).\n\n**Later chapters must be possible by data:** zones, quests, dialogue, monsters, loot, music and attract all live\nin `engine/game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\n\n### Setup (M0)\n```sh\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall.git engine\ncd engine\ngit rev-parse HEAD                                    # goes on the About screen\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav\n./target/debug/pav play scene=starter bot=true seeds=3\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8 scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene town --title \"Probe\" --out ../probe.html\n```\nFetch `README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from\n`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/` into `tools/hub/`, and read the\n`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\nmachine apply throughout.\n\nDev folder layout:\n```\nengine/          the engine and the game: you change it freely\ntools/check.sh   the one test command (§13), with Python helpers beside it\ntools/hub/       the hub's session client and harness\nshots/           captures for what a script can't judge\n```\n\n**Read:** `engine/docs/MAKE_A_GAME.md`, the \"Key rules\" in `engine/AGENTS.md`, `engine/docs/GAME.md`, `engine/docs/REFERENCE.md`\n\"Tools\" (search it), `engine/rooms/_template.toml` (search it). **Skip:** `engine/docs/HISTORY.md` (300 KB),\n`engine/docs/ASSET_SYSTEM_PLAN.md`, `engine/docs/AGENT_ASSET_STORE.md`, `pavilion-lite/`, `engine/anim/cmu/`. Don't read\n`arpg/world.rs` or `app.rs` whole; grep them.\n\n**Rhythm:** a Rust change rebuilds `pav` in about 2 minutes, so batch edits. Balance and content live\nin `engine/game/*.toml`: `game_reload` re-reads them with no rebuild. Use `pav repl` for sessions. Adding a\ndependency means one `cargo build` without `--locked`, because `engine/scripts/build-web.sh` uses `--locked`.\n\n**Old tests:** Shardfall's suites in `engine/crates/pav_core/tests/` (`arpg`, `loot`, `skills`, `monsters`, `levels`, `town`,\n`feel`, `heroes`) and `engine/crates/pav_tools/tests/game_ui.rs` name its content. They are your regression net through M2.\nRewrite or delete each as its content goes. You don't need to run the engine's other suites.\n\n### Code map: what happens to each part\n| Part | Do |\n|---|---|\n| `engine/crates/pav_core/src/arpg/mod.rs` (`Game`), `cmd.rs` (`GameCmd`, `Place`) | Keep. Refactor one hero into `HeroSlot`s (M2). New `Place`s: Title, Town, Zone floors via `Level(n)`, Undertoll. Every menu action stays a `GameCmd` |\n| `arpg/stats.rs`, `combat.rs`, `items.rs`, `loot.rs`, `powers.rs` | Keep, extend (§7) |\n| `arpg/skills.rs` | Keep. `Tweak`s become Tones. Add `summon` and `trap` behaviours |\n| `arpg/genome.rs`, `brain.rs`, `boss.rs` | Keep. Designed families and bosses first (§8); the genome feeds the Undertoll |\n| `arpg/levelgen.rs`, `world.rs`, `world/dress.rs`, `mechanics.rs` | Keep. Add an open-air grammar; re-theme mechanics (§8) |\n| `arpg/scene.rs` (`build_town`), `hall.rs` | Rebuild Vespergate. `hall.rs` becomes the class-select stage |\n| `arpg/tree.rs`, `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/arpg_tree.rs`, `engine/game/tree.toml` | **Remove.** Vows and the Tally replace the tree |\n| `arpg/bot.rs` | Keep and teach everything: quests, classes, ropes. It drives tests and attract |\n| New: `arpg/quest.rs`, `arpg/dialogue.rs`, `arpg/net.rs`, `arpg/attract.rs`, `arpg/follower.rs` | §4, §9, §12 |\n| `engine/game/*.toml` | Replace all content. New files: `quests`, `dialogue`, `lore`, `gems`, `regalia`, `vows`, `attract`, `about`, `sfx`, `voices`, `music` |\n| `engine/crates/pav_ui/` | Keep `headless.rs` and the `Device` idea. Replace `arpg_ui.rs`, `arpg_items.rs` with the screens of §9. **Remove `touch.rs` controls** |\n| `engine/crates/pav_app/src/ui.rs`, `input.rs`, `uiinput.rs`, `app.rs` | Replace the tech-demo pause menu and stick cursor. Fixed system keys (F1–F12, hold Backspace rewind) work **only with Dev Mode on** and never in a session |\n| `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs`, `looks.toml` | Keep, extend: new effects, the game's look (§10) |\n| `engine/crates/pav_audio/src/lib.rs` | Extend: data-driven sounds, music bus, voices (§11) |\n| `engine/web/index.html`, `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` | Paste the session client, add metas and shim (§12); drop the phone-only code and hint |\n\nMore engine traps:\n- **Game data may name only assets every build carries:** `BUILTIN/`, `LIB/core/`,\n  `LIB/kaykit_adventurers/`. `LIB/quaternius_medieval_village/*` and `LIB/kenney_mini_dungeon/*` are\n  on disk only and **would fail in the browser**. To use one, add its pack to the list in\n  `engine/crates/pav_core/build.rs` and to `SHIPPED` in `engine/crates/pav_core/src/props/store.rs` together.\n- New props: `asset_edit` makes them, `asset_edit action=publish ... ` puts them in `LIB/core` (token\n  caps apply; `engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md`), and a rebuild embeds them. Clips: any `.json` directly in\n  `engine/anim/` is embedded.\n- `engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` **refuses wasm-bindgen snippets**, so no `inline_js`. Call page functions with\n  `#[wasm_bindgen(js_namespace = ...)]`. Glue can't contain `<script`, `</script` or `<!--`.\n- `build-web.sh --out` is relative to where you ran it from.\n- **Change the `localStorage` key prefix** in `engine/crates/pav_app/src/save.rs` and `settings.rs` to one unique to\n  this game. On the hub's site all games share an origin, so Shardfall's keys would collide.\n- Replace user-facing engine strings: \"Shardfall crashed\" in `boot.rs`, room and scene lists, control cards.\n- Don't spend time shrinking the page or optimizing: TASK.md puts that out of scope.\n\n---\n\n## 4. World and story\n\n**Setting.** The vale of Aubrenne, a rainy, tired gothic country of parish churches and low hills.\nAbove it sits **the Choir**, a host of faceless, perfect beings of light and song, who are cruel in the\nway ledgers are cruel. Below it writhes **the Discord**, the host that wants everything loud and\nnothing kept. Their war was fought to a truce nine centuries ago and sealed under a bell.\n\n**Old Compline** is that bell. Every dusk it tolled, and the dead stayed down. Forty nights ago it\ncracked. Now the dusk toll comes out wrong, and what is buried climbs up.\n\n**The Unshriven** are those who died in the bell's first silence and were refused by both sides. Death\nwon't keep you, which is why you respawn and why you are stronger than you should be.\n","numLines":215,"startLine":1,"totalLines":997}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012XZfNqXQYsSg8LgRxRa8gi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
