{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCGU3tbpnUDcXyTUuP1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MdL3rPhVP5ZA12nzuDZA6v","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","offset":215,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11317,"cache_read_input_tokens":464730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11317},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"bf1fb85e-70d8-42c0-af04-79153d3ca01b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:41.222Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCGTmXTmVL1kYV7Jc9D","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MdL3rPhVP5ZA12nzuDZA6v":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","offset":215,"limit":400}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdL3rPhVP5ZA12nzuDZA6v","type":"tool_result","content":"215\t\n216\t**The truth (revealed in Q9).** The toll never laid the dead to rest. It herded them. Under the bell\n217\tlies **the Bellwether**, once the Choir's shepherd of souls, which for nine hundred years has been\n218\tgathering its flock down through the ground. The Tacet cracked the bell on purpose, to stop the\n219\therding, and in doing so let the shepherd wake.\n220\t\n221\t### Cast\n222\t| Who | Role | Voice and manner |\n223\t|---|---|---|\n224\t| **The Narrator** | Title crawl, chapter beats | Slow, deep, sure of the worst |\n225\t| **Sexton Mabry Thole** | Old gravedigger, quest-giver, keeps your Tally and the difficulty roll | Gruff, tender about corpses, knows everything because he buried it. Digs one grave throughout the game: deeper at every visit. It is his own |\n226\t| **Sister Aveline Pell** | One-armed bell-ringer, runs Tuning and the Reliquary | Young, furious, exact |\n227\t| **Hob Cullender** | Bell-founder turned smith, deaf from the bells | SHOUTS EVERYTHING |\n228\t| **Madam Ottoline Quire** | Chandler and jeweller | Dry, gossiping, expensive |\n229\t| **Goody Farthing** | Sells sealed boxes (gamble) | Cheerfully sinister |\n230\t| **Lisbet Marl** | Poacher, follower | Curt, unimpressed, good shot |\n231\t| **Brother Anselm** | Drunk healer, follower | Merry, ashamed, sings badly |\n232\t| **Ser Gaudry Vane, the Tithe Knight** | Boss 1 | Undead tax collector. Pompous, punctilious |\n233\t| **Prioress Amarante** | Boss 2, leader of the Tacet, speaks in your head | Tongueless, patient, nearly right |\n234\t| **The Bellwether** | Final boss | Speaks in tolls; subtitles in capitals |\n235\t| **The Tacet** | The cult | Cut out their tongues and wear iron mouth-bars. Never make a sound; their silence is the threat |\n236\t\n237\t**Your coffin** is the stash: Mabry had it brought to town. \"It's yours. You've used it.\"\n238\t\n239\t### Chapter One: The Silence (about 90 minutes first time)\n240\t| # | Quest | Where | Beats |\n241\t|---|---|---|---|\n242\t| Q1 | **Get Up** | Potter's Field | Crawl: the Narrator over the night churchyard. You claw out of a grave (press to rise, `MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`). Mabry greets you. Learn move, attack, rite, motes, breakable graves |\n243\t| Q2 | **The Lych Road** | Potter's Field → Vespergate | Reach the lych-gate. **Set piece:** hold the gate for 90 s beside the town's last watchmen, kegs and all |\n244\t| Q3 | **Last Rites** | Vespergate | Meet Hob, Ottoline, your coffin, the Lychstone. Mabry wants the Parish Roll from St. Orrin's |\n245\t| Q4 | **Arrears** | The Lych Road, then Undercroft 1–3 | First elites, first gargoyle ambush, first relic (guaranteed from Gaudry). Kill **Ser Gaudry**, take the Roll |\n246\t| Q5 | **Names That Don't Match** | Town → Sallow Fens | Mabry reads the Roll: hundreds of graves were empty long before the crack. The Tacet's camps are in the Fens |\n247\t| Q6 | **The Hush** | Sallow Fens 1–2 | Rescue Lisbet (first follower). Break three Tacet rites: each is an event where effigies ward the enemy. The Prioress first speaks in your head |\n248\t| Q7 | **The Drowned Chapel** (optional) | Fens side dungeon | Darkness, wells to light, Tome, sure relic |\n249\t| Q8 | **Founder's Debt** | Bellfoundry 1–2 | Hob wants his molds back; Aveline wants a new clapper cast. Kill **Prioress Amarante** |\n250\t| Q9 | **What the Bell Was Saying** | Cutscene, then town | Beaten, she shows you the truth; the Bellwether hauls her down. In town Mabry admits he too is Unshriven, the first, two hundred years digging. \"Who did you think buries the gravediggers?\" |\n251\t| Q10 | **The Great Belfry** | Belfry 1–3, Bell Pit | Climb in wind and lightning, Aveline at your side. Kill **the Bellwether**. The bell falls |\n252\t| End | **Compline** | Cutscene | The dead truly lie down. Mabry climbs into the grave he has been digging, and sleeps. Then the sky opens: the Choir's heralds, come to collect. Credits. The Undertoll unlocks |\n253\t\n254\t**Side events** (random placement, each with a one-line hook and a reward):\n255\t- *The Hanged Men:* three corpses drop from a gibbet and fight.\n256\t- *The Widow's Dowry:* a cursed reliquary calls waves, then pays.\n257\t- *The Weeping Saint:* break five urns round a statue for a long buff.\n258\t- *Lost Choirboy:* escort him to the Lychstone. He sings, badly, and draws attacks.\n259\t- *Magpie!:* see §8.\n260\t- *A Tithe of Geese:* opens the secret level. Find four hand-bells, one per zone, and ring them at\n261\t  Vespergate's broken pump.\n262\t\n263\t**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, stopped from the Journal): The\n264\tSexton's Ledger I–IV, Hymnal of the Tacet, Confession of Ser Gaudry, Founder's Notes, A Letter Never Sent.\n265\t\n266\t### Writing style\n267\tGrand and doom-laden when the world speaks, dry and human when people do. Short sentences. Villains\n268\tenjoy themselves. Nobody explains a joke. Every line is shown as a subtitle and spoken in gibberish\n269\t(§11). Write all of it yourself in this voice, and write plenty: barks for every NPC, 4–6 per villain\n270\tper phase, a line for every shop action. These set the tone:\n271\t\n272\t- **Narrator:** \"For nine hundred years, when dusk fell on the vale of Aubrenne, the great bell Old\n273\t  Compline spoke, and the dead lay still. Forty nights ago it cracked. Now it speaks only to them.\"\n274\t- **Mabry, first line:** \"Easy. Easy. You're the fourth this week, and the first to look sorry about\n275\t  it. Mind the headstone. I carved that one.\"\n276\t- **Mabry, on your death:** \"Back of the queue, friend.\"\n277\t- **Hob:** \"WHAT'S THAT? A SWORD? SPEAK UP, IT'S ALL BELLS IN HERE.\"\n278\t- **Ottoline:** \"Candles are for the living, dear. Gems are for the dead. I'm told you're undecided.\"\n279\t- **Aveline:** \"I have one arm and the only ear left in this vale that can hear a bell lie.\"\n280\t- **Goody Farthing:** \"Never ask what's in the box. Ask what's in you, that you want it so badly.\"\n281\t- **Gaudry:** \"Nine hundred years of tithes, and not one soul in arrears. Until you.\" / \"Your account,\n282\t  Unshriven, is overdrawn.\" / dying: \"Mark it... paid.\"\n283\t- **Prioress, in your head:** \"Little corpse. Do you hear how quiet it is between the tolls? That is\n284\t  the only honest thing left in this world.\" / \"We cut out our tongues so we would never sing for it.\n285\t  What have you given?\"\n286\t- **Bellwether:** \"COME IN FROM THE COLD.\" / \"EVERY FLOCK COMES HOME.\" / \"I HAVE COUNTED YOU. YOU ARE\n287\t  ONE SHORT.\"\n288\t- **Choir herald, last line of the chapter:** \"We have come for what was entrusted. You will kneel, or\n289\t  you will be catalogued.\"\n290\t\n291\t**How it's delivered:** quest log (`engine/game/quests.toml`, steps: `reach`, `kill`, `talk`, `use`, `clear`,\n292\t`hold`, `collect`), conversations (`engine/game/dialogue.toml`, one speaker at a time with a topic list),\n293\tvillain lines as a portrait slide-in at the side while you keep fighting, and four in-engine cutscenes\n294\t(letterbox, scripted camera and puppets, skippable with a held button): Rising, Gaudry's entrance,\n295\tPrioress's truth, Compline.\n296\t\n297\t---\n298\t\n299\t## 5. Play\n300\t\n301\t### Controls\n302\t| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyphs in brackets) | Keyboard and mouse |\n303\t|---|---|---|\n304\t| Move | Left stick | Hold left mouse on the ground (walks there by pathfinding), or WASD |\n305\t| Aim | Auto-target; right stick overrides while held | Mouse |\n306\t| Rite 1 (builder) | Cross (A) | Left mouse on an enemy (walks into reach, repeats while held); Shift + left mouse attacks in place |\n307\t| Rite 2 | Square (X) | Right mouse |\n308\t| Rite 3 · 4 | Triangle (Y) · Circle (B) | 1 · 2 |\n309\t| Rite 5 · 6 | R1 (RB) · R2 (RT) | 3 · 4 |\n310\t| Dodge roll | L1 (LB) | Space |\n311\t| Sexton's Gin | L2 (LT) | Q |\n312\t| Talk, use, pick up | Cross when a prompt shows and no enemy is within 3 m | E, or left mouse on the thing |\n313\t| Ring hand-bell (way home) | D-pad down, hold 1 s | T |\n314\t| Hero screen | D-pad up | I or C (Gear), K (Rites), J (Journal) |\n315\t| Map | D-pad left | M or Tab |\n316\t| Item labels | D-pad right toggles | Hold Alt |\n317\t| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc |\n318\t\n319\t**In menus, on every device:** D-pad or left stick moves focus, Cross/A/Enter confirms, Circle/B/Esc\n320\tbacks out, Square/Triangle or X/Y (R, F on keys) do what the prompts say, L1/R1 or Q/E change tabs,\n321\tthe right stick scrolls. The mouse hovers to move focus and clicks to confirm; arrow keys work too.\n322\t\n323\tStandard mapping notes: Options is `buttons[9]`, Create/View is `buttons[8]`, which this game leaves\n324\tunused. Don't use the touchpad button: not every pad has one. Gilrs names: L1 is `LeftTrigger`, L2 is\n325\t`LeftTrigger2`. In a session, ignore Options while Create is held: that chord belongs to the hub.\n326\t\n327\t**Pad targeting:** attacks snap to the best enemy in a 60° cone around the stick or facing, within reach\n328\tplus 1.5 m; `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/touch.rs`'s `pick_target` has the logic to salvage before you remove that file.\n329\tGround-target rites land on that target, or 8 m ahead. **Click-to-move** goes in the sim (a new\n330\t`InputFrame` field) with `NavGrid`, so it replays and works for guests.\n331\t\n332\t**Hover and focus in the world:** the thing under the cursor, or the pad's current target, gets an\n333\toutline, and its nameplate shows top centre.\n334\t\n335\t### Rules and feel\n336\t- **Life:** hero life; no regen by default. **Blood motes** drop from 30% of kills (elites always) and\n337\t  heal 15% within a 2 m pickup. **Sexton's Gin:** 60% life, 30 s cooldown, unlimited. Its label says\n338\t  \"tastes of grave\".\n339\t- **Dodge:** keep `DODGE_SPEED`, `DODGE_TIME`; i-frames throughout; 2 charges, 3.5 s each.\n340\t- **Hits:** keep `arpg`'s hit-stop (30–70 ms by weight), shake, flash, knockback, gibs. Deaths fling\n341\t  bodies. Big kills get slow-motion for one beat. All scaled by sliders.\n342\t- **Harvest:** kills within 4 s chain: 6 = \"Small Harvest\", 15 = \"Good Harvest\", 30 = \"Bumper Harvest\",\n343\t  with an XP bonus (`streak` exists). Kills by falling scenery: \"Act of God\", bonus XP.\n344\t- **Breakables everywhere:** urns, coffins, pews, kegs that blow, chandeliers and statues that drop on\n345\t  what stands under them. Use `destruct.rs`, the keg code and physics props. Each floor needs at least\n346\t  one thing that kills a pack if the player notices it.\n347\t- **Death:** desaturate, Mabry's line, respawn at the floor's start or the last Lychstone after 3 s.\n348\t  No penalty on Mercy and Penance; from Dread up, 10% gold. In co-op, hold the interact prompt 2 s over\n349\t  a fallen ally to revive; otherwise they respawn after 8 s.\n350\t- **Levels:** cap 20, reached about the final boss on Penance. Then **the Sexton's Tally**: every level's\n351\t  worth of XP earns a point, spent across all heroes on Might (damage), Mercy (life), Haste (speed) or\n352\t  Greed (gold and find). Four rows, no tree.\n353\t- **Difficulty** (`Sexton's roll`, in town or at New Hero):\n354\t\n355\t| Tier | Monster life and damage | XP, gold | Relic chance |\n356\t|---|---|---|---|\n357\t| Mercy | ×0.6 | +0% | ×1 |\n358\t| Penance (default) | ×1 | +0% | ×1 |\n359\t| Dread | ×1.7 | +25% | ×1.5 |\n360\t| Anathema | ×2.8 | +60% | ×2 |\n361\t| Perdition | ×4.5 | +110% | ×3 |\n362\t| Oblivion | ×7 | +200% | ×5 |\n363\t\n364\t- **Co-op scaling:** n heroes in the world: monster life ×(1 + 0.75(n−1)), damage ×(1 + 0.25(n−1)).\n365\t- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n366\t  starts fresh and never crashes. A roster of heroes, each with their own gold and gear; the coffin and\n367\t  the Tally are shared.\n368\t\n369\t### Endgame: the Undertoll\n370\tFrom the Lychstone after the chapter ends (and from Dev Mode). Choose a Depth (1 to your best + 3); it\n371\tsets monster level and difficulty. A shuffled run of 3–5 generated floors mixing every theme, mechanic\n372\tand family (the existing endless generator). A **10-minute** bar. Kills fill **the Peal** by monster\n373\tweight. At 100% **the Warden** appears (a generated boss: `gen:<seed>`, with phases). Kill it before time\n374\tfor a relic shower and a higher best; late still pays, less. Best Depth per hero is shown on the Lychstone.\n375\t\n376\t---\n377\t\n378\t## 6. Classes\n379\t\n380\tFour heroes, all bipeds, each with a look, a resource, 8 rites and 6 vows. Each skill \"base\" below is a\n381\tkey in the engine's `engine/game/skills.toml`: copy it, rename it, retune it. Keep `behavior`, change the\n382\trest. Tones are `Tweak`s, the engine's 13 fields: damage, count, radius, cooldown, cost, pierce, chain,\n383\tailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\n384\tmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown. A rite's first tone unlocks\n385\twith it, its second 3 levels later and its third 6 levels later (never past L20). Swapping is free once\n386\tyou've been out of combat for 3 s.\n387\t\n388\tSix bar slots. Resource rules go in one place: `max`, `regen`, `on_hit`, `on_hurt`, `on_corpse`,\n389\t`decay`, in `engine/game/heroes.toml`, mapped on to the engine's `mana` (rename it per class in all text).\n390\t\n391\t### The Penitent: melee, heavy\n392\tA hooded giant in sackcloth and wrapped chains, swinging an iron censer on a flail.\n393\t**Contrition** (max 100): +6 per Scourge hit, +1 per 2% life lost, −4/s after 5 s out of combat.\n394\tSpending heals 0.2% life per point. *Pain is prayer.* Hood helmet; new prop `censer_flail` on a `mace`.\n395\t\n396\t| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n397\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n398\t| Scourge | 1 | `slash` (3-swing combo) | builds | Barbed: ailment 30 · Thurible: element fire, damage 10 · Long Chain: range 40 |\n399\t| Sweep of Ash | 1 | `cleave` | 20 | Ember Wake: element fire, radius 25 · Heavy Hand: damage 40 · Second Blow: count 1 |\n400\t| Penitent's Leap | 2 | `leap_slam` | CD 8 | Crater: radius 35 · Quick Knees: cooldown 35 · Thunderclap: element lightning, damage 20 |\n401\t| Iron Litany | 4 | `whirlwind` | 9/s | Bleeding Hymn: ailment 40 · Swift Rosary: speed 30 · Burning Censer: element fire, damage 15 |\n402\t| Hair Shirt | 6 | `war_cry`: 6 s, 30% less damage taken, Contrition gain ×1.5 | CD 15 | Shared Burden: radius 100 · Long Fast: duration 60 · Bitter Cup: cooldown 30 |\n403\t| Grave Furrow | 9 | `earthsplitter` | 30, CD 5 | Long Furrow: count 3 · Wide Furrow: radius 30 · Sundered Saints: element fire, damage 25 |\n404\t| Drag to Confession | 12 | `blade_dash`: dashes through, drags and stuns 1 s | CD 6 | Long Reach: range 40 · Quick Confession: cooldown 35 · Breaking Wheel: knockback 3, damage 30 |\n405\t| Martyr's Toll | 15 | `frost_nova`, physical: huge, costs 15% life | CD 18 | Wide Toll: radius 40 · Red Toll: element fire, damage 30 · Quiet Toll: cooldown 35 |\n406\t\n407\t### The Carillon: ranged caster\n408\tSlim and robed; three small bells orbit them; carries a bell-staff. **Resonance** (max 100): regen 12/s.\n409\t**Changes:** casting a different rite from the last adds a stack (max 5, +8% damage each, 4 s); repeating\n410\tone clears them. Pips on the gauge. New props `bell_staff`, `hand_bell`. Clips as Shardfall's caster\n411\t(`heroes.toml`, the Ysolde kit).\n412\t\n413\t| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n414\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n415\t| Clear Note | 1 | `fireball`, physical | free | Sharp Note: pierce 2 · Twin Note: count 1 · Burning Note: element fire |\n416\t| Toll | 1 | `frost_nova`, physical | 25, CD 4 | Wide Peal: radius 35 · Hoar Peal: element cold, ailment 40 · Quick Peal: cooldown 35 |\n417\t| Carol of Sparks | 2 | `chain_lightning` | 18 | Long Carol: chain 2 · Bright Carol: damage 30 · Ember Carol: element fire |\n418\t| Step Between | 4 | `blink` | CD 6 | Far Step: range 40 · Quick Step: cooldown 35 · Thunder Step: damage 40 |\n419\t| Winter Hymn | 6 | `blizzard` | 30, CD 6 | Long Winter: duration 50 · Wide Winter: radius 30 · Killing Frost: damage 30, ailment 30 |\n420\t| The Great Knell | 9 | `meteor`: a spectral bell falls | 45, CD 6 | Triple Knell: count 2 · Wide Knell: radius 35 · Storm Knell: element lightning, damage 20 |\n421\t| Bronze Shards | 12 | `ice_shards`, physical | 22 | Full Fan: count 3 · Piercing: pierce 2 · Ember Shards: element fire, ailment 30 |\n422\t| Sympathetic Ring | 15 | `war_cry`: 8 s, +30% cast speed, regen ×2 | CD 20 | Long Ring: duration 50 · Shared Ring: radius 100 · Quick Ring: cooldown 30 |\n423\t\n424\t### The Plaguewright: ranged trapper\n425\tBeak mask, long coat, wide hat, crossbow. **Bile** (max 100): +10 per Tainted Bolt hit, +3/s. New props\n426\t`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket on a `wand`-kind weapon), `pitch_flask`.\n427\t\n428\t| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n429\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n430\t| Tainted Bolt | 1 | `fireball`, physical, anim `throw` | builds | Foul: element poison, ailment 40 · Piercing: pierce 2 · Split: count 2 |\n431\t| Flask of Pitch | 1 | `meteor`: delay 0.5, small | 25, CD 1 | Wide Splash: radius 40 · Burning Pitch: element fire, ailment 30 · Thrown Twice: count 1 |\n432\t| Bone Snare | 2 | **new `trap`**: arms on the ground, snaps when a foe is near; 3 armed at most | 20, CD 4 | Three at Once: count 2 · Wide Jaws: radius 40 · Venom Jaws: element poison, ailment 40 |\n433\t| Smoke Step | 4 | `blink` | CD 7 | Far: range 40 · Quick: cooldown 35 · Choking Cloud: element poison, ailment 40 |\n434\t| Miasma | 6 | `blizzard`, element poison | 30, CD 6 | Lingering: duration 50 · Creeping: radius 30 · Thick: damage 30 |\n435\t| Rain of Rot | 9 | `toxic_rain` | 35, CD 5 | Downpour: count 4 · Spreading: radius 30 · Burning Rain: element fire |\n436\t| Leech Swarm | 12 | `chain_lightning`, element poison | 22 | Long Swarm: chain 3 · Gorged: damage 30 · Hungry: ailment 40 |\n437\t| Quarantine | 15 | `war_cry`: 8 s, +25% speed, +20% crit, no ailments | CD 20 | Long: duration 50 · Shared: radius 100 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n438\t\n439\t### The Gravewarden: summoner\n440\tBroad, gravedigger's hat, swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool` with `head=shovel`, already in the store). **Dirge**\n441\t(max 100): +8 per corpse falling within 12 m, +5 per Spade hit, +2/s in combat.\n442\tAllied actors are the one big new system here; followers share it (`Team::Hero`, `Actor.master`, brain\n443\ttargets monsters). Thralls: skeleton look, follow, attack, die in 3–4 hits, respawn by casting.\n444\t\n445\t| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n446\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n447\t| Spade | 1 | `slash`, 2-swing | builds | Keen Edge: damage 20 · Long Handle: range 30 · Frost-Turned: element cold, ailment 30 |\n448\t| Raise Thrall | 1 | **new `summon`**: up to 3 | 30, CD 1.5 | Bigger Flock: count 2 · Burning Dead: element fire · Hard Bones: damage 40 |\n449\t| Corpse Burst | 2 | `frost_nova` at the nearest corpse in 12 m, uses `power_corpse` | 20, CD 1 | Wide: radius 35 · Cold Bodies: element cold, ailment 30 · Two at Once: count 1 |\n450\t| Fresh Earth | 4 | `blizzard`, physical: slows 50% | 20, CD 8 | Deep: duration 50 · Wide: radius 30 · Grasping: damage 30 |\n451\t| Bone Furrow | 6 | `earthsplitter` | 30, CD 5 | Long: count 3 · Wide: radius 30 · Rotten: element poison, ailment 40 |\n452\t| Go to Ground | 9 | `blink`: sinks, 0.6 s untouchable, erupts | CD 8 | Far: range 40 · Quick: cooldown 35 · Erupting: damage 40 |\n453\t| Funeral Cry | 12 | `war_cry`: self and thralls +30% attack speed | CD 15 | Long: duration 50 · Wide: radius 60 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n454\t| Mass Grave | 15 | `meteor`, huge; what it kills rises as a thrall for 12 s | 50, CD 20 | Wide: radius 40 · Deep: duration 60 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n455\t\n456\t### Vows (3 slots, opening at L5, L10, L15; each is a stat block or an engine power)\n457\t| Class | Vows |\n458\t|---|---|\n459\t| Penitent | Unmoved (`stand_firm`) · Mortification (rites also cost 2% life, +25% damage) · Red Fervour (`frenzy`) · Last Rites (`execute`) · The Second Stroke (`echo_strike`) · Iron Skin (+30% armour) |\n460\t| Carillon | Sympathetic Strings (`storm_call`) · Hum of Winter (`frost_crits`) · Quick Rounds (`quickening`) · Warding Note (`mana_shield`) · Three Small Bells (`orbit_blades`, drawn as bells) · Wide Voice (+20% area) |\n461\t| Plaguewright | Hot Pitch (`fire_trail`) · Light Feet (`dodge_reset`) · Bursting Bodies (`corpse_burst`) · Aura of Rot (`ignite_aura`, poison) · Long Shot (+25% range, +5% crit) · Steady Hands (+15% attack speed) |\n462\t| Gravewarden | Bursting Bodies (`corpse_burst`) · Grave Air (`ignite_aura`, cold) · Long Shift (+1 thrall) · Warding Dirge (`mana_shield`) · Tithe of Bone (`quickening`) · Heavy Spade (+30% melee damage) |\n463\t\n464\t---\n465\t\n466\t## 7. Items and town\n467\t\n468\t**Slots:** weapon, off-hand, helm, body, gloves, boots, belt, amulet, ring ×2 (`EquipSlot` as is). Keep\n469\tbases and affixes as a system; rename all of it to fit (rusted, parish, reliquary, saint's...). Worn gear\n470\tshows on the puppet, as now.\n471\t\n472\t**Rarity ladder:** Plain (bone white), Hallowed (cold blue), Storied (gold), **Relic** (ember orange, tall\n473\tbeam, a chime in the toll motif), **Regalia** (verdigris green). Shape as well as colour: Storied and up\n474\tget a mark on the name so colour alone never carries it. Gold and motes pick up by walking near. Items\n475\tare personal in co-op. **Item level follows the zone.** Elites drop more; bosses shower.\n476\t\n477\t**Relics:** 16, each an engine power with a lore line in voice. Each a legend of the vale. Keep the\n478\tpower and numbers from `engine/game/uniques.toml`, change the rest.\n479\t\n480\t| Relic | Slot | Power |\n481\t|---|---|---|\n482\t| The Undertaker's Mercy | gloves | `corpse_burst` |\n483\t| Winter Psalter | off-hand | `frost_crits` |\n484\t| Tithe of Red Coin | ring | `blood_magic` |\n485\t| Last Rites of Saint Orrin | weapon | `execute` |\n486\t| Cinder-Soled Pilgrim's Boots | boots | `fire_trail` |\n487\t| Three Small Mercies | amulet | `orbit_blades` (bells) |\n488\t| The Second Stroke | weapon | `echo_strike` |\n489\t| Gravedigger's Knee | belt | `dodge_reset` |\n490\t| Ringer's Rope of the Tempest | belt | `storm_call` |\n491\t| Bell-Bronze Buckler | off-hand | `block_nova` |\n492\t| Smouldering Mitre | helm | `ignite_aura` |\n493\t| Penitent's Anchor | boots | `stand_firm` |\n494\t| The Falling Saint | weapon | `meteor_slam` |\n495\t| Wolfsbane Cup | ring | `frenzy` |\n496\t| Voice of the Cloister | body | `mana_shield` |\n497\t| Hourglass of the Sexton | amulet | `quickening` |\n498\t\n499\t**Regalia:** one 4-piece set per class (a new `set` key on items; the `Sheet` counts pieces). 2 pieces: a\n500\tstat. 4 pieces: a build-changer.\n501\t- *Hair and Iron* (Penitent): Scourge's third swing casts a free Grave Furrow.\n502\t- *The Ringing Chamber* (Carillon): at 5 Changes, the next rite casts twice.\n503\t- *The Doctor's Rounds* (Plaguewright): poisoned enemies burst on death and spread it.\n504\t- *The Last Shift* (Gravewarden): thralls explode on death and rise again free.\n505\t\n506\t**Gems:** Bloodstone (damage or life), Seaglass (resource or armour), Jet (crit or resist), Verdigris\n507\t(gold and find); tiers Chipped, Cut, Flawless; three combine into one. Weapons and bodies roll 0–2 sockets.\n508\t\n509\t**Materials:** Scrap (Plain, Hallowed), Relic Dust (Storied), Saint's Ash (Relic, Regalia).\n510\t\n511\t**Vespergate services.** One verb set per person, on one big screen each (§9).\n512\t| Who | Verbs |\n513\t|---|---|\n514\t| Hob Cullender, founder | Buy, Sell, Salvage, Reforge (materials and gold make a Storied item for a slot) |\n515\t| Madam Ottoline Quire | Socket, Set gem, Pull gem, Combine |\n516\t| Sister Aveline Pell | Tune (reroll one affix), **the Reliquary** (destroy a Relic to keep its power; three slots, Weapon, Armour, Jewel, hold one stored power each; costs Saint's Ash) |\n517\t| Goody Farthing | Sealed boxes by slot: Hallowed 60%, Storied 22%, Relic 3% |\n518\t| Sexton Mabry | Quests, Tally, Difficulty, Tomes read back |\n519\t| Your coffin | Stash, shared by all heroes: 40 items, by slot |\n520\t| Lychstone | Waypoints, Undertoll |\n521\t| Lisbet, Anselm (once met) | Hire one follower, solo only. Each has one weapon, one trinket and two rites they choose; barks in the field |\n522\t\n523\t---\n524\t\n525\t## 8. Zones, monsters, bosses\n526\t\n527\tEach floor is a `[[level]]` row in `engine/game/levels.toml`, extended with `zone` and `floor`, painted by\n528\t`engine/game/themes.toml`. `Place::Level(n)` indexes the table; past its end comes the Undertoll generator.\n529\tTwo new grammars beside \"rooms and corridors\": **open** (wide irregular clearings 30–45 m joined by\n530\t8–10 m paths; walls are hedgerow, cliff, dead trees) and **designed** (ASCII room file). Generated floors\n531\tare new each visit, as now.\n532\t\n533\t| Zone | Floors, grammar | Theme, light | Mechanics (engine name → ours) | Monsters | Set piece |\n534\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n535\t| **Potter's Field** | 1, designed | Moonlit grey-green, fog, gravestones | Breakable graves, kegs | Shambler, Grave Hound | Rising; holding the lych-gate |\n536\t| **Vespergate** (town) | designed | Warm lamps under cold sky; Old Compline huge on the hill behind | — | — | Mabry's grave deepens each visit; townsfolk thin out as the chapter goes |\n537\t| **The Lych Road** | 2, open | Dusk blue, ember lanterns | `shrines` → Wayside Shrines; `cursed_vaults` → Cursed Reliquaries; carts to topple | Shambler, Bone Thrall, Grave Hound, Tithe-Taker | The Hanged Men |\n538\t| **Undercroft of St. Orrin** | 3, rooms | Bone and candle gold | `crumbling_halls`; `gauntlet` → Iron Maidens (spikes on a beat); `powder_keg` → Blight Kegs | Bone Thrall, Bone Archer, Tithe-Taker, Gargoyle | Gaudry in the Tithe Barn |\n539\t| **The Sallow Fens** | 2, open | Sickly green, rain, fireflies | `totems` → Tacet Effigies; bog (slows) | Bog Wight, Carrion Moth, Hush Sister, Tithe-Taker | Three rites; Lisbet |\n540\t| **The Drowned Chapel** (optional) | 1, rooms | Black water | `lightless_deep`: wells to light | Bog Wight, Hush Sister | Tome, sure relic |\n541\t| **The Bellfoundry** | 2, rooms | Black iron, molten orange | `molten_floor`, kegs, `gauntlet` as drop-forges | Slag Golem, Bell-Beetle, Hush Sister | Prioress in the Mold Pit |\n542\t| **The Great Belfry** | 3, designed short arenas | Bronze, storm, lightning | `windways`, `crumbling_halls` | Gargoyle, Choir Shard, Slag Golem | The climb |\n543\t| **The Bell Pit** | 1, designed | Black pit, the bell above | Ropes | The Bellwether | Finale |\n544\t| **The Bishop's Geese** (secret) | 1, open | Absurdly sunny meadow | — | Geese in tiny mitres, with narration straight-faced | Geese |\n545\t\n546\tRemove `frozen_lake`, `time_rift`, `rift_gates` unless you want them for the Undertoll. Dress floors from\n547\t`engine/game/props.toml` with the gothic kit (§10). **Density:** 60–120 monsters a floor, packs of 6–18, big\n548\tfights 30–40 on screen.\n549\t\n550\t### Monsters (`engine/game/monsters.toml`; bipeds use the engine's clips)\n551\t| Family | Body, archetype | Skills | Look and behaviour |\n552\t|---|---|---|---|\n553\t| Shambler | biped, melee | `claw` | Grey, shrouded. `QUATERNIUS/Zombie_*`. Slow, many |\n554\t| Bone Thrall | biped, melee | `smash` | Thin limbs, pale, rusted blade; bursts into bones |\n555\t| Bone Archer | biped, ranged | `spit`, as a bolt | Keeps its distance |\n556\t| Grave Hound | quadruped, charger | `bite`, `gore` | Lopes in packs |\n557\t| Carrion Moth | blob with `wings`, swarm | `bite` | Small, erratic, dozens |\n558\t| Tithe-Taker | biped, caster | bolts, summons Shamblers | Hood, iron mouth-bar. Silent |\n559\t| Hush Sister | biped, stalker | `blade_dash`, teleport | Blinks behind you; silence ring on hit (§ Prioress) |\n560\t| Bog Wight | biped, tank | `stomp` | Bloated; poison cloud on death |\n561\t| Gargoyle | biped with `wings`, charger | `leap_slam` | **A statue until you are near.** Stone skin |\n562\t| Bell-Beetle | beetle, bomber | blast | A small bell on its back rings faster as it nears you |\n563\t| Slag Golem | biped, tank | `smash`, burning ground | Glows through its cracks |\n564\t| Choir Shard | blob, floating, caster | beam, nova | A faceless gold head and halo |\n565\t| **The Magpie** | small biped, flees | none | In a dead man's coat with a stuffed sack and a stolen altar bell. Appears at random, flees, drops coins as you hit it; dives down a bolt-hole after 20 s; killed: a loot shower and a jingle |\n566\t| Goose | blob or lizard | `bite` | Mitre. Honk |\n567\t\n568\t**Elites.** *Accursed* packs: 3–5 blue, one shared affix. *Damned*: gold, named by the generator\n569\t(\"Gorrel the Unrepentant\"), 2–4 affixes, with minions. Rename `engine/game/monster_affixes.toml` and add the two\n570\tsignature ones: **Molten** (burning trail, burst on death), **Hoarfrost** (`frost_touched`), **Sparking**\n571\t(`storm_touched`), **Pestilent** (`venomous`), **Slipping** (`teleporting`), **Tithe-Lord** (`warlord`),\n572\t**Broody** (`brood`), **Wrathful** (`enraging`), **Warded** (`arcane_shield`), **Leeching** (`vampiric`),\n573\tnew **Tolling** (rings expand from it every 5 s), new **Jailer** (roots you for 1.5 s with a telegraph).\n574\tAffix names show under the target's bar.\n575\t\n576\t### Bosses (`engine/game/bosses.toml`; phase scripts exist)\n577\tEach has a designed arena, an entrance (the engine's boss entrance beat), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\n578\ta line per phase, a guaranteed relic the first time, and a shower of loot.\n579\t\n580\t**Ser Gaudry Vane, the Tithe Knight.** Biped, scale 2.2, greatsword and a great ledger on a chain.\n581\t- 100%: sweeps. **Assessment:** rings mark where you stand; they erupt 1.2 s later.\n582\t- 70%: **Collection:** four Bone Thralls climb out of the walls. \"The tithe is due!\"\n583\t- 40%: **Arrears:** charges three times along telegraphed lanes.\n584\t- 15%: **Foreclosure:** enrages.\n585\t\n586\t**Prioress Amarante.** Slim caster, scale 1.3, teleports between four platforms in the Mold Pit.\n587\t- **The Hush:** a slow ring spreads; caught in it, you can use only Rite 1 for 2 s. Roll through it.\n588\t- 66%: Hush Sisters. Molten bronze rises in quadrants, with warning.\n589\t- 33%: she stops mid-fight and speaks. Then all at once. Below 5% the cutscene takes over.\n590\t\n591\t**The Bellwether.** Scale 4.5. Biped, `wings`, a shepherd's crook, and **a bronze bell for a head** (a prop\n592\tdrawn at the head anchor with `emit_asset`; tiny `head_radius`). Bell Pit: a 30 m round arena with four\n593\tropes at its rim and the cracked Old Compline hanging above. Aveline is at the ropes.\n594\t- **Toll:** every 12 s, after a three-count of rising bell strokes, a ring of force expands from the boss:\n595\t  the screen-distortion ring is the picture, the bell is the warning. Roll through it, or stand by a\n596\t  Still Stone. **The audio is the telegraph; the visual must work alone too.**\n597\t- **Ropes:** a rope lights every 20 s. Hold interact 1 s beside it: Old Compline rings, the boss is stunned\n598\t  5 s and takes 50% more damage. Bots must use them. Works solo; great with four.\n599\t- 100–66%: crook sweeps, the Flock spawns at the rim.\n600\t- 66–33%: hovers; beams turn like a wheel; floor tiles crumble.\n601\t- 33–0%: the bell-head cracks; tolls come faster. The Prioress's voice helps one last time: \"Now, little\n602\t  corpse. It is listening to itself.\" At 0: slow-motion, the great bell falls, the Compline cutscene.\n603\t\n604\t---\n605\t\n606\t## 9. Screens\n607\t\n608\t### Rules for every screen (10-foot, controller-first)\n609\t- At 1920×1080: safe margin 96 px sides and 54 px top and bottom. Body text at least 28 px, no text under\n610\t  24 px, headings 40+, menu items 72 px tall at 36 px, at most 7 items in a column. Scale by screen\n611\t  height, with a UI scale setting (100, 125, 150%).\n612\t- **One thing focused at a time**, always clearly lit. A card shows the focused thing's detail. No\n613\t  hover-only information, no tiny icon grids, no tables of stats, no scroll bars except for long text.\n614\t- Build a shared **focus layer** in `pav_ui`: screens declare focusable items with ids and rects; the layer"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"6ac22ace-f0be-4be5-bb2c-4a782f78d9fa","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:41.389Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**The truth (revealed in Q9).** The toll never laid the dead to rest. It herded them. Under the bell\nlies **the Bellwether**, once the Choir's shepherd of souls, which for nine hundred years has been\ngathering its flock down through the ground. The Tacet cracked the bell on purpose, to stop the\nherding, and in doing so let the shepherd wake.\n\n### Cast\n| Who | Role | Voice and manner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **The Narrator** | Title crawl, chapter beats | Slow, deep, sure of the worst |\n| **Sexton Mabry Thole** | Old gravedigger, quest-giver, keeps your Tally and the difficulty roll | Gruff, tender about corpses, knows everything because he buried it. Digs one grave throughout the game: deeper at every visit. It is his own |\n| **Sister Aveline Pell** | One-armed bell-ringer, runs Tuning and the Reliquary | Young, furious, exact |\n| **Hob Cullender** | Bell-founder turned smith, deaf from the bells | SHOUTS EVERYTHING |\n| **Madam Ottoline Quire** | Chandler and jeweller | Dry, gossiping, expensive |\n| **Goody Farthing** | Sells sealed boxes (gamble) | Cheerfully sinister |\n| **Lisbet Marl** | Poacher, follower | Curt, unimpressed, good shot |\n| **Brother Anselm** | Drunk healer, follower | Merry, ashamed, sings badly |\n| **Ser Gaudry Vane, the Tithe Knight** | Boss 1 | Undead tax collector. Pompous, punctilious |\n| **Prioress Amarante** | Boss 2, leader of the Tacet, speaks in your head | Tongueless, patient, nearly right |\n| **The Bellwether** | Final boss | Speaks in tolls; subtitles in capitals |\n| **The Tacet** | The cult | Cut out their tongues and wear iron mouth-bars. Never make a sound; their silence is the threat |\n\n**Your coffin** is the stash: Mabry had it brought to town. \"It's yours. You've used it.\"\n\n### Chapter One: The Silence (about 90 minutes first time)\n| # | Quest | Where | Beats |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Q1 | **Get Up** | Potter's Field | Crawl: the Narrator over the night churchyard. You claw out of a grave (press to rise, `MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`). Mabry greets you. Learn move, attack, rite, motes, breakable graves |\n| Q2 | **The Lych Road** | Potter's Field → Vespergate | Reach the lych-gate. **Set piece:** hold the gate for 90 s beside the town's last watchmen, kegs and all |\n| Q3 | **Last Rites** | Vespergate | Meet Hob, Ottoline, your coffin, the Lychstone. Mabry wants the Parish Roll from St. Orrin's |\n| Q4 | **Arrears** | The Lych Road, then Undercroft 1–3 | First elites, first gargoyle ambush, first relic (guaranteed from Gaudry). Kill **Ser Gaudry**, take the Roll |\n| Q5 | **Names That Don't Match** | Town → Sallow Fens | Mabry reads the Roll: hundreds of graves were empty long before the crack. The Tacet's camps are in the Fens |\n| Q6 | **The Hush** | Sallow Fens 1–2 | Rescue Lisbet (first follower). Break three Tacet rites: each is an event where effigies ward the enemy. The Prioress first speaks in your head |\n| Q7 | **The Drowned Chapel** (optional) | Fens side dungeon | Darkness, wells to light, Tome, sure relic |\n| Q8 | **Founder's Debt** | Bellfoundry 1–2 | Hob wants his molds back; Aveline wants a new clapper cast. Kill **Prioress Amarante** |\n| Q9 | **What the Bell Was Saying** | Cutscene, then town | Beaten, she shows you the truth; the Bellwether hauls her down. In town Mabry admits he too is Unshriven, the first, two hundred years digging. \"Who did you think buries the gravediggers?\" |\n| Q10 | **The Great Belfry** | Belfry 1–3, Bell Pit | Climb in wind and lightning, Aveline at your side. Kill **the Bellwether**. The bell falls |\n| End | **Compline** | Cutscene | The dead truly lie down. Mabry climbs into the grave he has been digging, and sleeps. Then the sky opens: the Choir's heralds, come to collect. Credits. The Undertoll unlocks |\n\n**Side events** (random placement, each with a one-line hook and a reward):\n- *The Hanged Men:* three corpses drop from a gibbet and fight.\n- *The Widow's Dowry:* a cursed reliquary calls waves, then pays.\n- *The Weeping Saint:* break five urns round a statue for a long buff.\n- *Lost Choirboy:* escort him to the Lychstone. He sings, badly, and draws attacks.\n- *Magpie!:* see §8.\n- *A Tithe of Geese:* opens the secret level. Find four hand-bells, one per zone, and ring them at\n  Vespergate's broken pump.\n\n**Tomes** (8, found in the world, read aloud while you keep playing, subtitled, stopped from the Journal): The\nSexton's Ledger I–IV, Hymnal of the Tacet, Confession of Ser Gaudry, Founder's Notes, A Letter Never Sent.\n\n### Writing style\nGrand and doom-laden when the world speaks, dry and human when people do. Short sentences. Villains\nenjoy themselves. Nobody explains a joke. Every line is shown as a subtitle and spoken in gibberish\n(§11). Write all of it yourself in this voice, and write plenty: barks for every NPC, 4–6 per villain\nper phase, a line for every shop action. These set the tone:\n\n- **Narrator:** \"For nine hundred years, when dusk fell on the vale of Aubrenne, the great bell Old\n  Compline spoke, and the dead lay still. Forty nights ago it cracked. Now it speaks only to them.\"\n- **Mabry, first line:** \"Easy. Easy. You're the fourth this week, and the first to look sorry about\n  it. Mind the headstone. I carved that one.\"\n- **Mabry, on your death:** \"Back of the queue, friend.\"\n- **Hob:** \"WHAT'S THAT? A SWORD? SPEAK UP, IT'S ALL BELLS IN HERE.\"\n- **Ottoline:** \"Candles are for the living, dear. Gems are for the dead. I'm told you're undecided.\"\n- **Aveline:** \"I have one arm and the only ear left in this vale that can hear a bell lie.\"\n- **Goody Farthing:** \"Never ask what's in the box. Ask what's in you, that you want it so badly.\"\n- **Gaudry:** \"Nine hundred years of tithes, and not one soul in arrears. Until you.\" / \"Your account,\n  Unshriven, is overdrawn.\" / dying: \"Mark it... paid.\"\n- **Prioress, in your head:** \"Little corpse. Do you hear how quiet it is between the tolls? That is\n  the only honest thing left in this world.\" / \"We cut out our tongues so we would never sing for it.\n  What have you given?\"\n- **Bellwether:** \"COME IN FROM THE COLD.\" / \"EVERY FLOCK COMES HOME.\" / \"I HAVE COUNTED YOU. YOU ARE\n  ONE SHORT.\"\n- **Choir herald, last line of the chapter:** \"We have come for what was entrusted. You will kneel, or\n  you will be catalogued.\"\n\n**How it's delivered:** quest log (`engine/game/quests.toml`, steps: `reach`, `kill`, `talk`, `use`, `clear`,\n`hold`, `collect`), conversations (`engine/game/dialogue.toml`, one speaker at a time with a topic list),\nvillain lines as a portrait slide-in at the side while you keep fighting, and four in-engine cutscenes\n(letterbox, scripted camera and puppets, skippable with a held button): Rising, Gaudry's entrance,\nPrioress's truth, Compline.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Play\n\n### Controls\n| Action | DualSense (Xbox glyphs in brackets) | Keyboard and mouse |\n|---|---|---|\n| Move | Left stick | Hold left mouse on the ground (walks there by pathfinding), or WASD |\n| Aim | Auto-target; right stick overrides while held | Mouse |\n| Rite 1 (builder) | Cross (A) | Left mouse on an enemy (walks into reach, repeats while held); Shift + left mouse attacks in place |\n| Rite 2 | Square (X) | Right mouse |\n| Rite 3 · 4 | Triangle (Y) · Circle (B) | 1 · 2 |\n| Rite 5 · 6 | R1 (RB) · R2 (RT) | 3 · 4 |\n| Dodge roll | L1 (LB) | Space |\n| Sexton's Gin | L2 (LT) | Q |\n| Talk, use, pick up | Cross when a prompt shows and no enemy is within 3 m | E, or left mouse on the thing |\n| Ring hand-bell (way home) | D-pad down, hold 1 s | T |\n| Hero screen | D-pad up | I or C (Gear), K (Rites), J (Journal) |\n| Map | D-pad left | M or Tab |\n| Item labels | D-pad right toggles | Hold Alt |\n| Pause | Options (Menu) | Esc |\n\n**In menus, on every device:** D-pad or left stick moves focus, Cross/A/Enter confirms, Circle/B/Esc\nbacks out, Square/Triangle or X/Y (R, F on keys) do what the prompts say, L1/R1 or Q/E change tabs,\nthe right stick scrolls. The mouse hovers to move focus and clicks to confirm; arrow keys work too.\n\nStandard mapping notes: Options is `buttons[9]`, Create/View is `buttons[8]`, which this game leaves\nunused. Don't use the touchpad button: not every pad has one. Gilrs names: L1 is `LeftTrigger`, L2 is\n`LeftTrigger2`. In a session, ignore Options while Create is held: that chord belongs to the hub.\n\n**Pad targeting:** attacks snap to the best enemy in a 60° cone around the stick or facing, within reach\nplus 1.5 m; `engine/crates/pav_ui/src/touch.rs`'s `pick_target` has the logic to salvage before you remove that file.\nGround-target rites land on that target, or 8 m ahead. **Click-to-move** goes in the sim (a new\n`InputFrame` field) with `NavGrid`, so it replays and works for guests.\n\n**Hover and focus in the world:** the thing under the cursor, or the pad's current target, gets an\noutline, and its nameplate shows top centre.\n\n### Rules and feel\n- **Life:** hero life; no regen by default. **Blood motes** drop from 30% of kills (elites always) and\n  heal 15% within a 2 m pickup. **Sexton's Gin:** 60% life, 30 s cooldown, unlimited. Its label says\n  \"tastes of grave\".\n- **Dodge:** keep `DODGE_SPEED`, `DODGE_TIME`; i-frames throughout; 2 charges, 3.5 s each.\n- **Hits:** keep `arpg`'s hit-stop (30–70 ms by weight), shake, flash, knockback, gibs. Deaths fling\n  bodies. Big kills get slow-motion for one beat. All scaled by sliders.\n- **Harvest:** kills within 4 s chain: 6 = \"Small Harvest\", 15 = \"Good Harvest\", 30 = \"Bumper Harvest\",\n  with an XP bonus (`streak` exists). Kills by falling scenery: \"Act of God\", bonus XP.\n- **Breakables everywhere:** urns, coffins, pews, kegs that blow, chandeliers and statues that drop on\n  what stands under them. Use `destruct.rs`, the keg code and physics props. Each floor needs at least\n  one thing that kills a pack if the player notices it.\n- **Death:** desaturate, Mabry's line, respawn at the floor's start or the last Lychstone after 3 s.\n  No penalty on Mercy and Penance; from Dread up, 10% gold. In co-op, hold the interact prompt 2 s over\n  a fallen ally to revive; otherwise they respawn after 8 s.\n- **Levels:** cap 20, reached about the final boss on Penance. Then **the Sexton's Tally**: every level's\n  worth of XP earns a point, spent across all heroes on Might (damage), Mercy (life), Haste (speed) or\n  Greed (gold and find). Four rows, no tree.\n- **Difficulty** (`Sexton's roll`, in town or at New Hero):\n\n| Tier | Monster life and damage | XP, gold | Relic chance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mercy | ×0.6 | +0% | ×1 |\n| Penance (default) | ×1 | +0% | ×1 |\n| Dread | ×1.7 | +25% | ×1.5 |\n| Anathema | ×2.8 | +60% | ×2 |\n| Perdition | ×4.5 | +110% | ×3 |\n| Oblivion | ×7 | +200% | ×5 |\n\n- **Co-op scaling:** n heroes in the world: monster life ×(1 + 0.75(n−1)), damage ×(1 + 0.25(n−1)).\n- **Saving:** autosave on travel, level-up, quest step and quit; `localStorage`, versioned. A bad save\n  starts fresh and never crashes. A roster of heroes, each with their own gold and gear; the coffin and\n  the Tally are shared.\n\n### Endgame: the Undertoll\nFrom the Lychstone after the chapter ends (and from Dev Mode). Choose a Depth (1 to your best + 3); it\nsets monster level and difficulty. A shuffled run of 3–5 generated floors mixing every theme, mechanic\nand family (the existing endless generator). A **10-minute** bar. Kills fill **the Peal** by monster\nweight. At 100% **the Warden** appears (a generated boss: `gen:<seed>`, with phases). Kill it before time\nfor a relic shower and a higher best; late still pays, less. Best Depth per hero is shown on the Lychstone.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Classes\n\nFour heroes, all bipeds, each with a look, a resource, 8 rites and 6 vows. Each skill \"base\" below is a\nkey in the engine's `engine/game/skills.toml`: copy it, rename it, retune it. Keep `behavior`, change the\nrest. Tones are `Tweak`s, the engine's 13 fields: damage, count, radius, cooldown, cost, pierce, chain,\nailment, duration, speed, range, knockback, element. Each tone below reads as tweak values; all numbers\nmean the bonus (`cooldown 35` = 35% shorter). Rites unlock at the level shown. A rite's first tone unlocks\nwith it, its second 3 levels later and its third 6 levels later (never past L20). Swapping is free once\nyou've been out of combat for 3 s.\n\nSix bar slots. Resource rules go in one place: `max`, `regen`, `on_hit`, `on_hurt`, `on_corpse`,\n`decay`, in `engine/game/heroes.toml`, mapped on to the engine's `mana` (rename it per class in all text).\n\n### The Penitent: melee, heavy\nA hooded giant in sackcloth and wrapped chains, swinging an iron censer on a flail.\n**Contrition** (max 100): +6 per Scourge hit, +1 per 2% life lost, −4/s after 5 s out of combat.\nSpending heals 0.2% life per point. *Pain is prayer.* Hood helmet; new prop `censer_flail` on a `mace`.\n\n| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Scourge | 1 | `slash` (3-swing combo) | builds | Barbed: ailment 30 · Thurible: element fire, damage 10 · Long Chain: range 40 |\n| Sweep of Ash | 1 | `cleave` | 20 | Ember Wake: element fire, radius 25 · Heavy Hand: damage 40 · Second Blow: count 1 |\n| Penitent's Leap | 2 | `leap_slam` | CD 8 | Crater: radius 35 · Quick Knees: cooldown 35 · Thunderclap: element lightning, damage 20 |\n| Iron Litany | 4 | `whirlwind` | 9/s | Bleeding Hymn: ailment 40 · Swift Rosary: speed 30 · Burning Censer: element fire, damage 15 |\n| Hair Shirt | 6 | `war_cry`: 6 s, 30% less damage taken, Contrition gain ×1.5 | CD 15 | Shared Burden: radius 100 · Long Fast: duration 60 · Bitter Cup: cooldown 30 |\n| Grave Furrow | 9 | `earthsplitter` | 30, CD 5 | Long Furrow: count 3 · Wide Furrow: radius 30 · Sundered Saints: element fire, damage 25 |\n| Drag to Confession | 12 | `blade_dash`: dashes through, drags and stuns 1 s | CD 6 | Long Reach: range 40 · Quick Confession: cooldown 35 · Breaking Wheel: knockback 3, damage 30 |\n| Martyr's Toll | 15 | `frost_nova`, physical: huge, costs 15% life | CD 18 | Wide Toll: radius 40 · Red Toll: element fire, damage 30 · Quiet Toll: cooldown 35 |\n\n### The Carillon: ranged caster\nSlim and robed; three small bells orbit them; carries a bell-staff. **Resonance** (max 100): regen 12/s.\n**Changes:** casting a different rite from the last adds a stack (max 5, +8% damage each, 4 s); repeating\none clears them. Pips on the gauge. New props `bell_staff`, `hand_bell`. Clips as Shardfall's caster\n(`heroes.toml`, the Ysolde kit).\n\n| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Clear Note | 1 | `fireball`, physical | free | Sharp Note: pierce 2 · Twin Note: count 1 · Burning Note: element fire |\n| Toll | 1 | `frost_nova`, physical | 25, CD 4 | Wide Peal: radius 35 · Hoar Peal: element cold, ailment 40 · Quick Peal: cooldown 35 |\n| Carol of Sparks | 2 | `chain_lightning` | 18 | Long Carol: chain 2 · Bright Carol: damage 30 · Ember Carol: element fire |\n| Step Between | 4 | `blink` | CD 6 | Far Step: range 40 · Quick Step: cooldown 35 · Thunder Step: damage 40 |\n| Winter Hymn | 6 | `blizzard` | 30, CD 6 | Long Winter: duration 50 · Wide Winter: radius 30 · Killing Frost: damage 30, ailment 30 |\n| The Great Knell | 9 | `meteor`: a spectral bell falls | 45, CD 6 | Triple Knell: count 2 · Wide Knell: radius 35 · Storm Knell: element lightning, damage 20 |\n| Bronze Shards | 12 | `ice_shards`, physical | 22 | Full Fan: count 3 · Piercing: pierce 2 · Ember Shards: element fire, ailment 30 |\n| Sympathetic Ring | 15 | `war_cry`: 8 s, +30% cast speed, regen ×2 | CD 20 | Long Ring: duration 50 · Shared Ring: radius 100 · Quick Ring: cooldown 30 |\n\n### The Plaguewright: ranged trapper\nBeak mask, long coat, wide hat, crossbow. **Bile** (max 100): +10 per Tainted Bolt hit, +3/s. New props\n`beak_mask` (helmet shape), `crossbow` (held by its grip socket on a `wand`-kind weapon), `pitch_flask`.\n\n| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Tainted Bolt | 1 | `fireball`, physical, anim `throw` | builds | Foul: element poison, ailment 40 · Piercing: pierce 2 · Split: count 2 |\n| Flask of Pitch | 1 | `meteor`: delay 0.5, small | 25, CD 1 | Wide Splash: radius 40 · Burning Pitch: element fire, ailment 30 · Thrown Twice: count 1 |\n| Bone Snare | 2 | **new `trap`**: arms on the ground, snaps when a foe is near; 3 armed at most | 20, CD 4 | Three at Once: count 2 · Wide Jaws: radius 40 · Venom Jaws: element poison, ailment 40 |\n| Smoke Step | 4 | `blink` | CD 7 | Far: range 40 · Quick: cooldown 35 · Choking Cloud: element poison, ailment 40 |\n| Miasma | 6 | `blizzard`, element poison | 30, CD 6 | Lingering: duration 50 · Creeping: radius 30 · Thick: damage 30 |\n| Rain of Rot | 9 | `toxic_rain` | 35, CD 5 | Downpour: count 4 · Spreading: radius 30 · Burning Rain: element fire |\n| Leech Swarm | 12 | `chain_lightning`, element poison | 22 | Long Swarm: chain 3 · Gorged: damage 30 · Hungry: ailment 40 |\n| Quarantine | 15 | `war_cry`: 8 s, +25% speed, +20% crit, no ailments | CD 20 | Long: duration 50 · Shared: radius 100 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n\n### The Gravewarden: summoner\nBroad, gravedigger's hat, swings a spade (`LIB/core/hafted_tool` with `head=shovel`, already in the store). **Dirge**\n(max 100): +8 per corpse falling within 12 m, +5 per Spade hit, +2/s in combat.\nAllied actors are the one big new system here; followers share it (`Team::Hero`, `Actor.master`, brain\ntargets monsters). Thralls: skeleton look, follow, attack, die in 3–4 hits, respawn by casting.\n\n| Rite | L | Base | Cost, cooldown | Tones |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Spade | 1 | `slash`, 2-swing | builds | Keen Edge: damage 20 · Long Handle: range 30 · Frost-Turned: element cold, ailment 30 |\n| Raise Thrall | 1 | **new `summon`**: up to 3 | 30, CD 1.5 | Bigger Flock: count 2 · Burning Dead: element fire · Hard Bones: damage 40 |\n| Corpse Burst | 2 | `frost_nova` at the nearest corpse in 12 m, uses `power_corpse` | 20, CD 1 | Wide: radius 35 · Cold Bodies: element cold, ailment 30 · Two at Once: count 1 |\n| Fresh Earth | 4 | `blizzard`, physical: slows 50% | 20, CD 8 | Deep: duration 50 · Wide: radius 30 · Grasping: damage 30 |\n| Bone Furrow | 6 | `earthsplitter` | 30, CD 5 | Long: count 3 · Wide: radius 30 · Rotten: element poison, ailment 40 |\n| Go to Ground | 9 | `blink`: sinks, 0.6 s untouchable, erupts | CD 8 | Far: range 40 · Quick: cooldown 35 · Erupting: damage 40 |\n| Funeral Cry | 12 | `war_cry`: self and thralls +30% attack speed | CD 15 | Long: duration 50 · Wide: radius 60 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n| Mass Grave | 15 | `meteor`, huge; what it kills rises as a thrall for 12 s | 50, CD 20 | Wide: radius 40 · Deep: duration 60 · Quick: cooldown 30 |\n\n### Vows (3 slots, opening at L5, L10, L15; each is a stat block or an engine power)\n| Class | Vows |\n|---|---|\n| Penitent | Unmoved (`stand_firm`) · Mortification (rites also cost 2% life, +25% damage) · Red Fervour (`frenzy`) · Last Rites (`execute`) · The Second Stroke (`echo_strike`) · Iron Skin (+30% armour) |\n| Carillon | Sympathetic Strings (`storm_call`) · Hum of Winter (`frost_crits`) · Quick Rounds (`quickening`) · Warding Note (`mana_shield`) · Three Small Bells (`orbit_blades`, drawn as bells) · Wide Voice (+20% area) |\n| Plaguewright | Hot Pitch (`fire_trail`) · Light Feet (`dodge_reset`) · Bursting Bodies (`corpse_burst`) · Aura of Rot (`ignite_aura`, poison) · Long Shot (+25% range, +5% crit) · Steady Hands (+15% attack speed) |\n| Gravewarden | Bursting Bodies (`corpse_burst`) · Grave Air (`ignite_aura`, cold) · Long Shift (+1 thrall) · Warding Dirge (`mana_shield`) · Tithe of Bone (`quickening`) · Heavy Spade (+30% melee damage) |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Items and town\n\n**Slots:** weapon, off-hand, helm, body, gloves, boots, belt, amulet, ring ×2 (`EquipSlot` as is). Keep\nbases and affixes as a system; rename all of it to fit (rusted, parish, reliquary, saint's...). Worn gear\nshows on the puppet, as now.\n\n**Rarity ladder:** Plain (bone white), Hallowed (cold blue), Storied (gold), **Relic** (ember orange, tall\nbeam, a chime in the toll motif), **Regalia** (verdigris green). Shape as well as colour: Storied and up\nget a mark on the name so colour alone never carries it. Gold and motes pick up by walking near. Items\nare personal in co-op. **Item level follows the zone.** Elites drop more; bosses shower.\n\n**Relics:** 16, each an engine power with a lore line in voice. Each a legend of the vale. Keep the\npower and numbers from `engine/game/uniques.toml`, change the rest.\n\n| Relic | Slot | Power |\n|---|---|---|\n| The Undertaker's Mercy | gloves | `corpse_burst` |\n| Winter Psalter | off-hand | `frost_crits` |\n| Tithe of Red Coin | ring | `blood_magic` |\n| Last Rites of Saint Orrin | weapon | `execute` |\n| Cinder-Soled Pilgrim's Boots | boots | `fire_trail` |\n| Three Small Mercies | amulet | `orbit_blades` (bells) |\n| The Second Stroke | weapon | `echo_strike` |\n| Gravedigger's Knee | belt | `dodge_reset` |\n| Ringer's Rope of the Tempest | belt | `storm_call` |\n| Bell-Bronze Buckler | off-hand | `block_nova` |\n| Smouldering Mitre | helm | `ignite_aura` |\n| Penitent's Anchor | boots | `stand_firm` |\n| The Falling Saint | weapon | `meteor_slam` |\n| Wolfsbane Cup | ring | `frenzy` |\n| Voice of the Cloister | body | `mana_shield` |\n| Hourglass of the Sexton | amulet | `quickening` |\n\n**Regalia:** one 4-piece set per class (a new `set` key on items; the `Sheet` counts pieces). 2 pieces: a\nstat. 4 pieces: a build-changer.\n- *Hair and Iron* (Penitent): Scourge's third swing casts a free Grave Furrow.\n- *The Ringing Chamber* (Carillon): at 5 Changes, the next rite casts twice.\n- *The Doctor's Rounds* (Plaguewright): poisoned enemies burst on death and spread it.\n- *The Last Shift* (Gravewarden): thralls explode on death and rise again free.\n\n**Gems:** Bloodstone (damage or life), Seaglass (resource or armour), Jet (crit or resist), Verdigris\n(gold and find); tiers Chipped, Cut, Flawless; three combine into one. Weapons and bodies roll 0–2 sockets.\n\n**Materials:** Scrap (Plain, Hallowed), Relic Dust (Storied), Saint's Ash (Relic, Regalia).\n\n**Vespergate services.** One verb set per person, on one big screen each (§9).\n| Who | Verbs |\n|---|---|\n| Hob Cullender, founder | Buy, Sell, Salvage, Reforge (materials and gold make a Storied item for a slot) |\n| Madam Ottoline Quire | Socket, Set gem, Pull gem, Combine |\n| Sister Aveline Pell | Tune (reroll one affix), **the Reliquary** (destroy a Relic to keep its power; three slots, Weapon, Armour, Jewel, hold one stored power each; costs Saint's Ash) |\n| Goody Farthing | Sealed boxes by slot: Hallowed 60%, Storied 22%, Relic 3% |\n| Sexton Mabry | Quests, Tally, Difficulty, Tomes read back |\n| Your coffin | Stash, shared by all heroes: 40 items, by slot |\n| Lychstone | Waypoints, Undertoll |\n| Lisbet, Anselm (once met) | Hire one follower, solo only. Each has one weapon, one trinket and two rites they choose; barks in the field |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Zones, monsters, bosses\n\nEach floor is a `[[level]]` row in `engine/game/levels.toml`, extended with `zone` and `floor`, painted by\n`engine/game/themes.toml`. `Place::Level(n)` indexes the table; past its end comes the Undertoll generator.\nTwo new grammars beside \"rooms and corridors\": **open** (wide irregular clearings 30–45 m joined by\n8–10 m paths; walls are hedgerow, cliff, dead trees) and **designed** (ASCII room file). Generated floors\nare new each visit, as now.\n\n| Zone | Floors, grammar | Theme, light | Mechanics (engine name → ours) | Monsters | Set piece |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Potter's Field** | 1, designed | Moonlit grey-green, fog, gravestones | Breakable graves, kegs | Shambler, Grave Hound | Rising; holding the lych-gate |\n| **Vespergate** (town) | designed | Warm lamps under cold sky; Old Compline huge on the hill behind | — | — | Mabry's grave deepens each visit; townsfolk thin out as the chapter goes |\n| **The Lych Road** | 2, open | Dusk blue, ember lanterns | `shrines` → Wayside Shrines; `cursed_vaults` → Cursed Reliquaries; carts to topple | Shambler, Bone Thrall, Grave Hound, Tithe-Taker | The Hanged Men |\n| **Undercroft of St. Orrin** | 3, rooms | Bone and candle gold | `crumbling_halls`; `gauntlet` → Iron Maidens (spikes on a beat); `powder_keg` → Blight Kegs | Bone Thrall, Bone Archer, Tithe-Taker, Gargoyle | Gaudry in the Tithe Barn |\n| **The Sallow Fens** | 2, open | Sickly green, rain, fireflies | `totems` → Tacet Effigies; bog (slows) | Bog Wight, Carrion Moth, Hush Sister, Tithe-Taker | Three rites; Lisbet |\n| **The Drowned Chapel** (optional) | 1, rooms | Black water | `lightless_deep`: wells to light | Bog Wight, Hush Sister | Tome, sure relic |\n| **The Bellfoundry** | 2, rooms | Black iron, molten orange | `molten_floor`, kegs, `gauntlet` as drop-forges | Slag Golem, Bell-Beetle, Hush Sister | Prioress in the Mold Pit |\n| **The Great Belfry** | 3, designed short arenas | Bronze, storm, lightning | `windways`, `crumbling_halls` | Gargoyle, Choir Shard, Slag Golem | The climb |\n| **The Bell Pit** | 1, designed | Black pit, the bell above | Ropes | The Bellwether | Finale |\n| **The Bishop's Geese** (secret) | 1, open | Absurdly sunny meadow | — | Geese in tiny mitres, with narration straight-faced | Geese |\n\nRemove `frozen_lake`, `time_rift`, `rift_gates` unless you want them for the Undertoll. Dress floors from\n`engine/game/props.toml` with the gothic kit (§10). **Density:** 60–120 monsters a floor, packs of 6–18, big\nfights 30–40 on screen.\n\n### Monsters (`engine/game/monsters.toml`; bipeds use the engine's clips)\n| Family | Body, archetype | Skills | Look and behaviour |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Shambler | biped, melee | `claw` | Grey, shrouded. `QUATERNIUS/Zombie_*`. Slow, many |\n| Bone Thrall | biped, melee | `smash` | Thin limbs, pale, rusted blade; bursts into bones |\n| Bone Archer | biped, ranged | `spit`, as a bolt | Keeps its distance |\n| Grave Hound | quadruped, charger | `bite`, `gore` | Lopes in packs |\n| Carrion Moth | blob with `wings`, swarm | `bite` | Small, erratic, dozens |\n| Tithe-Taker | biped, caster | bolts, summons Shamblers | Hood, iron mouth-bar. Silent |\n| Hush Sister | biped, stalker | `blade_dash`, teleport | Blinks behind you; silence ring on hit (§ Prioress) |\n| Bog Wight | biped, tank | `stomp` | Bloated; poison cloud on death |\n| Gargoyle | biped with `wings`, charger | `leap_slam` | **A statue until you are near.** Stone skin |\n| Bell-Beetle | beetle, bomber | blast | A small bell on its back rings faster as it nears you |\n| Slag Golem | biped, tank | `smash`, burning ground | Glows through its cracks |\n| Choir Shard | blob, floating, caster | beam, nova | A faceless gold head and halo |\n| **The Magpie** | small biped, flees | none | In a dead man's coat with a stuffed sack and a stolen altar bell. Appears at random, flees, drops coins as you hit it; dives down a bolt-hole after 20 s; killed: a loot shower and a jingle |\n| Goose | blob or lizard | `bite` | Mitre. Honk |\n\n**Elites.** *Accursed* packs: 3–5 blue, one shared affix. *Damned*: gold, named by the generator\n(\"Gorrel the Unrepentant\"), 2–4 affixes, with minions. Rename `engine/game/monster_affixes.toml` and add the two\nsignature ones: **Molten** (burning trail, burst on death), **Hoarfrost** (`frost_touched`), **Sparking**\n(`storm_touched`), **Pestilent** (`venomous`), **Slipping** (`teleporting`), **Tithe-Lord** (`warlord`),\n**Broody** (`brood`), **Wrathful** (`enraging`), **Warded** (`arcane_shield`), **Leeching** (`vampiric`),\nnew **Tolling** (rings expand from it every 5 s), new **Jailer** (roots you for 1.5 s with a telegraph).\nAffix names show under the target's bar.\n\n### Bosses (`engine/game/bosses.toml`; phase scripts exist)\nEach has a designed arena, an entrance (the engine's boss entrance beat), ground telegraphs for every big hit,\na line per phase, a guaranteed relic the first time, and a shower of loot.\n\n**Ser Gaudry Vane, the Tithe Knight.** Biped, scale 2.2, greatsword and a great ledger on a chain.\n- 100%: sweeps. **Assessment:** rings mark where you stand; they erupt 1.2 s later.\n- 70%: **Collection:** four Bone Thralls climb out of the walls. \"The tithe is due!\"\n- 40%: **Arrears:** charges three times along telegraphed lanes.\n- 15%: **Foreclosure:** enrages.\n\n**Prioress Amarante.** Slim caster, scale 1.3, teleports between four platforms in the Mold Pit.\n- **The Hush:** a slow ring spreads; caught in it, you can use only Rite 1 for 2 s. Roll through it.\n- 66%: Hush Sisters. Molten bronze rises in quadrants, with warning.\n- 33%: she stops mid-fight and speaks. Then all at once. Below 5% the cutscene takes over.\n\n**The Bellwether.** Scale 4.5. Biped, `wings`, a shepherd's crook, and **a bronze bell for a head** (a prop\ndrawn at the head anchor with `emit_asset`; tiny `head_radius`). Bell Pit: a 30 m round arena with four\nropes at its rim and the cracked Old Compline hanging above. Aveline is at the ropes.\n- **Toll:** every 12 s, after a three-count of rising bell strokes, a ring of force expands from the boss:\n  the screen-distortion ring is the picture, the bell is the warning. Roll through it, or stand by a\n  Still Stone. **The audio is the telegraph; the visual must work alone too.**\n- **Ropes:** a rope lights every 20 s. Hold interact 1 s beside it: Old Compline rings, the boss is stunned\n  5 s and takes 50% more damage. Bots must use them. Works solo; great with four.\n- 100–66%: crook sweeps, the Flock spawns at the rim.\n- 66–33%: hovers; beams turn like a wheel; floor tiles crumble.\n- 33–0%: the bell-head cracks; tolls come faster. The Prioress's voice helps one last time: \"Now, little\n  corpse. It is listening to itself.\" At 0: slow-motion, the great bell falls, the Compline cutscene.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Screens\n\n### Rules for every screen (10-foot, controller-first)\n- At 1920×1080: safe margin 96 px sides and 54 px top and bottom. Body text at least 28 px, no text under\n  24 px, headings 40+, menu items 72 px tall at 36 px, at most 7 items in a column. Scale by screen\n  height, with a UI scale setting (100, 125, 150%).\n- **One thing focused at a time**, always clearly lit. A card shows the focused thing's detail. No\n  hover-only information, no tiny icon grids, no tables of stats, no scroll bars except for long text.\n- Build a shared **focus layer** in `pav_ui`: screens declare focusable items with ids and rects; the layer","numLines":400,"startLine":215,"totalLines":997}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MdL3rPhVP5ZA12nzuDZA6v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
