{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjCGwTuNducUqDbWT4Lt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012QB6anN6xoDSZzgPLRZJkq","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","offset":614},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15297,"cache_read_input_tokens":476047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15297},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"a19bec47-3ca0-4989-9b8c-c1a8f07a14a4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:50.256Z","request_id":"req_011CgjCGw8a5APAM1sFUnxBT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012QB6anN6xoDSZzgPLRZJkq":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","offset":614}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012QB6anN6xoDSZzgPLRZJkq","type":"tool_result","content":"614\t- Build a shared **focus layer** in `pav_ui`: screens declare focusable items with ids and rects; the layer\n615\t  turns D-pad, stick, arrows, Enter, Esc, mouse hover and click into the same actions by geometry. Hover\n616\t  moves focus. Click confirms. Everything is reachable by pad **and** by mouse. Draw with `egui::Area` and\n617\t  the painter, not desktop `Window`s. Remove the stick-driven cursor.\n618\t- **Prompts follow the last input used:** PlayStation shapes for pad (Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1,\n619\t  R1, L2, R2, D-pad, Options), or Xbox A B X Y and LB RB LT RT Menu if chosen in Settings; keycaps and\n620\t  mouse-button icons for keyboard and mouse. Draw glyphs as vectors in one `Prompt` widget. Hide the\n621\t  pointer when the pad was used last.\n622\t- Every screen says at the bottom what its buttons do, right-aligned, with glyphs.\n623\t- Fonts: fonts are allowed. Fetch a heading face and a body face with open licences (Cinzel and Alegreya\n624\t  suit), `include_bytes!` them, and credit them. If the fetch fails, use egui's.\n625\t- Frames, bars and icons are code-drawn in bell-bronze and bone; rite icons are vector marks.\n626\t\n627\t### Flow\n628\t**Title** → press any button → **Main menu** → New Hero or Continue → play. 10 s idle on Title, Main menu\n629\tor class select starts attract.\n630\t\n631\t- **Title:** a 3D night churchyard, the cracked bell against the sky, falling ash. The title, big. \"Press\n632\t  any button\" (or \"Press any key\" on keyboard). Music starts on first input: browsers keep sound off until\n633\t  then. Try `resume()` on pad presses too; if the context stays suspended after a pad press, show a quiet\n634\t  line \"Press a key or click to wake the bells\".\n635\t- **Touch-only device** (`(any-pointer: fine)` false, no pad seen, no key pressed): **no touch controls.**\n636\t  The Title shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and one big Settings button that a tap opens. Attract\n637\t  still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Taps reach the focus layer as clicks, so Settings work by tap. A pad\n638\t  connecting or a key press restores the normal Title.\n639\t- **Main menu:** Continue (hero, class, level, current quest) · New Hero · Co-op on This Screen · Settings ·\n640\t  About & Credits.\n641\t- **Class select:** four pedestals in a crypt, each hero performing a showreel (`hall.rs`). Left and right\n642\t  move. Card: name, one line of fantasy, resource, three rites. Then name (typed if on keyboard; on pad a\n643\t  list of period names, Square rerolls). Then difficulty (one line each). Then Q1.\n644\t- **HUD:**\n645\t  - Bottom left: life gauge, a bronze bell-shaped gauge filling with red. Bottom right: resource gauge, in\n646\t    the class's colour. These are ours, not the source's orbs.\n647\t  - Bottom centre: six 96 px rite slots, each tagged with its button glyph, cooldown as a sweep; Gin and\n648\t    dodge charges beside them; XP bar under.\n649\t  - Top centre: target nameplate and bar, affixes under it. Boss bar wider, with its title.\n650\t  - Top right: small map, one line of objective under it.\n651\t  - Toasts: loot worth seeing, Harvests, quest steps; big centre banner on entering a zone.\n652\t  - World: damage numbers (setting), small bars on damaged elites only, ground telegraphs, seat-coloured\n653\t    ring and name for co-op heroes.\n654\t  - Co-op: small plates at left for other heroes.\n655\t- **Hero screen** (L1/R1 tabs; the world keeps running in a session, pauses otherwise):\n656\t  - **Gear:** the hero in the middle, ten slots ringed round them; focus moves round the ring. Three big\n657\t    numbers at top: **Damage, Toughness, Recovery**. Focused slot: a large item card (name, rarity, up to 6\n658\t    lines). Confirm opens a strip of what you carry for that slot, five cards at a time; each card shows ▲▼\n659\t    on the three big numbers against what's worn. Confirm equips, Square salvages, Triangle marks as junk.\n660\t    \"Details\" is a second page, not a denser first page.\n661\t  - **Rites:** six slots laid out like the pad's buttons. Confirm a slot: pick a rite from a list; then one\n662\t    of its three tones, one card each. Vows on a second row.\n663\t  - **Journal:** current objective big; story so far; Tomes, one page each.\n664\t  - **Map:** the floor drawn large. On a Lychstone: travel list.\n665\t- **Service screens** (§7): a full screen with the person's portrait, their verbs as tabs, big cards. Never a\n666\t  grid. Portraits are code-drawn 2-tone vector silhouettes with a moving mouth, as for villain slide-ins.\n667\t- **Pause:** Resume · Hero · Settings · Controls · Dev Mode · About & Credits · Save & Quit. In a session:\n668\t  Settings and Controls only, and it never pauses.\n669\t- **Settings:** Audio: **Music 10% by default**, Effects 80%, Voices 80%. Controls: Controller glyphs\n670\t  (PlayStation or Xbox), Rumble, Aim assist. Display: UI scale, Camera (Near, Middle, Far), Damage numbers,\n671\t  Screen shake, Full screen, Graphics quality. Subtitles size.\n672\t- **Controls:** the table of §5 for the device in use.\n673\t- **About & Credits:** paged, large type: the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and\n674\t  Prompt Feedback TASK.md lists, all from `engine/game/about.toml`, then credits: engine, clip and prop libraries\n675\t  with their licences (`engine/assets/props/CREDITS.md`, each `engine/anim/*.json`'s `credit`, `engine/store/licences.tsv`),\n676\t  fonts. Usage says \"added on import\".\n677\t\n678\t### Attract mode (`engine/game/attract.toml`, `arpg/attract.rs`)\n679\tA throwaway `Game` with saving off, the bot at the wheel, cheats on (no damage, no cost, no cooldowns,\n680\tteleports). Wall-clock 10 s idle (not ticks: the sim crawls in software rendering) on the Title, Main menu or\n681\tclass select starts it; **any** key, click, real mouse move, pad button, stick past 0.4 or tap goes back to\n682\tthe Title. A list of vignettes with an engine screen transition between them, looping for ever, with a\n683\t\"Demo\" tag, a caption and \"Press any button\":\n684\t1. Potter's Field: a hero claws out of the grave. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish, Hob shouts, the coffin opens.\n685\t2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n686\t3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam; the Gear screen as the bot equips it.\n687\t4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n688\t5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n689\t6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n690\t7. The Great Belfry, then the Bellwether: wind, the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\n691\t\n692\tIts job is to show as much of the game as it can. It never touches saves.\n693\t\n694\t### Dev Mode (pause menu, not in a session)\n695\tTabs, all by pad and mouse.\n696\t- **Balance:** live sliders with a value readout and **Reset to defaults**, all as `impl Tunable` under\n697\t  `balance.*`, extending `arpg::Difficulty`, so they're also in `pav params`:\n698\t  player damage, player life, enemy life, enemy damage, enemy speed, pack density, elite rate, XP, gold, drop\n699\t  rate, relic rate, mote chance, Gin cooldown, resource gain, cooldown scale, hit-stop, shake, co-op life per\n700\t  player, co-op damage per player.\n701\t- **Cheats:** God, one-hit kills, no cost, no cooldowns, no-clip, reveal map, freeze AI, time scale\n702\t  (0.25–4×), kill all.\n703\t- **Hero:** set level, add XP, add 100k gold, full materials, grant every rite and tone.\n704\t- **Spawn:** family, rarity, affix, count; any boss; the Magpie.\n705\t- **Items:** any relic, any regalia set, an item by slot and rarity.\n706\t- **Go:** any zone and floor, any Undertoll Depth, town, any quest step, the ending, the credits.\n707\t- **Show:** frame and tick stats, nav grid overlay, hit circles, aggro lines, entity list; play any music state or\n708\t  voice line; engine tuning panel and its system keys.\n709\t\n710\t---\n711\t\n712\t## 10. Art and animation\n713\t\n714\t**Base: the engine's native look**, procedural primitives and materials lit by real lights with shadows, plus\n715\tits own filters. Add one look, `[[look]] name = \"Compline\"`, in `engine/crates/pav_view/src/looks.toml`, applied from\n716\t`place_look`. The planner compared the engine's 21 looks on a crypt floor: **ink outlines over the native\n717\tmaterials read far best** at distance (\"Cartoon\" tile 8), and full paint filters smear the architecture. So:\n718\t`view.outlines` on at about 2 px with a heavy `outline_darken`, `cel_bands` 3–4, `view.saturation` about 0.8,\n719\t`filter.contrast` about 1.1, `filter.vignette` modest, per-zone `haze` and `halos`, like an inked woodcut with\n720\tcandlelight in it. Compare with `look bench`.\n721\t\n722\t**Camera:** tilt 56°, distance 20, fov 38 (Shardfall's are 62, 18, 40). Camera setting: Near 17, Middle 20, Far 24.\n723\t`view.cutaway.*` on, so walls never hide a hero. Judge at 1920×1080: a hero should stand about 7% of screen height.\n724\tBoss and cutscene moments may move it: add a `GameFrame` camera override with smooth blends.\n725\t\n726\t**Light is the art direction:** dark world, pools of warm candle and cold moon, with every magic effect a real\n727\tlight. Colour by zone (§8). Monster elements and telegraphs stay readable through grade and vignette.\n728\t\n729\t**New props (format-2, primitives; publish to `LIB/core`):** headstones (3 variants), mausoleum, iron fence,\n730\tlych-gate, gibbet, gallows, tomb slab, sarcophagus, coffin (open, closed), pew, lectern, censer stand, pointed arch,\n731\tlancet window (glowing), rose window, flying buttress, weeping saint statue, gargoyle perch, chandelier (breakable),\n732\tsmall bell, **great cracked bell** (6 m), bell frame, dead trees (2), reeds, bog lantern, crucible, mold, drop-forge,\n733\tgear wheel, scaffold, rope with handle, Still Stone, wayside shrine, broken pump; weapons and gear `censer_flail`,\n734\t`bell_staff`, `hand_bell`, `crossbow`, `pitch_flask`, `beak_mask`, `wide_hat`, `gravedigger_hat`, `mouth_bar`. Each\n735\tgets a look at the game camera (`asset_preview views=true elevation=game`). Generic props may come from the library\n736\t(`assets shelf=prop`, `assets find=`): barrels, crates, candles, chains, cages, anvils, rubble.\n737\t\n738\t**Effects** (view code + particles + lights): bell rings (`distortion` plus an expanding mesh), toll shockwaves, ember\n739\twake, ash fall, chain arcs, poison clouds, thrall rises (dirt burst), relic beams, level-up ring of bells, soul wisps\n740\toff corpses, ember and rain ambience per zone.\n741\t\n742\t**Animation: the engine's own system.** Procedural biped, moves in `engine/anim/moves.toml`, clips from `engine/anim/*.json` on\n743\t`idle_clip`, `walk_clip`, `run_clip`, `death_clip`, `attack_clips`, `attack_moves`, `dodge_clip` in looks. Check with\n744\t`animsheet` and `filmstrip`. New work:\n745\t- **Moves:** flail swings on long arcs (with verlet chain following the censer), crossbow aim and shot, flask throw, spade\n746\t  chops and dig, bell-staff strike, hand-bell ring.\n747\t- **Clips to find or author** with `assets find= kind=clip` and `anim_edit`: rising from a grave (`MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`),\n748\t  gravedigging loop for Mabry, Hob hammering, Aveline pulling a rope one-armed, Tacet kneeling, the Prioress' levitating idle, the\n749\t  Bellwether's slow walk and crook sweep, goose waddle. Each hero's level-up and triumph gesture.\n750\t- **Monster gaits** per family from the clip tables, so nothing shares a walk with its neighbour.\n751\t\n752\t---\n753\t\n754\t## 11. Audio\n755\t\n756\t**All sound is written in code, with no audio files.** Extend `engine/crates/pav_audio`. Three buses over the `Mixer`:\n757\tMusic (**default 0.10**), Effects (0.80), Voices (0.80), persisted in settings. In a session, the `end` message stops all\n758\tsound.\n759\t\n760\t**Bell synthesis** is the game's signature. One function: additive inharmonic partials at ratios about 0.5, 1, 1.19,\n761\t1.5, 2, 2.5, 2.67, 3, 4, each with its own decay, plus a noise strike. Add a detuned beat for the cracked Old Compline.\n762\tUsed in music, tolls, UI and loot.\n763\t\n764\t**Music** (a small sequencer, data in `engine/game/music.toml`, generated at runtime, crossfading at bar lines). Original\n765\tthroughout: write your own motif on a three-note cell of D, A, B♭, and don't imitate the source's themes. No solo guitar in\n766\ttown.\n767\t| State | When | Sound |\n768\t|---|---|---|\n769\t| Title | Title, attract | Slow toll motif, deep drone, far-off wordless choir of formant voices |\n770\t| Dread | Exploring | Drone, sparse bell strokes, chant fragments; D Phrygian, about 60 BPM |\n771\t| Battle | Enemies near (intensity from count within 12 m) | Adds low drums (sine thump + noise), saw ostinato; layers in and out, not a hard switch |\n772\t| Town | Vespergate | Hurdy-gurdy drone (saw + LP) and handbells; tired, kind |\n773\t| Boss | Gaudry, Prioress | Battle plus a theme per boss: a pompous march, a silence-heavy one with rests |\n774\t| Bellwether | Finale | The tolling tritone, full choir; ducks for each toll |\n775\t| Ending | Compline | The title motif resolved to major, once |\n776\t\n777\t**Effects** (make `sounds_for` data-driven: a `SimEvent::Sfx { id, pos }` and patches in `engine/game/sfx.toml`): about 60, each\n778\twith pitch variation: hits by element and weapon, crits, flail whoosh and chain rattle, crossbow, bell cast, spade, thrall rise,\n779\tfootsteps by surface, breaking wood, stone and pot, keg blast, body falls, gore, gold, mote, Gin (a gulp and a cough), loot by rarity\n780\t(Relic's chime is unmistakable), level up, shrine, portal, hand-bell, UI move, confirm, back, quest, boss entrance, and monster calls per\n781\tfamily: moaning, chitter, honk. The Tacet make no sound at all.\n782\t\n783\t**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish** (`engine/game/voices.toml`), played as a line's subtitle appears. Each letter of the line maps to a\n784\tshort syllable: a formant pair per vowel, a noise tick per consonant; the same word always sounds the same. Add a formant\n785\tfilter to `Patch`. Per speaker: base pitch, rate, formant shift, breath, growl. `?` rises, `!` is louder, capitals (Hob, the Bellwether) are\n786\tloud and slow. The Prioress: a whisper, unvoiced noise only. The Bellwether: pitched bell partials as syllables. Monster\n787\tbarks use the same engine.\n788\t\n789\tCheck it headless: `pav audio_capture` writes a `.wav` (§13).\n790\t\n791\t---\n792\t\n793\t## 12. Multiplayer\n794\t\n795\t### Modes\n796\t| Where | Mode | How |\n797\t|---|---|---|\n798\t| **In an AI Hub session** | `shared-world`, 1–4 seats, 8 minutes | The round below, online through the hub |\n799\t| **On its own** | Solo, plus **Co-op on This Screen**, up to 4 pads and/or keyboard on one TV | Same multi-hero sim, no network. \"Online\" is the hub's job: its lobby, invite and network are what the protocol gives you, and outside a session the game opens no sockets |\n800\t\n801\tRead `tools/hub/README.md` (the protocol) whole before M7. It wins over this section.\n802\t\n803\t### The page\n804\t`engine/web/index.html`, in order: `<meta charset>`, then **`tools/hub/session.js` pasted unmodified as the first script**, exactly one\n805\tcopy (`engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` reads it from disk and inlines it; the hub checks its SHA-256), then:\n806\t```html\n807\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n808\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n809\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n810\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n811\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fill the Peal, slay the Warden, top the Glory count\">\n812\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Rites: face buttons, or mouse + 1-4 · Dodge: L1/Space\">\n813\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n814\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n815\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">   <!-- players on one screen: \"1\" if Co-op on This Screen is cut -->\n816\t```\n817\tKeep `<title>` as \"Title — tagline\", a real `description`, `theme-color`, and a `data:` SVG bell icon: the hub's catalogue reads them.\n818\t\n819\tThen a **JS shim, in `<head>`, before the game loads.** This pattern passed the harness with real wasm copies. Protocol timing lives here, because a\n820\tframe may take over a second under software rendering:\n821\t```js\n822\tconst hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null, waiting: AIHub.active });\n823\tif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n824\t  hub.waiting = false;\n825\t  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n826\t  hub.info = info;\n827\t  if (!navigator.gpu) return AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU.');\n828\t  for (const e of ['start', 'leave', 'end']) AIHub.on(e, (d) => hub.inbox.push({ k: e, d }));\n829\t  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => hub.inbox.push({ k: 'm', d, from }));\n830\t  AIHub.on('time-up', () => {            // answer now, not at the next frame\n831\t    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\n832\t    hub.inbox.push({ k: 'time-up' });\n833\t  });\n834\t});\n835\t```\n836\tRust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): at boot, holds on a plain \"Connecting\" while `__hub.waiting` is true (the hub answers within 10 s; `info` stays null if there is none, and\n837\tthe game then starts normally). Then it reads `__hub.info`, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\n838\tbuilt, with no key press), `AIHub.finish`, `AIHub.fail`, and writes `__hub.standings` and `scores` every second. Use `js_namespace` extern functions,\n839\t**no `inline_js`.** `AIHub.time()` is the shared clock; input is locked while it's below 0, with a large 3-2-1 over the world.\n840\t\n841\t**Session rules:** straight into the round, no title, attract or menus; no Dev Mode, no save prompts; pause never pauses; no Quit; no dialogs; no text entry;\n842\tnames and colours only from the hub (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700` by seat); no chat, emotes or pings. Use the hub's own card through the metas: it\n843\tworks as it is, and a custom card is optional polish (§15). On `end`: no input, no sends, no sound.\n844\t\n845\t### The round: the Vigil\n846\tOne Undertoll run, the same for every copy from `info.seed`: three floors, each with a Peal and a Warden; the third Warden's death wins. Seats get heroes: 0 Penitent,\n847\t1 Carillon, 2 Plaguewright, 3 Gravewarden (cycle if you shipped fewer). All level 12, with a fixed session kit from data and a sensible bar. Loot, levels and motes during\n848\tthe round work as usual; personal loot; a one-button \"Equip\" prompt on anything better. No town.\n849\t\n850\t**Glory:** kills ×1, elites ×25, Wardens ×100, revives ×50, deaths ×−25. On win or `time-up` the host calls `finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`: standings by\n851\tGlory, `won` true if the last Warden fell; stats: Kills, Deaths, Revives (6 names max, 16 chars); awards such as \"Most Harvests\" (3 max). A leaver is removed and monsters rescale.\n852\tHost leaving voids the round: the hub tells every copy; show \"The host has gone\" and stop. **`AIHub.server` true:** the host copy has no hero, camera, input or drawing, and still runs\n853\tthe world and calls `finish`.\n854\t\n855\t### Netcode: thin guests that own their feet\n856\tHost authority, with each player owning their own position, as the protocol's example games do. It is far smaller than `engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` and fits the hub's limits.\n857\t\n858\t- **Same level everywhere:** every copy builds floors from the same seed with the same build. Host sends a hash of the floor at each floor start; mismatch on a guest calls `AIHub.fail`. A test\n859\t  guards this.\n860\t- **Host:** runs one full `Game` with one `HeroSlot` per player: all AI, monster movement, all damage, loot, quests, Peal. Remote heroes are placed where they say they are; their rites\n861\t  run from their cast messages. Slots use their own `Hero` sheet.\n862\t- **Guest:** runs its own `Sim` with `Game` in **mirror mode**: no AI, no damage, no rewards. Its own hero moves locally with no delay and collides locally. Pressing a rite plays its\n863\t  animation, effects and sound at once (`fire_cast` with a `cosmetic` flag) and tells the host. Monsters and other heroes are remote-driven puppets: a target position fed from the stream with\n864\t  velocity set, so the procedural walk animates (`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` C0's `Character.remote`). Hits, deaths, floaters and loot come as events. The guest's menu actions are `GameCmd`s\n865\t  sent to the host, which sends back that hero's state.\n866\t- **Interpolation:** mirrors render 200 ms behind `AIHub.time()`, extrapolate up to 150 ms, then hold; corrections blend over 100 ms.\n867\t- **Multi-hero rules** (`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` §3 lists the places): monsters target the nearest living hero, sticky; a flow field per targeted hero; aggro, crumbling floors and mechanics check\n868\t  any hero. **Hit-stop can't slow a shared world:** in a session `time_scale` stays 1 and only the local hero and what it struck hold their pose. No pause, speed or rewind.\n869\t\n870\t**Messages (JSON, short keys, integers in decimetres):**\n871\t| Key | Direction | Rate, delivery | Holds |\n872\t|---|---|---|---|\n873\t| `w` | host → all | 10/s, `reliable: false`, **≤ 1,100 characters** | Clock; every hero `[seat,x,z,yaw,hp%,res%,flags,act]`; up to about 40 actors `[id,x,z,yaw,hp%,flags]`, those nearest any hero first, round-robin past the cap |\n874\t| `e` | host → all | ≤ 5/s, reliable, ≤ 14 KB | Batched: spawn (id, family or genome seed, level, rarity, affixes, pos), die (id, killer, impulse), cast (id, rite, aim), hits (merged), floaters, loot (owner, item, pos), picks, breaks, Peal, quest, banners, boss lines, hero sheets on change |\n875\t| `f` | host → all | reliable, on floor start | Floor index, seed, hash |\n876\t| `me` | guest → host | 10/s, `reliable: false` | Clock, x, z, yaw, velocity, flags (rolling, channelling) |\n877\t| `c` `i` `g` | guest → host | reliable, on use | Cast (slot, aim), interact (id), `GameCmd` |\n878\t\n879\t**Own a Rust `SendBudget`: never more than 18 messages a second per copy, never a message over 16 KB.** The client drops anything past its limit and logs `[AIHub]`, and hub-check fails on any such\n880\twarning. Oversized batches split; unreliable messages above about 1,200 bytes are lost whole on one lost packet, which is why `w` is capped.\n881\t\n882\t**Put all of this logic in `arpg/net.rs`, pure:** a per-tick `NetInbox` and `NetOutbox`, no IO, so tests run 2–4 full `Sim`s in one process with a `SimNet` of seeded latency, jitter and loss (§13), far\n883\tfaster than real time. `engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs` only carries bytes. Add one `coop` tool to `pav`: `coop players=4 latency=150 jitter=50 loss=0.05 bots=true seconds=120`.\n884\t\n885\t### Co-op on This Screen\n886\tThe same `HeroSlot`s with `NetRole::Solo`. Main menu screen: each pad presses Cross to take a seat and a hero from the roster (one per seat), or a new one at the party's level. One camera on the\n887\tcentroid, pulling out up to 30%; a hero over 20 m away is pulled in. Plates at left. A full-screen menu belongs to the pad that opened it, and the world pauses for it. Keyboard and mouse can hold one seat.\n888\t\n889\t---\n890\t\n891\t## 13. Testing\n892\t\n893\t**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|playthrough|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and a single line of counts. Rerun only the group covering what you changed. Screenshots only for what a script can't\n894\tjudge. Follow TASK.md: no subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit.\n895\t\n896\t| Group | How | What it proves |\n897\t|---|---|---|\n898\t| `core` | `cargo test -p pav_core --test <your suites>`, and `pav` tools | Every class's resource rule; every tone changes its rite; vows; relics, regalia, gems, salvage, Reliquary; every elite affix fires; every boss phase (force life with `set`); toll hits unless rolling; ropes stun; each quest step; Tally; difficulty table; saves round-trip; a bad save doesn't crash; a replay reproduces its hash. **Banned-word grep** over `engine/game/`, UI text and the page |\n899\t| `playthrough` (its own group: slow) | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**, with a new `pav` tool: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. About 10× real time, so about 9 minutes a run in a dev build: build `pav` with `--release`, run classes as separate processes, and rerun only after world, quest or balance changes. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\n900\t| `net` | `cargo test --test coop` over `SimNet`, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss | 2, 3, 4 bots finish a Vigil. Own hero never waits. Mirror error median ≤ 0.3 m, p99 ≤ 1 m. Budget never above 18/s or 16 KB. Leave, host leave. Floor hash equal across copies. Standings valid |\n901\t| `ui` | `pav ui` extended: `press=down|confirm|back`, reports screen, focus and items | From each screen, every item is reachable by pad path and can be hovered and clicked. Prompts change for pad (PlayStation), pad (Xbox) and keys. Text ≥ 24 px at 1080p. Touch gate shows. Attract timer logic with a test clock |\n902\t| `audio` | `pav audio_capture` and a small WAV reader; settings defaults | Music default is exactly 0.10; each music state, effect and speaker is non-silent; speakers differ in spectrum; the page contains no `<audio>` or audio file |\n903\t| `web` (slow) | One Playwright script, one browser, plain `python3`, flags from §2, `file://`. Add `window.__game.state()` returning JSON (screen, focus, device, attract, music volume, role) | Boots with no console errors. Title shows. 10 s idle starts attract; a key leaves it. Pad stub (`navigator.getGamepads`, `add_init_script`) walks Menu → Settings → Xbox glyphs. Phone profile with `page.touchscreen`: gate, Settings tap, attract. Never waits on gameplay: the sim crawls here |\n904\t| `hub` (slow) | Copy the page and `tools/hub/*` to one folder, serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page is your game, open `harness.html?game=<page>&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` plus each of `players=2`, `3`, `4`, `players=3&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`; read `window.__hubCheck` once `body[data-complete]` is true | All pass. No `[AIHub]` console warnings, no page errors. One pristine client (SHA-256 of 1.4.0, banner to last line, starts `529eac78`; if upstream moved on, use its current release). Then **on its own**: page opens, Enter and Space pressed, `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched, a screenshot well above a blank page's size |\n905\t\n906\tIf `harness.html` fetches a page with spaces or odd characters in its name, serve a copy with a plain name. Harness frames share one main thread, so keep JS light. Keep one or two browsers at a time and stop only what you\n907\tstarted, by PID. `hub-check.mjs` in the hub repo needs the whole repo: use your own small driver as above.\n908\t\n909\t**Look at these yourself at 1920×1080, once per milestone:** a `see` capture of each zone, each boss, each screen with `ui ... image=true`.\n910\t\n911\t**Sound in a browser:** the wasm build opens a real `AudioContext`; `web` only asserts that it exists and resumes. Judge content from `audio_capture`.\n912\t\n913\t---\n914\t\n915\t## 14. Build order\n916\t\n917\tDo these in order; each ends with its checks passing and a page you could ship. Earlier milestones touch what later ones build on, which is why many-heroes comes so early.\n918\t\n919\t| # | Build | Done when |\n920\t|---|---|---|\n921\t| **M0** | §3 setup. Title step. `tools/check.sh` skeleton. Reproduce §2 | `pav` runs, a page boots in your Playwright, harness files in place |\n922\t| **M1** | Page assembly with client, metas, shim. Screen state machine: Title, Main menu, Settings, About. Focus layer, `Prompt` glyphs, device tracking, settings persistence, touch gate. Pavilion and tech-demo UI gone; system keys gated. `window.__game.state()`. `localStorage` prefix | `ui` and `web` pass for those screens; harness passes with Shardfall's old content standing in |\n923\t| **M2** | `HeroSlot` refactor: several heroes in one `Game`, each with its own input, sheet and rewards. Monsters target any hero. Bot per slot. Scaling | Four bots clear a floor natively. Solo plays as before |\n924\t| **M3** | Combat and classes: controls of §5 (click-to-move, pad targeting), resource rules, Rites, Tones, Vows, `summon`, `trap`, allied AI, motes, Gin, dodge, Harvest, new looks and weapons. Remove the tree. HUD. Rites screen, Gear screen | Bot per class clears a test floor. Each class looks and plays apart in a `filmstrip` |\n925\t| **M4** | World: Compline look, camera, gothic kit, themes, open grammar, zones, monsters, elites, three bosses, Vespergate, quests, dialogue, voices stubbed to silence only until M6, cutscenes, Tomes, events, Journal, Map | **Playthrough runs to the credits** for one class |\n926\t| **M5** | Loot and town: rarity ladder and beams, relics, regalia, gems, materials, all service screens, coffin, Reliquary, Sexton's roll, Tally, followers, Undertoll, the Magpie | `core` passes. Playthrough per class |\n927\t| **M6** | Audio: buses, bell synth, music states, data-driven effects, voices on every line | `audio` passes. Listened to by numbers, not ear: levels sane against each other |\n928\t| **M7** | Multiplayer: `arpg/net.rs`, mirror mode, `SimNet`, `coop` tool, the Vigil, `hub.rs`, server role, Co-op on This Screen | `net` and `hub` pass |\n929\t| **M8** | Attract mode, Dev Mode, class select stage, Secret level, Feats if kept | `web` and `ui` pass |\n930\t| **M9** | Polish: effects, lights, breakables on every floor, barks, balance by bot on all tiers, 1080p look pass of every zone and screen, write-through of every player-facing line | `all` passes. Play time and deaths in range |\n931\t| **M10** | §16 | Done |\n932\t\n933\t**Balance targets:** first clear on Penance about 90 minutes of game time; bot deaths: under 3 a zone and under 8 per boss for each class; level 20 near the final boss; first relic by the first boss; a relic or regalia piece about every 15 minutes after that.\n934\t\n935\t---\n936\t\n937\t## 15. Cut list\n938\t\n939\tTASK.md allows no stubs. If you must cut, **cut a whole feature from this list, top first, and remove every trace of it from menus and text.** Never leave a dead button. Record the cut in your exit interview.\n940\t\n941\t1. Custom hub card (never required).\n942\t2. Rumble (via `vibrationActuator`, if tried at all).\n943\t3. Feats (12 small achievements with toasts).\n944\t4. The Bishop's Geese and the hand-bell hunt.\n945\t5. Followers (keep allied AI for thralls).\n946\t6. The Drowned Chapel.\n947\t7. Regalia sets beyond the class you have most tested. Then all of them.\n948\t8. Gravewarden, the fourth class. Then Plaguewright. Never below two classes.\n949\t9. Co-op on This Screen (the game on its own is then solo; say so plainly in your Prompt Feedback).\n950\t\n951\tNever cut: Title, attract, Dev Mode with sliders, Settings with glyph choice and music at 10%, touch gate, About & Credits, the full chapter with its three bosses, Relics, the Undertoll, `shared-world` in the hub, the voices, the tests.\n952\t\n953\tIf shared-world networking truly fails after real effort, the last-ditch fallback is `ghost` mode (each copy runs its own Vigil and shows the others' heroes), with the metas and result calls changed, and the reason written in your exit interview. Try hard not to need it.\n954\t\n955\t---\n956\t\n957\t## 16. Finishing\n958\t\n959\t1. Build the page to the root path TASK.md names:\n960\t   `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene <title scene> --title \"<Title> — <tagline>\" --description \"...\" --theme-color \"#14110f\" --out <path>`.\n961\t2. `tools/check.sh all`. Open the shipped file, not a dev copy.\n962\t3. **Fill in `engine/game/about.toml`** with TASK.md's Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, rebuild, and confirm the About screen shows them. Plan: this file's name. Testing: what TASK.md allowed. Environment and Model: as TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n963\t4. Write TASK.md's exit interview file and check it parses. Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls in one line; tags such as `3d, co-op, fantasy, boss fights, loot, top-down`.\n964\t5. Give the same feedback in your final chat reply, as TASK.md asks.\n965\t6. **Clean up:** delete `engine/target`, `engine/out`, `engine/.git`, any `node_modules` and stray probe pages. They are large or would confuse the record. Keep the source, `tools/` and a few useful `shots/`. Stop any process you started.\n966\t\n967\t---\n968\t\n969\t## 17. Coverage of TASK.md\n970\t\n971\t| TASK.md asks | Where |\n972\t|---|---|\n973\t| Genre, perspective | §1 |\n974\t| Title: riff, 50 ideas, real RNG | Builder's first step (top of this plan, M0) |\n975\t| Research | Done here (§2); more is your choice |\n976\t| Package: single HTML, deps may be external | §3, §16; this plan inlines everything |\n977\t| Tech: build on the engine, new game, change anything | §3 |\n978\t| Art direction on the engine's native style, new assets | §10 |\n979\t| Animation on the native system, new animations | §10 |\n980\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §11, §9 Settings, §13 |\n981\t| Online via the hub library | §12 |\n982\t| Dev folder, no reading others' folders, ports and PIDs | §3, §13 |\n983\t| Performance out of scope | §3 |\n984\t| Testing: headless, scripted whole game, one command, few screenshots, no review subagents | §13 |\n985\t| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, sound, two players, TV | §2, §13 |\n986\t| Feature-complete demo of all mechanics; capture the source's world, themes, tone | §1, §4–§8 |\n987\t| Infrastructure for later build-out with designer tools | Data in `engine/game/*.toml`, `pav` tools, §3 |\n988\t| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | §9 |\n989\t| Attract at 10 s, loop, any input exits, may cheat | §9 |\n990\t| Multiplayer in the hub and on its own | §12 |\n991\t| Narrative tone | §4 |\n992\t| 10-foot UI, DualSense first, native keys and mouse, prompts by last device, Xbox option, no dense screens | §5, §9 |\n993\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings, attract runs | §9 |\n994\t| No TODOs or stubs | §15 |\n995\t| Source Information, feedback in chat and About screen | §9, §16 |\n996\t| Exit interview file | §16 |\n997\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"d2570e48-f826-4d65-a838-98358306f321","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:02:50.428Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Build a shared **focus layer** in `pav_ui`: screens declare focusable items with ids and rects; the layer\n  turns D-pad, stick, arrows, Enter, Esc, mouse hover and click into the same actions by geometry. Hover\n  moves focus. Click confirms. Everything is reachable by pad **and** by mouse. Draw with `egui::Area` and\n  the painter, not desktop `Window`s. Remove the stick-driven cursor.\n- **Prompts follow the last input used:** PlayStation shapes for pad (Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1,\n  R1, L2, R2, D-pad, Options), or Xbox A B X Y and LB RB LT RT Menu if chosen in Settings; keycaps and\n  mouse-button icons for keyboard and mouse. Draw glyphs as vectors in one `Prompt` widget. Hide the\n  pointer when the pad was used last.\n- Every screen says at the bottom what its buttons do, right-aligned, with glyphs.\n- Fonts: fonts are allowed. Fetch a heading face and a body face with open licences (Cinzel and Alegreya\n  suit), `include_bytes!` them, and credit them. If the fetch fails, use egui's.\n- Frames, bars and icons are code-drawn in bell-bronze and bone; rite icons are vector marks.\n\n### Flow\n**Title** → press any button → **Main menu** → New Hero or Continue → play. 10 s idle on Title, Main menu\nor class select starts attract.\n\n- **Title:** a 3D night churchyard, the cracked bell against the sky, falling ash. The title, big. \"Press\n  any button\" (or \"Press any key\" on keyboard). Music starts on first input: browsers keep sound off until\n  then. Try `resume()` on pad presses too; if the context stays suspended after a pad press, show a quiet\n  line \"Press a key or click to wake the bells\".\n- **Touch-only device** (`(any-pointer: fine)` false, no pad seen, no key pressed): **no touch controls.**\n  The Title shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and one big Settings button that a tap opens. Attract\n  still runs after 10 s, and a tap leaves it. Taps reach the focus layer as clicks, so Settings work by tap. A pad\n  connecting or a key press restores the normal Title.\n- **Main menu:** Continue (hero, class, level, current quest) · New Hero · Co-op on This Screen · Settings ·\n  About & Credits.\n- **Class select:** four pedestals in a crypt, each hero performing a showreel (`hall.rs`). Left and right\n  move. Card: name, one line of fantasy, resource, three rites. Then name (typed if on keyboard; on pad a\n  list of period names, Square rerolls). Then difficulty (one line each). Then Q1.\n- **HUD:**\n  - Bottom left: life gauge, a bronze bell-shaped gauge filling with red. Bottom right: resource gauge, in\n    the class's colour. These are ours, not the source's orbs.\n  - Bottom centre: six 96 px rite slots, each tagged with its button glyph, cooldown as a sweep; Gin and\n    dodge charges beside them; XP bar under.\n  - Top centre: target nameplate and bar, affixes under it. Boss bar wider, with its title.\n  - Top right: small map, one line of objective under it.\n  - Toasts: loot worth seeing, Harvests, quest steps; big centre banner on entering a zone.\n  - World: damage numbers (setting), small bars on damaged elites only, ground telegraphs, seat-coloured\n    ring and name for co-op heroes.\n  - Co-op: small plates at left for other heroes.\n- **Hero screen** (L1/R1 tabs; the world keeps running in a session, pauses otherwise):\n  - **Gear:** the hero in the middle, ten slots ringed round them; focus moves round the ring. Three big\n    numbers at top: **Damage, Toughness, Recovery**. Focused slot: a large item card (name, rarity, up to 6\n    lines). Confirm opens a strip of what you carry for that slot, five cards at a time; each card shows ▲▼\n    on the three big numbers against what's worn. Confirm equips, Square salvages, Triangle marks as junk.\n    \"Details\" is a second page, not a denser first page.\n  - **Rites:** six slots laid out like the pad's buttons. Confirm a slot: pick a rite from a list; then one\n    of its three tones, one card each. Vows on a second row.\n  - **Journal:** current objective big; story so far; Tomes, one page each.\n  - **Map:** the floor drawn large. On a Lychstone: travel list.\n- **Service screens** (§7): a full screen with the person's portrait, their verbs as tabs, big cards. Never a\n  grid. Portraits are code-drawn 2-tone vector silhouettes with a moving mouth, as for villain slide-ins.\n- **Pause:** Resume · Hero · Settings · Controls · Dev Mode · About & Credits · Save & Quit. In a session:\n  Settings and Controls only, and it never pauses.\n- **Settings:** Audio: **Music 10% by default**, Effects 80%, Voices 80%. Controls: Controller glyphs\n  (PlayStation or Xbox), Rumble, Aim assist. Display: UI scale, Camera (Near, Middle, Far), Damage numbers,\n  Screen shake, Full screen, Graphics quality. Subtitles size.\n- **Controls:** the table of §5 for the device in use.\n- **About & Credits:** paged, large type: the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and\n  Prompt Feedback TASK.md lists, all from `engine/game/about.toml`, then credits: engine, clip and prop libraries\n  with their licences (`engine/assets/props/CREDITS.md`, each `engine/anim/*.json`'s `credit`, `engine/store/licences.tsv`),\n  fonts. Usage says \"added on import\".\n\n### Attract mode (`engine/game/attract.toml`, `arpg/attract.rs`)\nA throwaway `Game` with saving off, the bot at the wheel, cheats on (no damage, no cost, no cooldowns,\nteleports). Wall-clock 10 s idle (not ticks: the sim crawls in software rendering) on the Title, Main menu or\nclass select starts it; **any** key, click, real mouse move, pad button, stick past 0.4 or tap goes back to\nthe Title. A list of vignettes with an engine screen transition between them, looping for ever, with a\n\"Demo\" tag, a caption and \"Press any button\":\n1. Potter's Field: a hero claws out of the grave. Vespergate: Mabry talks in gibberish, Hob shouts, the coffin opens.\n2. Penitent on the Lych Road: crowd, kegs, chandelier, Harvest banner, loot shower.\n3. Carillon in the Undercroft against a Damned pack: Changes, the Great Knell, a relic beam; the Gear screen as the bot equips it.\n4. Plaguewright in the Fens: snares, the Magpie chase, its shower.\n5. Gravewarden in the Foundry: thralls, Mass Grave, molten floor.\n6. Four bots in the Undertoll: co-op plates, the Peal filling, the Warden.\n7. The Great Belfry, then the Bellwether: wind, the toll ring, a rope, the bell.\n\nIts job is to show as much of the game as it can. It never touches saves.\n\n### Dev Mode (pause menu, not in a session)\nTabs, all by pad and mouse.\n- **Balance:** live sliders with a value readout and **Reset to defaults**, all as `impl Tunable` under\n  `balance.*`, extending `arpg::Difficulty`, so they're also in `pav params`:\n  player damage, player life, enemy life, enemy damage, enemy speed, pack density, elite rate, XP, gold, drop\n  rate, relic rate, mote chance, Gin cooldown, resource gain, cooldown scale, hit-stop, shake, co-op life per\n  player, co-op damage per player.\n- **Cheats:** God, one-hit kills, no cost, no cooldowns, no-clip, reveal map, freeze AI, time scale\n  (0.25–4×), kill all.\n- **Hero:** set level, add XP, add 100k gold, full materials, grant every rite and tone.\n- **Spawn:** family, rarity, affix, count; any boss; the Magpie.\n- **Items:** any relic, any regalia set, an item by slot and rarity.\n- **Go:** any zone and floor, any Undertoll Depth, town, any quest step, the ending, the credits.\n- **Show:** frame and tick stats, nav grid overlay, hit circles, aggro lines, entity list; play any music state or\n  voice line; engine tuning panel and its system keys.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Art and animation\n\n**Base: the engine's native look**, procedural primitives and materials lit by real lights with shadows, plus\nits own filters. Add one look, `[[look]] name = \"Compline\"`, in `engine/crates/pav_view/src/looks.toml`, applied from\n`place_look`. The planner compared the engine's 21 looks on a crypt floor: **ink outlines over the native\nmaterials read far best** at distance (\"Cartoon\" tile 8), and full paint filters smear the architecture. So:\n`view.outlines` on at about 2 px with a heavy `outline_darken`, `cel_bands` 3–4, `view.saturation` about 0.8,\n`filter.contrast` about 1.1, `filter.vignette` modest, per-zone `haze` and `halos`, like an inked woodcut with\ncandlelight in it. Compare with `look bench`.\n\n**Camera:** tilt 56°, distance 20, fov 38 (Shardfall's are 62, 18, 40). Camera setting: Near 17, Middle 20, Far 24.\n`view.cutaway.*` on, so walls never hide a hero. Judge at 1920×1080: a hero should stand about 7% of screen height.\nBoss and cutscene moments may move it: add a `GameFrame` camera override with smooth blends.\n\n**Light is the art direction:** dark world, pools of warm candle and cold moon, with every magic effect a real\nlight. Colour by zone (§8). Monster elements and telegraphs stay readable through grade and vignette.\n\n**New props (format-2, primitives; publish to `LIB/core`):** headstones (3 variants), mausoleum, iron fence,\nlych-gate, gibbet, gallows, tomb slab, sarcophagus, coffin (open, closed), pew, lectern, censer stand, pointed arch,\nlancet window (glowing), rose window, flying buttress, weeping saint statue, gargoyle perch, chandelier (breakable),\nsmall bell, **great cracked bell** (6 m), bell frame, dead trees (2), reeds, bog lantern, crucible, mold, drop-forge,\ngear wheel, scaffold, rope with handle, Still Stone, wayside shrine, broken pump; weapons and gear `censer_flail`,\n`bell_staff`, `hand_bell`, `crossbow`, `pitch_flask`, `beak_mask`, `wide_hat`, `gravedigger_hat`, `mouth_bar`. Each\ngets a look at the game camera (`asset_preview views=true elevation=game`). Generic props may come from the library\n(`assets shelf=prop`, `assets find=`): barrels, crates, candles, chains, cages, anvils, rubble.\n\n**Effects** (view code + particles + lights): bell rings (`distortion` plus an expanding mesh), toll shockwaves, ember\nwake, ash fall, chain arcs, poison clouds, thrall rises (dirt burst), relic beams, level-up ring of bells, soul wisps\noff corpses, ember and rain ambience per zone.\n\n**Animation: the engine's own system.** Procedural biped, moves in `engine/anim/moves.toml`, clips from `engine/anim/*.json` on\n`idle_clip`, `walk_clip`, `run_clip`, `death_clip`, `attack_clips`, `attack_moves`, `dodge_clip` in looks. Check with\n`animsheet` and `filmstrip`. New work:\n- **Moves:** flail swings on long arcs (with verlet chain following the censer), crossbow aim and shot, flask throw, spade\n  chops and dig, bell-staff strike, hand-bell ring.\n- **Clips to find or author** with `assets find= kind=clip` and `anim_edit`: rising from a grave (`MESH2MOTION/Zombie_Rise`),\n  gravedigging loop for Mabry, Hob hammering, Aveline pulling a rope one-armed, Tacet kneeling, the Prioress' levitating idle, the\n  Bellwether's slow walk and crook sweep, goose waddle. Each hero's level-up and triumph gesture.\n- **Monster gaits** per family from the clip tables, so nothing shares a walk with its neighbour.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Audio\n\n**All sound is written in code, with no audio files.** Extend `engine/crates/pav_audio`. Three buses over the `Mixer`:\nMusic (**default 0.10**), Effects (0.80), Voices (0.80), persisted in settings. In a session, the `end` message stops all\nsound.\n\n**Bell synthesis** is the game's signature. One function: additive inharmonic partials at ratios about 0.5, 1, 1.19,\n1.5, 2, 2.5, 2.67, 3, 4, each with its own decay, plus a noise strike. Add a detuned beat for the cracked Old Compline.\nUsed in music, tolls, UI and loot.\n\n**Music** (a small sequencer, data in `engine/game/music.toml`, generated at runtime, crossfading at bar lines). Original\nthroughout: write your own motif on a three-note cell of D, A, B♭, and don't imitate the source's themes. No solo guitar in\ntown.\n| State | When | Sound |\n|---|---|---|\n| Title | Title, attract | Slow toll motif, deep drone, far-off wordless choir of formant voices |\n| Dread | Exploring | Drone, sparse bell strokes, chant fragments; D Phrygian, about 60 BPM |\n| Battle | Enemies near (intensity from count within 12 m) | Adds low drums (sine thump + noise), saw ostinato; layers in and out, not a hard switch |\n| Town | Vespergate | Hurdy-gurdy drone (saw + LP) and handbells; tired, kind |\n| Boss | Gaudry, Prioress | Battle plus a theme per boss: a pompous march, a silence-heavy one with rests |\n| Bellwether | Finale | The tolling tritone, full choir; ducks for each toll |\n| Ending | Compline | The title motif resolved to major, once |\n\n**Effects** (make `sounds_for` data-driven: a `SimEvent::Sfx { id, pos }` and patches in `engine/game/sfx.toml`): about 60, each\nwith pitch variation: hits by element and weapon, crits, flail whoosh and chain rattle, crossbow, bell cast, spade, thrall rise,\nfootsteps by surface, breaking wood, stone and pot, keg blast, body falls, gore, gold, mote, Gin (a gulp and a cough), loot by rarity\n(Relic's chime is unmistakable), level up, shrine, portal, hand-bell, UI move, confirm, back, quest, boss entrance, and monster calls per\nfamily: moaning, chitter, honk. The Tacet make no sound at all.\n\n**Voices: Animalese-style gibberish** (`engine/game/voices.toml`), played as a line's subtitle appears. Each letter of the line maps to a\nshort syllable: a formant pair per vowel, a noise tick per consonant; the same word always sounds the same. Add a formant\nfilter to `Patch`. Per speaker: base pitch, rate, formant shift, breath, growl. `?` rises, `!` is louder, capitals (Hob, the Bellwether) are\nloud and slow. The Prioress: a whisper, unvoiced noise only. The Bellwether: pitched bell partials as syllables. Monster\nbarks use the same engine.\n\nCheck it headless: `pav audio_capture` writes a `.wav` (§13).\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n### Modes\n| Where | Mode | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| **In an AI Hub session** | `shared-world`, 1–4 seats, 8 minutes | The round below, online through the hub |\n| **On its own** | Solo, plus **Co-op on This Screen**, up to 4 pads and/or keyboard on one TV | Same multi-hero sim, no network. \"Online\" is the hub's job: its lobby, invite and network are what the protocol gives you, and outside a session the game opens no sockets |\n\nRead `tools/hub/README.md` (the protocol) whole before M7. It wins over this section.\n\n### The page\n`engine/web/index.html`, in order: `<meta charset>`, then **`tools/hub/session.js` pasted unmodified as the first script**, exactly one\ncopy (`engine/scripts/pack_single_html.py` reads it from disk and inlines it; the hub checks its SHA-256), then:\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"8\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Fill the Peal, slay the Warden, top the Glory count\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD · Rites: face buttons, or mouse + 1-4 · Dodge: L1/Space\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">   <!-- players on one screen: \"1\" if Co-op on This Screen is cut -->\n```\nKeep `<title>` as \"Title — tagline\", a real `description`, `theme-color`, and a `data:` SVG bell icon: the hub's catalogue reads them.\n\nThen a **JS shim, in `<head>`, before the game loads.** This pattern passed the harness with real wasm copies. Protocol timing lives here, because a\nframe may take over a second under software rendering:\n```js\nconst hub = (window.__hub = { inbox: [], standings: null, scores: null, info: null, waiting: AIHub.active });\nif (AIHub.active) AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4] }).then((info) => {\n  hub.waiting = false;\n  if (!info) return;                     // no hub after all: play on as usual\n  hub.info = info;\n  if (!navigator.gpu) return AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU.');\n  for (const e of ['start', 'leave', 'end']) AIHub.on(e, (d) => hub.inbox.push({ k: e, d }));\n  AIHub.on('message', (d, from) => hub.inbox.push({ k: 'm', d, from }));\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => {            // answer now, not at the next frame\n    if (info.isHost) AIHub.finish({ standings: hub.standings ?? [AIHub.players.map((p) => p.id)], scores: hub.scores ?? {} });\n    hub.inbox.push({ k: 'time-up' });\n  });\n});\n```\nRust (`pav_app`, a new `hub.rs`, wasm only): at boot, holds on a plain \"Connecting\" while `__hub.waiting` is true (the hub answers within 10 s; `info` stays null if there is none, and\nthe game then starts normally). Then it reads `__hub.info`, drains `inbox` each frame, calls `AIHub.send`, `AIHub.ready` (once the world is\nbuilt, with no key press), `AIHub.finish`, `AIHub.fail`, and writes `__hub.standings` and `scores` every second. Use `js_namespace` extern functions,\n**no `inline_js`.** `AIHub.time()` is the shared clock; input is locked while it's below 0, with a large 3-2-1 over the world.\n\n**Session rules:** straight into the round, no title, attract or menus; no Dev Mode, no save prompts; pause never pauses; no Quit; no dialogs; no text entry;\nnames and colours only from the hub (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700` by seat); no chat, emotes or pings. Use the hub's own card through the metas: it\nworks as it is, and a custom card is optional polish (§15). On `end`: no input, no sends, no sound.\n\n### The round: the Vigil\nOne Undertoll run, the same for every copy from `info.seed`: three floors, each with a Peal and a Warden; the third Warden's death wins. Seats get heroes: 0 Penitent,\n1 Carillon, 2 Plaguewright, 3 Gravewarden (cycle if you shipped fewer). All level 12, with a fixed session kit from data and a sensible bar. Loot, levels and motes during\nthe round work as usual; personal loot; a one-button \"Equip\" prompt on anything better. No town.\n\n**Glory:** kills ×1, elites ×25, Wardens ×100, revives ×50, deaths ×−25. On win or `time-up` the host calls `finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`: standings by\nGlory, `won` true if the last Warden fell; stats: Kills, Deaths, Revives (6 names max, 16 chars); awards such as \"Most Harvests\" (3 max). A leaver is removed and monsters rescale.\nHost leaving voids the round: the hub tells every copy; show \"The host has gone\" and stop. **`AIHub.server` true:** the host copy has no hero, camera, input or drawing, and still runs\nthe world and calls `finish`.\n\n### Netcode: thin guests that own their feet\nHost authority, with each player owning their own position, as the protocol's example games do. It is far smaller than `engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` and fits the hub's limits.\n\n- **Same level everywhere:** every copy builds floors from the same seed with the same build. Host sends a hash of the floor at each floor start; mismatch on a guest calls `AIHub.fail`. A test\n  guards this.\n- **Host:** runs one full `Game` with one `HeroSlot` per player: all AI, monster movement, all damage, loot, quests, Peal. Remote heroes are placed where they say they are; their rites\n  run from their cast messages. Slots use their own `Hero` sheet.\n- **Guest:** runs its own `Sim` with `Game` in **mirror mode**: no AI, no damage, no rewards. Its own hero moves locally with no delay and collides locally. Pressing a rite plays its\n  animation, effects and sound at once (`fire_cast` with a `cosmetic` flag) and tells the host. Monsters and other heroes are remote-driven puppets: a target position fed from the stream with\n  velocity set, so the procedural walk animates (`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` C0's `Character.remote`). Hits, deaths, floaters and loot come as events. The guest's menu actions are `GameCmd`s\n  sent to the host, which sends back that hero's state.\n- **Interpolation:** mirrors render 200 ms behind `AIHub.time()`, extrapolate up to 150 ms, then hold; corrections blend over 100 ms.\n- **Multi-hero rules** (`engine/docs/COOP_PLAN.md` §3 lists the places): monsters target the nearest living hero, sticky; a flow field per targeted hero; aggro, crumbling floors and mechanics check\n  any hero. **Hit-stop can't slow a shared world:** in a session `time_scale` stays 1 and only the local hero and what it struck hold their pose. No pause, speed or rewind.\n\n**Messages (JSON, short keys, integers in decimetres):**\n| Key | Direction | Rate, delivery | Holds |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `w` | host → all | 10/s, `reliable: false`, **≤ 1,100 characters** | Clock; every hero `[seat,x,z,yaw,hp%,res%,flags,act]`; up to about 40 actors `[id,x,z,yaw,hp%,flags]`, those nearest any hero first, round-robin past the cap |\n| `e` | host → all | ≤ 5/s, reliable, ≤ 14 KB | Batched: spawn (id, family or genome seed, level, rarity, affixes, pos), die (id, killer, impulse), cast (id, rite, aim), hits (merged), floaters, loot (owner, item, pos), picks, breaks, Peal, quest, banners, boss lines, hero sheets on change |\n| `f` | host → all | reliable, on floor start | Floor index, seed, hash |\n| `me` | guest → host | 10/s, `reliable: false` | Clock, x, z, yaw, velocity, flags (rolling, channelling) |\n| `c` `i` `g` | guest → host | reliable, on use | Cast (slot, aim), interact (id), `GameCmd` |\n\n**Own a Rust `SendBudget`: never more than 18 messages a second per copy, never a message over 16 KB.** The client drops anything past its limit and logs `[AIHub]`, and hub-check fails on any such\nwarning. Oversized batches split; unreliable messages above about 1,200 bytes are lost whole on one lost packet, which is why `w` is capped.\n\n**Put all of this logic in `arpg/net.rs`, pure:** a per-tick `NetInbox` and `NetOutbox`, no IO, so tests run 2–4 full `Sim`s in one process with a `SimNet` of seeded latency, jitter and loss (§13), far\nfaster than real time. `engine/crates/pav_app/src/hub.rs` only carries bytes. Add one `coop` tool to `pav`: `coop players=4 latency=150 jitter=50 loss=0.05 bots=true seconds=120`.\n\n### Co-op on This Screen\nThe same `HeroSlot`s with `NetRole::Solo`. Main menu screen: each pad presses Cross to take a seat and a hero from the roster (one per seat), or a new one at the party's level. One camera on the\ncentroid, pulling out up to 30%; a hero over 20 m away is pulled in. Plates at left. A full-screen menu belongs to the pad that opened it, and the world pauses for it. Keyboard and mouse can hold one seat.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Testing\n\n**One command: `tools/check.sh [core|playthrough|net|ui|audio|web|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and a single line of counts. Rerun only the group covering what you changed. Screenshots only for what a script can't\njudge. Follow TASK.md: no subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit.\n\n| Group | How | What it proves |\n|---|---|---|\n| `core` | `cargo test -p pav_core --test <your suites>`, and `pav` tools | Every class's resource rule; every tone changes its rite; vows; relics, regalia, gems, salvage, Reliquary; every elite affix fires; every boss phase (force life with `set`); toll hits unless rolling; ropes stun; each quest step; Tally; difficulty table; saves round-trip; a bad save doesn't crash; a replay reproduces its hash. **Banned-word grep** over `engine/game/`, UI text and the page |\n| `playthrough` (its own group: slow) | A bot-driven **whole-game run per class, 2 seeds**, with a new `pav` tool: `pav playthrough class=... seed=...`: rises, walks the quests, buys and equips, beats all three bosses, reaches credits, then clears an Undertoll Depth. Reports minutes, deaths, level per zone. Fails if it stalls | The game can be finished. About 10× real time, so about 9 minutes a run in a dev build: build `pav` with `--release`, run classes as separate processes, and rerun only after world, quest or balance changes. Also your balance tool, with `campaign`, `loot_roll`, `autoplay` |\n| `net` | `cargo test --test coop` over `SimNet`, 150 ± 50 ms, 5% loss | 2, 3, 4 bots finish a Vigil. Own hero never waits. Mirror error median ≤ 0.3 m, p99 ≤ 1 m. Budget never above 18/s or 16 KB. Leave, host leave. Floor hash equal across copies. Standings valid |\n| `ui` | `pav ui` extended: `press=down|confirm|back`, reports screen, focus and items | From each screen, every item is reachable by pad path and can be hovered and clicked. Prompts change for pad (PlayStation), pad (Xbox) and keys. Text ≥ 24 px at 1080p. Touch gate shows. Attract timer logic with a test clock |\n| `audio` | `pav audio_capture` and a small WAV reader; settings defaults | Music default is exactly 0.10; each music state, effect and speaker is non-silent; speakers differ in spectrum; the page contains no `<audio>` or audio file |\n| `web` (slow) | One Playwright script, one browser, plain `python3`, flags from §2, `file://`. Add `window.__game.state()` returning JSON (screen, focus, device, attract, music volume, role) | Boots with no console errors. Title shows. 10 s idle starts attract; a key leaves it. Pad stub (`navigator.getGamepads`, `add_init_script`) walks Menu → Settings → Xbox glyphs. Phone profile with `page.touchscreen`: gate, Settings tap, attract. Never waits on gameplay: the sim crawls here |\n| `hub` (slow) | Copy the page and `tools/hub/*` to one folder, serve with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page is your game, open `harness.html?game=<page>&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&play=8000` plus each of `players=2`, `3`, `4`, `players=3&scenario=host-leave`, `players=2&scenario=server`; read `window.__hubCheck` once `body[data-complete]` is true | All pass. No `[AIHub]` console warnings, no page errors. One pristine client (SHA-256 of 1.4.0, banner to last line, starts `529eac78`; if upstream moved on, use its current release). Then **on its own**: page opens, Enter and Space pressed, `AIHub.active` false, `Math.random` untouched, a screenshot well above a blank page's size |\n\nIf `harness.html` fetches a page with spaces or odd characters in its name, serve a copy with a plain name. Harness frames share one main thread, so keep JS light. Keep one or two browsers at a time and stop only what you\nstarted, by PID. `hub-check.mjs` in the hub repo needs the whole repo: use your own small driver as above.\n\n**Look at these yourself at 1920×1080, once per milestone:** a `see` capture of each zone, each boss, each screen with `ui ... image=true`.\n\n**Sound in a browser:** the wasm build opens a real `AudioContext`; `web` only asserts that it exists and resumes. Judge content from `audio_capture`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build order\n\nDo these in order; each ends with its checks passing and a page you could ship. Earlier milestones touch what later ones build on, which is why many-heroes comes so early.\n\n| # | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | §3 setup. Title step. `tools/check.sh` skeleton. Reproduce §2 | `pav` runs, a page boots in your Playwright, harness files in place |\n| **M1** | Page assembly with client, metas, shim. Screen state machine: Title, Main menu, Settings, About. Focus layer, `Prompt` glyphs, device tracking, settings persistence, touch gate. Pavilion and tech-demo UI gone; system keys gated. `window.__game.state()`. `localStorage` prefix | `ui` and `web` pass for those screens; harness passes with Shardfall's old content standing in |\n| **M2** | `HeroSlot` refactor: several heroes in one `Game`, each with its own input, sheet and rewards. Monsters target any hero. Bot per slot. Scaling | Four bots clear a floor natively. Solo plays as before |\n| **M3** | Combat and classes: controls of §5 (click-to-move, pad targeting), resource rules, Rites, Tones, Vows, `summon`, `trap`, allied AI, motes, Gin, dodge, Harvest, new looks and weapons. Remove the tree. HUD. Rites screen, Gear screen | Bot per class clears a test floor. Each class looks and plays apart in a `filmstrip` |\n| **M4** | World: Compline look, camera, gothic kit, themes, open grammar, zones, monsters, elites, three bosses, Vespergate, quests, dialogue, voices stubbed to silence only until M6, cutscenes, Tomes, events, Journal, Map | **Playthrough runs to the credits** for one class |\n| **M5** | Loot and town: rarity ladder and beams, relics, regalia, gems, materials, all service screens, coffin, Reliquary, Sexton's roll, Tally, followers, Undertoll, the Magpie | `core` passes. Playthrough per class |\n| **M6** | Audio: buses, bell synth, music states, data-driven effects, voices on every line | `audio` passes. Listened to by numbers, not ear: levels sane against each other |\n| **M7** | Multiplayer: `arpg/net.rs`, mirror mode, `SimNet`, `coop` tool, the Vigil, `hub.rs`, server role, Co-op on This Screen | `net` and `hub` pass |\n| **M8** | Attract mode, Dev Mode, class select stage, Secret level, Feats if kept | `web` and `ui` pass |\n| **M9** | Polish: effects, lights, breakables on every floor, barks, balance by bot on all tiers, 1080p look pass of every zone and screen, write-through of every player-facing line | `all` passes. Play time and deaths in range |\n| **M10** | §16 | Done |\n\n**Balance targets:** first clear on Penance about 90 minutes of game time; bot deaths: under 3 a zone and under 8 per boss for each class; level 20 near the final boss; first relic by the first boss; a relic or regalia piece about every 15 minutes after that.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Cut list\n\nTASK.md allows no stubs. If you must cut, **cut a whole feature from this list, top first, and remove every trace of it from menus and text.** Never leave a dead button. Record the cut in your exit interview.\n\n1. Custom hub card (never required).\n2. Rumble (via `vibrationActuator`, if tried at all).\n3. Feats (12 small achievements with toasts).\n4. The Bishop's Geese and the hand-bell hunt.\n5. Followers (keep allied AI for thralls).\n6. The Drowned Chapel.\n7. Regalia sets beyond the class you have most tested. Then all of them.\n8. Gravewarden, the fourth class. Then Plaguewright. Never below two classes.\n9. Co-op on This Screen (the game on its own is then solo; say so plainly in your Prompt Feedback).\n\nNever cut: Title, attract, Dev Mode with sliders, Settings with glyph choice and music at 10%, touch gate, About & Credits, the full chapter with its three bosses, Relics, the Undertoll, `shared-world` in the hub, the voices, the tests.\n\nIf shared-world networking truly fails after real effort, the last-ditch fallback is `ghost` mode (each copy runs its own Vigil and shows the others' heroes), with the metas and result calls changed, and the reason written in your exit interview. Try hard not to need it.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Finishing\n\n1. Build the page to the root path TASK.md names:\n   `engine/scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene <title scene> --title \"<Title> — <tagline>\" --description \"...\" --theme-color \"#14110f\" --out <path>`.\n2. `tools/check.sh all`. Open the shipped file, not a dev copy.\n3. **Fill in `engine/game/about.toml`** with TASK.md's Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, rebuild, and confirm the About screen shows them. Plan: this file's name. Testing: what TASK.md allowed. Environment and Model: as TASK.md gives them. Usage: \"added on import\".\n4. Write TASK.md's exit interview file and check it parses. Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls in one line; tags such as `3d, co-op, fantasy, boss fights, loot, top-down`.\n5. Give the same feedback in your final chat reply, as TASK.md asks.\n6. **Clean up:** delete `engine/target`, `engine/out`, `engine/.git`, any `node_modules` and stray probe pages. They are large or would confuse the record. Keep the source, `tools/` and a few useful `shots/`. Stop any process you started.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Coverage of TASK.md\n\n| TASK.md asks | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Genre, perspective | §1 |\n| Title: riff, 50 ideas, real RNG | Builder's first step (top of this plan, M0) |\n| Research | Done here (§2); more is your choice |\n| Package: single HTML, deps may be external | §3, §16; this plan inlines everything |\n| Tech: build on the engine, new game, change anything | §3 |\n| Art direction on the engine's native style, new assets | §10 |\n| Animation on the native system, new animations | §10 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §11, §9 Settings, §13 |\n| Online via the hub library | §12 |\n| Dev folder, no reading others' folders, ports and PIDs | §3, §13 |\n| Performance out of scope | §3 |\n| Testing: headless, scripted whole game, one command, few screenshots, no review subagents | §13 |\n| This computer: stand-ins for pad, touch, sound, two players, TV | §2, §13 |\n| Feature-complete demo of all mechanics; capture the source's world, themes, tone | §1, §4–§8 |\n| Infrastructure for later build-out with designer tools | Data in `engine/game/*.toml`, `pav` tools, §3 |\n| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | §9 |\n| Attract at 10 s, loop, any input exits, may cheat | §9 |\n| Multiplayer in the hub and on its own | §12 |\n| Narrative tone | §4 |\n| 10-foot UI, DualSense first, native keys and mouse, prompts by last device, Xbox option, no dense screens | §5, §9 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings, attract runs | §9 |\n| No TODOs or stubs | §15 |\n| Source Information, feedback in chat and About screen | §9, §16 |\n| Exit interview file | §16 |\n","numLines":384,"startLine":614,"totalLines":997}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012QB6anN6xoDSZzgPLRZJkq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
