{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0174gtqssUHMrCmkHKZr2gKu","type":"tool_result","content":"5:- **Authority:** TASK.md first, then this plan, then the engine's docs.\n8:- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder TASK.md names. `engine/` is the engine's clone inside it.\n11:- **The title** is yours: do TASK.md's title step first. Keep it in one place\n19:· §13 testing · §14 build order · §15 cut list · §16 finishing · §17 coverage of TASK.md.\n88:| The same page with TASK.md's flag list (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, no `--use-vulkan=swiftshader`) | **GPU device lost, blank canvas.** Use the flags above; they are also what `\n118:So you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\n132:in `engine/game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\n145:`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\n204:- Don't spend time shrinking the page or optimizing: TASK.md puts that out of scope.\n681:  Prompt Feedback TASK.md lists, all from `engine/game/about.toml`, then credits: engine, clip and prop libraries\n902:judge. Follow TASK.md: no subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit.\n947:TASK.md allows no stubs. If you must cut, **cut a whole feature from this list, top first, and remove every trace of it from menus and text.** Never leave a dead button. Record the cut i\n967:1. Build the page to the root path TASK.md names:\n970:3. **Fill in `engine/game/about.toml`** with TASK.md's Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, rebuild, and confirm the About screen shows them. Plan: \n971:4. Write TASK.md's exit interview file and check it parses. Suggestions: type Game; genre RPG; source Diablo 3; series Diablo; players 1–4; controls in one line; tags such as `3d, co-op,\n972:5. Give the same feedback in your final chat reply, as TASK.md asks.\n977:## 17. Coverage of TASK.md\n979:| TASK.md asks | Where |\n\n18\nYou are the game director. TASK.md is the CEO's brief. Write PLAN.md: the plan other AI agents will build the game from, without you. Leave the game's title to them: each builder picks its own, as TASK.md says. Leave out TASK.md's file and folder names too, since each builder's TASK.md has its own; write paths relative to the dev folder.\n\nThen review the prompt you were given (TASK.md and these instructions): save planner-exit-interview.json in this folder, a JSON list of {\"question\", \"answer\"}, one for each of these questions:\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"3493b8a2-e054-471e-a4eb-78117bd14aac","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:51.055Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5:- **Authority:** TASK.md first, then this plan, then the engine's docs.\n8:- **Paths** are relative to the dev folder TASK.md names. `engine/` is the engine's clone inside it.\n11:- **The title** is yours: do TASK.md's title step first. Keep it in one place\n19:· §13 testing · §14 build order · §15 cut list · §16 finishing · §17 coverage of TASK.md.\n88:| The same page with TASK.md's flag list (`--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, no `--use-vulkan=swiftshader`) | **GPU device lost, blank canvas.** Use the flags above; they are also what `\n118:So you edit `arpg/`, `engine/game/`, `pav_ui`, `engine/crates/pav_view/src/arpg.rs` and `pav_app` directly. TASK.md lets\n132:in `engine/game/*.toml`, checked by `pav` tools. That is the \"infrastructure for the rest of the game\" TASK.md asks for.\n145:`README.md` once (you need all of it). Keep everything inside the dev folder; TASK.md's rules on sharing this\n204:- Don't spend time shrinking the page or optimizing: TASK.md puts that 