{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD7kYwkRq36D5QnX4UU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gaps are closed: `PLAN.md` now states every requirement itself instead of pointing to `TASK.md`, and I checked it against `TASK.md` line by line. You were right that my earlier \"covers everything\" claim was overstated. The one thing not copied in full is the machine inventory (tool versions, disk, RAM); the plan restates only what builders need, and the rest stays in their own brief.\n\n**What changed in the plan:**\n- **New \"What must ship\" section (§0):** it states the source, the goal and the done bar, plus the rules on research, effort, performance, the engine and online play. It also lists the rules for sharing the machine and the stand-ins for hardware this computer lacks.\n- **Title step:** it's now spelled out: silently brainstorm 50 riffs on the source's name, then pick one by running a real random number generator. Each builder still chooses its own title.\n- **Reports:** the plan now lists every Source Information field, all the feedback questions, and the exit interview's exact JSON shape and rules.\n- **Same screens:** keyboard and mouse must use the same screens as the controller, which the plan hadn't said outright.\n- **Coverage table (§17):** rewritten to match the additions, in the same order as the brief.\n\n**Where I read the feedback differently:**\n- **Literal names:** the plan still doesn't contain the required folder and file names, because `STAGE.md` says to leave them out. It gives the pattern as `<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>/` and `<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>.html`, and tells builders to copy the exact names from their own brief.\n- **Saying \"TASK.md\":** I don't read `STAGE.md` as banning the word itself, since it only rules out the names inside that file. The plan now says \"the brief\" anyway, because that costs nothing.\n\nI also recorded this conflict between `STAGE.md` and the completion check in the exit interview, and suggested a fix. The page metas and shim I tested in the harness didn't change. No game code exists yet, so the Rust netcode is still untested design, and nothing is committed.\n\nFiles are in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211941__xf7be7f/work`:\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `planner-exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7720,"cache_read_input_tokens":543790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7720},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"dd2e20bf-1611-4c8a-aa30-f0d45a8121e2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:13:56.726Z","request_id":"req_011CgjD7kF5mFucXhmkJWEci"}
