{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjD8wU48krLTi6xaeEMD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JKjUfccJoEdNkdig4vgq81","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib, json, re\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ntask = pathlib.Path('TASK.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, (s.count(old), old[:90])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n# 1. The name's form, field by field.\nrep(\"\"\"**Where things go.** Your brief spells out the exact names. They carry your run's own stamp, so copy them from there with\nyour title filled in. This plan gives only the pattern, with `<stamp>` standing in for that part:\n\"\"\", \"\"\"**Where things go.** The dev folder and the game's file share one name, in this form: `<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>`. `<Title>` is\nthe title you just picked, `<Source>` is the source, and `<stamp>` is your run's model, effort, date and time, joined by hyphens.\nYour brief writes this form out with your run's own stamp in it: copy that exactly and fill in your title. This plan can't give one\nliteral name, because the title doesn't exist until you pick it and every builder's stamp differs.\n\"\"\")\n\n# 2. Source Information: the exact forms, not just \"from your brief\".\nrep(\"\"\"| Date | The date and time your brief gives |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Date | Your run's date and time, as `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`, from your brief |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Environment | As your brief gives it |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Environment | `Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux`, unless your brief says otherwise |\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| Model | As your brief gives it |\"\"\", \"\"\"| Model | `Anthropic, <model id>, reasoning effort <level>`, with your run's values from your brief |\"\"\")\n\n# 3. The brief's requirements, verbatim, generated from the file so the wording can't drift.\nNAME = re.search(r\"\\[(GameTitle-SOURCE-[^\\]]+)\\]\", task).group(1)\nbody = task.replace(f\"[{NAME}]\", \"`<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>`\")\nlines = body.split(\"\\n\")\ndef block(start, end):\n    a = next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(start))\n    b = next(i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(end) and i > a)\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines[a:b]).strip()\ntop = block(\"Genre:\", \"## This computer\")\ngoal = block(\"## Goal\", \"## Source Information\")\ngoal = goal.replace(\"## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\", \"### UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\")\\\n           .replace(\"## Done\", \"### Done\").replace(\"## Goal\", \"### Goal\")\ncritical = next(l for l in lines if l.startswith(\"CRITICAL:\"))\nassert NAME not in top + goal + critical\nappendix = f\"\"\"\n\n---\n\n## 18. The brief's requirements, word for word\n\nSo this plan stands alone, here is what the brief asks, copied exactly, with its run-specific name written in §0's form. Left out: the\ncomputer's inventory of versions, which isn't a request (its rules are in §0); and the Source Information, feedback questions and exit\ninterview, which are in §16. Your own brief wins wherever it differs.\n\n### Source: Diablo 3\n\n{top}\n\n{goal}\n\n### Reports\n\n{critical}\n\"\"\"\ns = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + appendix\n\n# Point the map and the coverage table at it.\nrep(\"\"\"§16 finishing and reports · §17 coverage of the brief.\"\"\", \"\"\"§16 finishing and reports · §17 coverage of the brief · §18 the brief's requirements, word for word.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| The brief asks | Where |\n|---|---|\n\"\"\", \"\"\"Every request below is also in the brief's own words in §18.\n\n| The brief asks | Where |\n|---|---|\n\"\"\")\np.write_text(s, encoding='utf-8')\n\n# 4. The planner's review: record the decision, not just the conflict.\nq = pathlib.Path('planner-exit-interview.json')\nd = json.loads(q.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\na = d[1]['answer']\ni = a.index(\"(5) STAGE.md says\")\nd[1]['answer'] = a[:i] + (\"(5) STAGE.md says to leave out TASK.md's file and folder names, yet the goal is that PLAN.md covers everything TASK.md asks for, and TASK.md asks for \"\n  \"those names. My first version left them out and also pointed to TASK.md for other requirements, and the completion check rightly rejected that. The plan now states every \"\n  \"requirement itself and gives the name's form field by field. The check then asked for the literal names. I decided not to add them: STAGE.md says to leave them out and says why, \"\n  \"the name starts with a title that doesn't exist until a builder picks it, and this run's stamp would be wrong for every other builder. The check also first objected to the words \"\n  \"'TASK.md' and then to 'the brief', so I couldn't satisfy it on wording either. Only the prompt's author can settle this conflict.\")\nq.write_text(json.dumps(d, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\", encoding='utf-8')\nprint(len(s.split()), 'words')\nPY\npython3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('planner-exit-interview.json')); print('interview ok', len(d))\"; echo \"run-specific leaks: $(grep -c 'claude-opus\\|20261104\\|211941\\|GameTitle' PLAN.md)\"; echo \"TASK.md mentions: $(grep -c 'TASK\\.md' PLAN.md)\"; grep -n \"exit-interview\\.json\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-200; tail -n 62 PLAN.md | cut -c1-175 | head -40","description":"Add the name's form and verbatim requirements to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1468,"cache_read_input_tokens":551510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1468},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"e47cecb1-f601-4a1e-a481-f86cc147c1e7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05