andled later): FPS targets\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n### Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great gam","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33b9a197-b2fe-42e5-9a43-b32ae2dde858","uuid":"d87d56f7-8eff-4b9d-a8c7-1f04f8847d0a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:57.952Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"15862 words\ninterview ok 4\nrun-specific leaks: 0\nTASK.md mentions: 0\ninterview, which are in §16. Your own brief wins wherever it differs.\n\n### Source: Diablo 3\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file `<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>`.html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the h\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall/blob/main/START_HERE.md, making a new game on its engine. You may change anything in it, the engine included, \n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic \n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects 