{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDHfMRshwhCX2fub3de","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan now covers everything `TASK.md` asks for in full, except one thing I left out on purpose: the literal folder and file names. The completion check asks for those, but I still won't add them, so it may keep rejecting the plan until you decide.\n\n**Why the literal names stay out:**\n- `STAGE.md` says to leave them out because each builder's `TASK.md` has its own.\n- The name starts with the game's title, and `STAGE.md` leaves that to each builder, so no finished name exists at plan time.\n- This run's version carries this run's model and timestamp, which would be wrong for every other builder.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Name form:** §0 now spells it out as `<Title>-<Source>-<stamp>`, where the stamp is the run's model, effort, date and time. It tells builders to copy their own brief's form exactly, and says why the plan can't give a literal name.\n- **Requirements word for word:** the new §18 is copied directly from `TASK.md`, with only the run-specific name swapped for that form. A scan finds no stamp or `GameTitle` text in the plan.\n- **Left out of §18:** the machine's version inventory, which isn't a request. The feedback questions and exit-interview shape are in §16, and the Source Information fields are there in table form. The sharing rules and hardware stand-ins are in §0.\n- **Source Information:** the date, environment and model fields now show their exact format. Each builder still fills in its own run's values.\n- **Exit interview:** it now records this decision, including that the check first objected to \"TASK.md\" and then to \"the brief\".\n\n**Your decision:** do you want this run's literal names in `PLAN.md`?\n- **No (my recommendation):** the plan stays as it is. If the check keeps blocking, `/goal clear` ends it.\n- **Yes:** tell me and I'll add them in one line, but every other